      "id": "usestrix/strix",
      "skew": 0,
      "agentReview": {
        "name": "Strix",
        "description": "Autonomous AI pentesting with Strix: scan code, web apps, APIs and the OWASP Top 10, fix findings and gate pull requests, self-hosted or managed.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to find and fix security vulnerabilities in your own app, API or code with autonomous AI pentesting"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs Strix agents that exploit a target and validate each finding with a PoC, then helps you patch and re-test"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Exploit-proven findings, root-cause fixes, CI gating and SARIF, from one engine run locally or in the cloud"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "The open-source CLI (Docker plus your LLM key) or the managed app.strix.ai cloud"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A target you own or are authorized to test"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Strix's skills share one engine: autonomous AI agents that dynamically exploit a target and report only findings proven with a working proof-of-concept. penetration-testing-with-strix is the hub, covering install and the choice between the self-hosted open-source CLI (Docker plus your own LLM key, air-gap capable) and the managed app.strix.ai cloud. Four skills target a specific surface: web-app-penetration-testing for a running site, api-security-testing for REST/GraphQL/gRPC, owasp-top-10-testing for a category-mapped assessment, and find-security-vulnerabilities-in-code for a white-box code review. application-security-testing routes a whole product's assets to the right one and merges the results into a ranked plan. Once a scan reports, fix-security-vulnerabilities-with-strix patches root causes and re-scans to prove each exploit is closed, and ci-security-scanning-with-strix gates every pull request. All share the same SARIF output, so findings line up across local and cloud runs.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/usestrix/strix/tree/06015506625a78b981ae0b34be40239fc1b389be"
        },
