            }
          ],
          "text": "Claude SEO is a Claude Code plugin whose skills share Python tools and subagents kept outside their folders, and many read the seo skill's references, so it's meant to be installed whole. seo is the entry point: /seo <command> <url> loads the matching skill. seo-audit crawls up to 500 pages, has subagents check technical SEO, content, schema, sitemaps, speed, visuals, AI search, agent readiness, search experience and backlinks in parallel, adds local, maps, clustering, e-commerce or drift checks when they apply, and scores the site out of 100; seo-page reviews one URL. Each other skill takes one job: seo-technical, seo-sitemap, seo-images, seo-hreflang, seo-schema, seo-content for E-E-A-T (Google's experience, expertise, authoritativeness and trust criteria), seo-geo for citations in AI answers, seo-sxo for whether a page is the type that ranks, seo-local, seo-maps, seo-backlinks and seo-ecommerce. seo-google brings Google's own figures. seo-plan, seo-cluster, seo-content-brief, seo-competitor-pages and seo-programmatic plan sites and pages, seo-flow supplies the author's FLOW prompts, and seo-drift snapshots a page to catch regressions. The plugin also installs seo-agentic, and seo-dataforseo and seo-image-gen, optional front ends to DataForSEO's and Gemini's paid APIs, which SkillHub doesn't list.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/tree/6be93f45064ffbadced572b5d5c95f55fd263af0"
