          "text": "It hands the reading to a background agent, so you and the main agent keep working. That agent investigates the question against primary sources, such as official docs, source code, specs and first-party APIs, rather than second-hand write-ups, and follows each claim back to the source that owns it. The findings go into a single Markdown file with a citation for each claim, saved in the folder where your repo keeps similar notes; if there's none, it picks a place and tells you where.",
