          ],
          "text": "For claude.ai artifacts too complex to write as one file. One script creates a React 18 and TypeScript project with Tailwind CSS and over 40 shadcn/ui components already installed. The agent then builds the app by editing those files like any frontend project. When it's done, a second script inlines every script, style and asset into a single bundle.html, which you see as an artifact in the conversation. A design note warns against the usual AI look: everything centered, purple gradients, the same rounded corners everywhere, the Inter font. Testing in a browser is optional and comes after you've seen the result, so you aren't kept waiting.",
