      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Makes candidate research code changes, such as LoRA layers or a new head, on an isolated branch with rollback notes.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've authorized trying a code change on a research model: transplanting a module, adapting a backbone, replacing a head, or adding LoRA or adapter layers"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Makes the change on an isolated branch or worktree, copying from the source repo rather than rewriting, and records why it matters and how to undo it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An explore_outputs/ folder: changeset, scientific changelog, comparability report, top runs and status, all marked as candidates"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Your explicit go-ahead for exploratory changes; the trusted baseline stays untouched"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike ai-research-explore",
              "text": "That one coordinates a whole search for ideas; this one only makes the code change, and hands runs to minimal-run-and-audit or run-train"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The implementation step of RigorPilot's exploration lane, which tries new ideas on top of a reproduced baseline, kept apart from the reproduction itself. It's for changes such as bringing a module over from another repository, adapting a backbone, replacing a model's head, adding LoRA or adapter layers (small trainable add-ons to a pretrained model), or combining low-risk modules. A bundled planner maps the change, and the work happens on an isolated branch or worktree, never on the trusted baseline, the unmodified reproduced version. It prefers copying code from the source repository with minimal adaptation over freeform rewrites, records the baseline and branch it worked from, where any transplanted code came from and how to roll back, and explains why the result is still only a candidate. Broad refactors and implementing an idea from scratch are out of scope, and running the changed model is handed to minimal-run-and-audit or run-train.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/tree/fb3ccdf5aa64b1fa5b1d0463e666a8bc8bc26e01/skills/explore-code"
