            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Run sweeps, change the architecture, or present a startup check as a reproduced result"
            },
            {
              "label": "Usually called by",
              "text": "RigorPilot's main skill, ai-research-reproduction, for its training steps"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The training step of RigorPilot, a set of skills that reproduces deep-learning research code from its README; minimal-run-and-audit covers inference and evaluation instead. You give it the goal, the command, what the environment and data are assumed to be, and the mode: startup verification, a short verification run, a full kickoff, or a resume. It records the exact command and the data and checkpoint assumptions and, when the logs show them, the steps completed, best metric, best checkpoint and why the run stopped, without inventing values when logs are silent. Long runs are watched for a limited window rather than indefinitely. Conclusions stay cautious for short or partial runs, and the scientific changelog and comparability report say what could change the result's meaning. Planning experiments, choosing data subsets and comparing variants are left to the main skill or the exploration skills.",
