          "text": "Performance ad creative in four modes. From scratch, it sets 3 to 5 angles, different reasons to click such as pain, outcome, proof or curiosity, and writes variations of each. From performance data you paste or export, it finds the themes and structures of winners and losers, doubles down on the winners, tests one or two new angles and logs the round. For scaled static batches, such as 50 concepts at a time, it works from an inputs folder of your best ads, reviews and comments and a library of static ad layouts ranked by tier, citing the source of every concept. A strategy mode ranks which ads are worth making, keeps a roadmap and runs a monthly retro. References cover Meta ad formats, iPhone-style chat reveal videos, generated faceless motion videos, creator-style short videos, and image, video and voice generation tools. To pull ad data yourself it points to the repo's ad-platform CLIs, and to Magister, its maintainer's own marketing agent, as a shortcut, with a disclosure.",
