            {
              "label": "Health signals",
              "text": "What to track weekly, such as DAU/MAU above 20%, new members posting within 7 days, and unanswered questions"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Community-led growth built on one idea: people join for the product but stay for the people and a shared identity, such as bootstrapped founders or self-hosting tinkerers. After reading your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes), it asks about your product, platform, community stage, main goal and ideal member, and makes and flags assumptions where details are missing. Playbooks cover launching from zero (recruit 20-50 founding members by hand and seed posts before opening), growing an existing community (find where members drop off, run weekly rituals, invest in the few power users), building an ambassador program, and community-led support. A platform table weighs Discord, Slack, Circle, Reddit, Facebook Groups and Discourse forums. A reference describes four community models and how the builder's role shifts as a community passes 100 and then 1,000 members. It insists on specifics you can act on today rather than \"be consistent\" advice.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/96798cf38736ecdba015a1d2b0521b0c8f8f41dd/skills/community-marketing"
