          ],
          "text": "A guide to making marketing images efficiently. After reading your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes), it asks what the image is, where it goes, its size, your brand assets and which image tools you have API keys for. A decision tree picks the model: Ideogram when the image needs text, Flux or Gemini (Nano Banana) for consistency across many images, Recraft for vector illustrations, cheaper models for volume. Prompts follow subject, setting, style, lighting, composition and technical details. Workflows cover blog heroes at 1200x630 (which doubles as the link preview), resizing social graphics per platform, framing real screenshots in device mockups, and banners for LinkedIn, X, Product Hunt and G2. Images are meant to be compressed, served as WebP with a fallback, lazy loaded and given explicit sizes, with commands for cwebp, ImageMagick and jpegoptim. It also gives the meta tags for link previews and ways to generate them per page. Video goes to the repo's video skill.",
