            }
          ],
          "text": "Social content with storytelling first: platform tactics only amplify a good story. It reads your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes), then asks about goals, audience, brand voice and how much time you have. A quick reference gives each platform's audience, posting frequency and main format, with deeper references on each platform, character limits, and how X ranks its For You feed. Hooks come in curiosity, story, value and contrarian shapes, to be filled with a specific fact or story. Repurposing pulls 5-10 self-contained moments from a blog post, podcast, webinar or newsletter and adapts each to a platform. It also sets a 30-minute daily engagement routine, a weekly review of top and bottom posts, a method for studying what works for top creators in your niche, and short-form video structures in which the visual, spoken and on-screen hooks all land in the first second. A listening reference helps pick which posts to comment on and track brand mentions.",
