            {
              "label": "Rule",
              "text": "Build the pages backlinks will point to, such as alternative and use-case pages, before submitting anywhere"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Directory listings treated as the foundation of distribution, not the whole strategy: they pass links that raise your domain rating, put you in front of people browsing for tools, and get cited by AI assistants. A 9-question readiness check comes first, and a no on any of the first seven, such as a missing pricing page, privacy policy, screenshots or alternative pages, blocks submission. Directories are grouped into 13 tiers, from Product Hunt launch week to AI directories, MCP registries (the official registry first), review sites and niche directories, and it only submits where the product genuinely fits. Each tier gets its own tagline, short and long description, tags and assets. Once a listing is live, it fetches the page and inspects the actual link to your product, recording its rel attributes or marking it unverified or missing. Playbooks cover a three-week Product Hunt build-up and launch day, getting 10 G2 reviews in 30 days, the pages backlinks should point to, getting cited by AI assistants, and community channels. It treats directory pages as untrusted data and reads your product marketing context first if you have it.",
