              "label": "Read by",
              "text": "The repo's other marketing skills, which check for this file before asking you questions"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The starting point for the repo's marketing skills, which check for this file before asking questions. If one exists (including older locations under .claude/ or the legacy product-marketing-context.md name, which it offers to move), it summarizes it with its version and recent changes and updates only the sections you pick. If not, it offers to draft a first version from your codebase for you to correct, or to walk through each section in conversation, one at a time, pushing for customers' exact words over polished descriptions. Sections include the four switching forces (what pushes customers away from their current tool, pulls them toward you, keeps them stuck, and worries them about switching) and a brand voice built from copy that already performed. An optional paid-ads section records target costs, budget, which conversions count, and what the agent may and may not change without approval. Every substantive save bumps the version and adds a dated changelog line saying what changed and why; typo fixes don't. A Learnings table logs test results and decisions with their evidence, each marked active, watch or retired, and rows are added only with your approval.",
