        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a feature from its approved PRODUCT.md and TECH.md, updating both specs in the same PR whenever the implementation changes course.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The product and tech specs are approved and it's time to build"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks the specs exist and are approved, plans steps against them, builds with tests, and edits the specs whenever behavior or design changes"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The feature's code and tests, with the specs edited to describe what actually ships, in the same PR as the code when practical"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "PRODUCT.md and, when warranted, TECH.md under specs/<ticket>/, as write-product-spec and write-tech-spec write them"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The building step of the spec workflow. It first confirms that PRODUCT.md exists, TECH.md too when the feature called for one, and that both have been reviewed and approved enough to start. PRODUCT.md is the source of truth for what users see, TECH.md for architecture, sequencing and the shape of the implementation. The agent breaks the work into concrete steps, builds against the specs, and adds tests and verification as the work lands. For large or long-running features it may offer a PROJECT_LOG.md of checkpoints and explored paths, or a DECISIONS.md of product and technical decisions, only when they'd help. When building shows that behavior or design should change, it updates the specs right away rather than at the end, in the same PR as the code, so the PR describes the feature that actually ships. Before calling it done, it checks the code against the current specs with unit, regression, and integration or end-to-end tests that follow the repo's conventions.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/warpdotdev/common-skills/tree/8792394ff1b655e0af451b8fabb68ef0cfcbd208/.agents/skills/implement-specs"
        },
