    {
      "id": "addyosmani/agent-skills/skills/incremental-implementation",
      "name": "incremental-implementation",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/addyosmani/agent-skills/incremental-implementation",
        "installs": 73214,
        "weeklyInstalls": [4051, 3778, 3916, 4977, 5644, 5280, 4556, 4131],
        "firstSeen": "2026-02-16"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a change in thin slices, each implemented, tested, verified and committed before the next, touching only what the task needs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A feature or change touches more than one file, or the agent is about to write a lot of code at once"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Builds one small working piece, runs the tests and build, commits it, then moves to the next piece"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A series of small commits, each leaving the project building and tested, and each revertible on its own"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Clean up nearby code or add features outside the task; it lists what it noticed and asks"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The cycle is implement, test, verify, commit, repeat, with each slice the smallest complete piece of functionality. Slices are vertical by default, one path through database, API and UI, such as \"create a task\"; contract-first when front and back end are built in parallel, with the API types defined first; or risk-first, proving the riskiest part works before building on it. Rules keep each slice clean: start with the simplest thing that could work and no abstraction until a third use; touch only what the task needs and list anything else worth fixing instead of fixing it; one logical change per increment; the project builds and tests pass after every slice; unfinished features hide behind feature flags; new options default to the safe choice; and each increment can be reverted alone, with rollback migrations for schema changes. After each slice the agent runs the repository's own test, build, type-check and lint commands, without rerunning one when nothing has changed. More than about 100 lines without a test run is a red flag.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/tree/301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde/skills/incremental-implementation"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "implementation",
          "scope-control"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "addyosmani/agent-skills/skills/git-workflow-and-versioning",
      "name": "git-workflow-and-versioning",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/addyosmani/agent-skills/git-workflow-and-versioning",
        "installs": 71058,
        "weeklyInstalls": [4012, 3719, 3878, 4953, 5603, 5303, 4680, 4248],
        "firstSeen": "2026-02-16"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Keeps git history clean: short-lived branches, small atomic commits with messages that explain why, and releases tagged with semantic versions and changelogs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The agent commits, branches, splits messy work into commits, opens a PR, writes a changelog entry or cuts a release"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Applies trunk-based habits: main always deployable, branches merged within one to three days, one logical change per commit"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Commits like \"feat: add email validation\" with the why in the body, and a summary of what changed and what was left alone"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "Pre-commit checks for secrets, worktrees for parallel agents, git bisect and blame, semantic versioning, tags and changelogs written for users"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Git is treated as a safety net: commits are save points, branches are sandboxes, history is documentation. The agent works trunk-based, keeping main deployable and feature branches short-lived, with feature flags rather than long branches for unfinished work. It commits after each passing increment and goes back to the last commit when a test fails. Each commit does one thing, never mixing formatting, refactoring and features, and aims for about 100 changed lines. Messages follow type: description (feat, fix, refactor, test, docs, chore) with a body explaining why. After a change it writes a summary of what it changed, what it deliberately didn't touch, and any concerns. Before committing it checks the staged diff, searches it for likely secrets and runs tests, lint and type checks. Git worktrees let several agents work on separate branches at once. For anything with consumers, versions follow semver, where a behavior change users relied on is major whatever its size; releases are tagged and the version derived from the tag; and the changelog is curated for users, written with the change rather than dumped from commits.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/tree/301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde/skills/git-workflow-and-versioning"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:remote",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "stack:git",
          "git"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "addyosmani/agent-skills/skills/idea-refine",
      "name": "idea-refine",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/addyosmani/agent-skills/idea-refine",
        "installs": 70492,
        "weeklyInstalls": [3884, 3622, 3811, 4856, 5727, 5345, 4728, 4060],
        "firstSeen": "2026-02-19"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde",
