      "skillMd": {
        "version": "301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Sets up CI that blocks merges until lint, type checks, tests, build and a security audit pass, and plans deploys you can roll back.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You set up or change a build and deploy pipeline, add automated checks, or a CI failure needs fixing"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Lays out a pipeline where every pull request passes lint, type check, unit tests, build, integration tests, optional end-to-end tests, an audit and a bundle-size check"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "GitHub Actions workflows for CI, a Postgres integration job, Playwright tests, preview deploys and a rollback, plus a Dependabot config"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rule",
              "text": "No gate gets skipped: a failing lint rule is fixed, not disabled, and a failing test means fixing the code, not skipping the test"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "Feeding CI errors back to the agent, feature flags, staged rollouts, secrets per environment, branch protection and speeding up slow pipelines"
            }
          ],
          "text": "CI is framed as the enforcement mechanism for every other skill, built on two ideas: shift left, catching problems as early in the pipeline as possible, and faster is safer, since small, frequent releases are easier to debug. Every change passes the same gates before review: lint, type check, unit tests, build, integration tests, optional end-to-end tests, a security audit and a bundle-size check, and none can be skipped. The examples are GitHub Actions: a basic quality job on Node, an integration job with a Postgres service and Prisma migrations, a Playwright job that uploads its report on failure, a Vercel preview deploy per pull request, and a manual rollback workflow that passes its input through an environment variable to avoid shell injection. When CI fails, the error goes back to the agent to fix and verify locally before pushing again. It also covers feature flags with a cleanup date, staged rollouts with a monitoring window, keeping production secrets out of CI, Dependabot, a Build Cop who keeps the build green, required reviews and status checks, and, for pipelines over ten minutes, caching, parallel jobs, path filters and sharded tests.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/tree/301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde/skills/ci-cd-and-automation"
        },
