      "skillMd": {
        "version": "301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Interviews you for a quality bar, records it in CONSTRAINTS.md with the commands that enforce it, and catches diffs that weaken it.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "No quality bar is written down, or an agent keeps skipping tests and silencing checks to get to green"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Detects your stack, asks four questions with defaults, writes CONSTRAINTS.md, installs a standard tool per dimension and places each check by cost"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "CONSTRAINTS.md with a floor, enforced rules that each name their command, measured numbers that mustn't get worse, and dated exceptions"
            },
            {
              "label": "Catches",
              "text": "Lowered thresholds, skipped or deleted tests, new @ts-ignore or eslint-disable comments, empty catch blocks, stubs and undiscussed exceptions"
            },
            {
              "label": "Defaults",
              "text": "80% coverage of changed lines, no vulnerabilities rated high or above, LCP of 2.5 seconds or less, no critical or serious accessibility violations, exceptions lasting 90 days"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Its interview only with a person present; in CI or loops it applies just the floor and flags the rest"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Other skills describe good code in prose an agent may forget; this one writes the project's own bar down, with numbers, where any agent and the build can check it. It reads what it can first, stack, test runner, linters, coverage, CI, then asks four questions one at a time, each with a default: which dimensions to enforce beyond the floor (coverage, security, performance, accessibility, architecture), block or warn, target numbers or today's values, and the slowest check you'll tolerate. The floor applies to every project: no new suppression comments, stubs or empty catch blocks, no unexplained skipped tests, no secrets, and no weakening the file itself. Each chosen dimension gets a standard tool, such as Semgrep, gitleaks, osv-scanner, Lighthouse, axe or Stryker, a package script, and a test against a known violation; fast checks run after each edit, slow ones at task end or in CI. Without a target it uses a ratchet: record today's number and refuse to get worse. At review it checks the diff for the five ways agents lower the bar. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md get a line pointing to it. A gate script and a diff-scoped floor checker ship with the skill.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/tree/301b02b12bff98e4688e6984af6556802322bbde/skills/constraint-driven-development"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
