      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Interviews you about your brand, then designs a landing page with Stitch, iterates on your feedback and bundles deployment-ready HTML.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've built a product or side project and need a landing page, but have no visual direction or brand yet"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Interviews you in about ten questions, turns your answers into a design system in Stitch, a service that generates screens from text prompts, then generates the page"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A zip with index.html, an optional mobile.html, DESIGN.md, color tokens and a DEPLOY.md checklist"
            },
            {
              "label": "Iterates",
              "text": "Opens each version in your browser, asks three feedback questions, and turns your answers into edits or new variants"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A Stitch API key; the agent installs the Stitch SDK"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Pages you already have a mockup for, dashboards, app UI, multi-page apps or restyling with known design tokens; it points you to frontend-design"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A design consultant for developers who have built something but haven't thought about brand. Before generating anything, it gets the Stitch SDK working and checks your API key with one call. The interview has three parts: the product (name, what it does, who it's for, what visitors should do), brand feel (three adjectives, a landing page you admire, light or dark) and visual preferences (colors, modern or traditional type, sharp or rounded shapes). It maps those answers to Stitch's design-system settings and documents them in .stitch/DESIGN.md. Then it generates a desktop page, opens it in your browser and loops: a specific request becomes a direct edit, general dissatisfaction two or three variants to compare, and \"something totally different\" a full rethink. Every version is kept, and the state saved in .stitch/metadata.json lets a later session resume without interviewing you again. After you approve the desktop page it offers a mobile layout, then zips the final files for deployment. It doesn't take your logo as input, since Stitch generates from text; it saves any image you attach so you can swap it into the HTML.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/brand-landingpage/skills/brand-landingpage"
