    {
      "id": "wshobson/agents/plugins/developer-essentials/skills/code-review-excellence",
      "name": "code-review-excellence",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/wshobson/agents/code-review-excellence",
        "installs": 31000,
        "weeklyInstalls": [333, 363, 417, 362, 380, 370, 334, 277],
        "firstSeen": "2026-01-20"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews pull requests in four phases, from context to line-by-line checks, with constructive, prioritized feedback and a review comment template.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're reviewing a pull request, or setting review standards or a checklist for a team"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Walks a review through four phases: context, high-level design, line-by-line checks, then a summary and a clear verdict"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Review comments in a template of summary, strengths, required changes, suggestions, questions and verdict, with blocking issues kept apart from nits"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "Phrasing hard feedback, handling disagreement, and pitfalls such as rubber-stamping and bike-shedding"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A review process plus advice on tone. Before reading code, the agent reads the PR description and linked issue, checks the size (over 400 lines, ask to split it) and whether CI passes. A high-level pass asks whether the solution fits the problem, whether something simpler exists and whether tests cover the edge cases. The line-by-line pass checks logic (off-by-one errors, null checks, race conditions), security (input validation, SQL injection, XSS, exposed data), performance (N+1 queries, memory leaks, blocking calls) and maintainability. It ends with the key concerns, what was done well, and a verdict: approve, comment or request changes. Formatting, import order and lint issues are left to tools. Feedback should be specific, actionable and about the code rather than the person, with nits marked non-blocking; hard feedback goes context, specific issue, then a helpful solution. Much of the advice also speaks to human reviewers and teams: review within a day, keep PRs to 200-400 lines, offer to pair. Two extra files hold review techniques and checklists for language, architecture, test and security reviews.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/developer-essentials/skills/code-review-excellence"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:debugging",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
