            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3.12+ and Node, yt-dlp for YouTube, and API keys or cookies for some sources; Hacker News and Polymarket work without any"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A research engine for recent community opinion. The agent checks for a usable web-search tool and, on first run, walks you through setup, asking before it reads browser cookies. For a topic, it resolves the relevant handles, subreddits and hashtags, writes a JSON query plan itself and passes it to the bundled engine, which searches each source and returns ranked evidence with engagement counts. The agent turns that into prose paragraphs with inline links, weaves in at least two quoted, attributed comments when qualifying ones exist, gives Polymarket odds as percentages, and ends with the engine's source footer; when nothing solid turned up, it says so instead of padding. Other modes compare two or three things, rank what's trending in a field, look at competitors or hiring signals, recommend items, answer follow-ups from saved research, or export an HTML brief, which it publishes to ht-ml.app only if you ask, where it's public unless password-protected. Keyed calls to ScrapeCreators spend credits. It never posts, likes or edits anything on these platforms.",
