      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Generates images from prompts and reference images through a dozen AI providers, one at a time or in parallel batches.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want images made from a prompt, prompt files or reference images, one or many"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Calls an image API, such as OpenAI, Google, Azure, OpenRouter, Replicate, DashScope, MiniMax or Seedream, through its bundled script"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Image files at the paths you name, in the aspect ratio you ask for, at 2K quality by default"
            },
            {
              "label": "Batches",
              "text": "Runs a JSON file of prompts in parallel, up to 10 at once by default, giving each image up to 3 attempts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx, plus an API key for one provider or a logged-in codex CLI"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "The repo's cover, illustration, infographic, card, slide and comic skills, which can use it to generate their images"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The image backend of Baoyu's skills, also usable on its own. On first use it won't generate anything until you've picked a provider, model, quality and save location, which it saves as preferences. When you don't name a provider, it uses the one whose API key it finds, preferring Google, then OpenAI, when there are several; with reference images it only picks providers that accept them. Before each image it says which provider and model it's using and how to switch. To keep a real person or object recognizable across images, it uses short instructions to keep the same identity and two to four reference images, since long descriptions make models invent a lookalike. A Codex or ChatGPT login isn't an OpenAI API key: the codex-cli provider uses that subscription through the codex command instead, and is never picked automatically. When prompts are already saved as files, a batch file runs them with shared throttling and retries, and can be built from what baoyu-article-illustrator writes.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-image-gen"
