        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds where an article needs pictures, generates the illustrations and inserts them into the Markdown.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "An article needs illustrations and you'd rather not decide where each one goes or draw them"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Finds the passages a picture would help, asks how many and in what style, writes a prompt for each and generates them"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The images in an imgs folder next to the article, linked in after their paragraphs, plus an outline.md listing each one"
            },
            {
              "label": "Image types",
              "text": "Infographic, scene, flowchart, comparison, framework and timeline, in styles such as minimal-flat, sci-fi, hand-drawn or editorial"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "An image generator: your agent's own (as in Codex or Cursor), baoyu-image-gen with an API key, or a logged-in codex CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It first works out the article's kind (technical, tutorial, methodology or narrative), its two to five core arguments and where a visual adds value; metaphors are drawn as the idea behind them, not literally. Then comes one round of questions: a preset or image type, how many images (one or two, three to five, one per section, or six or more), a style and an optional palette (macaron, warm or neon). Every prompt is saved to a file before any image is made, with labels drawn from the article's actual numbers, terms and quotes. Images then render in batches, four at a time by default when the agent can make parallel calls, and failed ones are retried once. Preferences, such as the output folder, a watermark and a default style, are set up on first run. If text in an image comes out wrong, it writes a new prompt and regenerates instead of patching the picture.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-article-illustrator"
