      "skillMd": {
        "version": "ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Saves web pages as Markdown through Chrome, with site adapters for X, YouTube transcripts and Hacker News threads.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a web page saved as a Markdown file, including pages that need a login or a CAPTCHA"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Loads the page in Chrome with its bundled baoyu-fetch tool, using adapters for X, YouTube transcripts and Hacker News threads, and Defuddle for other pages"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown file under url-to-markdown/<domain>/<slug>/, optionally with its images and videos downloaded and relinked"
            },
            {
              "label": "Logins",
              "text": "A wait mode lets you log in or solve a CAPTCHA in the browser, then carries on"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun, and Chrome or Chromium"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike defuddle",
              "text": "Kepano's defuddle skill runs a command-line tool on a URL; this one drives a real browser and has site adapters"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Before its first conversion it asks a few setup questions, such as whether to download media and where to save, and stores the answers; it never assumes them silently. If the fetcher's packages aren't installed yet, it installs them with Bun first. The fetcher runs Chrome headless by default and prints Markdown, or writes Markdown or JSON to a file. For pages that need you, one wait mode notices a login or CAPTCHA and continues once it's cleared, another waits for you to press Enter. It can reuse a Chrome that's already running with its debugging port open, or a profile you name. Because headless captures sometimes return thin content without any error, the agent checks the saved Markdown after each headless run against a quality checklist. A debug option saves the captured HTML and network log.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown"
