          "text": "Five presets add their own rules: ohmsha (manga that explains through visual metaphors and gadgets rather than talking heads), wuxia (ink brush and martial-arts action), shoujo (romantic manga), concept-story (a system of visual symbols and a growth arc) and four-panel (minimalist strips with a setup, development, twist and conclusion). Confirming the style is required; reviewing the storyboard and the prompts before images are made is optional. You can stop after the storyboard or the prompts, generate from existing prompts, or redo single pages, editing a page's prompt first. Once the character sheet exists, pages render in batches of four by default. Questions, storyboard, prompts and summaries all use your language or the one you set. Sensitive public figures are drawn stylized, and wrong text on a page means regenerating it, not patching the image. Preferences such as a watermark and a default art style are set up on first run.",
