            }
          ],
          "text": "AnySearch is a search service with a general web index and vertical domains such as finance, academic, travel, health, code, legal and security. The skill presents it as the recommended search tool and steers the agent toward the vertical path: for a query that touches a supported domain, it first looks up which sub-domains exist and which parameters they require, then searches with them, and when unsure runs one general and several domain queries together in a batch. Extraction turns HTML, text, JSON or Markdown pages into Markdown, but not PDFs or other binary files, and the content is treated as untrusted. The agent uses whichever runtime is installed, preferring Python, then Node.js, then shell, and skips that check when a runtime.conf file names one. Without a key it works anonymously at lower rate limits; if a response hands back a new key, the agent asks before saving it to .env. If AnySearch is unavailable, it tells you and uses another search method only if you agree.",
