        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns data analysis into a story for stakeholders, with narrative structures, presentation templates, annotated charts and headline formulas.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're presenting analytics to executives or investors, writing a data report or business review, or explaining findings to a non-technical audience"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Shapes findings into an arc: a hook, the baseline, the data that builds up, the key insight, recommendations and a call to action"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A report or presentation that leads with the insight and ends with next steps"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "Headlines that state a number and its business impact, transition phrases, and ways to state uncertainty such as ranges and confidence levels"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A guide to presenting data, not to analyzing it. The core is a story structure: set up the context and baseline, name the problem or opportunity, then resolve it with insights and recommendations, carried by three pillars of data, narrative and visuals. Its rules: start with the \"so what\", group in threes, curate instead of dumping data, connect to the audience's goals, avoid jargon, give context before method and end with clear next steps. A separate file holds three story frameworks (problem and solution, trend, comparison), each worked through on an example such as a churn analysis; visualization techniques such as revealing a chart one layer per slide, before-and-after contrasts and annotating a chart in matplotlib; templates for an executive summary slide, a seven-slide deck from the headline to the ask, and a one-page monthly business review; and writing techniques: headlines built from a number, its business impact and context, transition phrases and ways to present uncertainty.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/business-analytics/skills/data-storytelling"
