      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs KPI dashboards: which metrics to show to whom, how to lay them out, and how to fix numbers people don't trust.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're choosing KPIs and laying out an executive, departmental or real-time operations dashboard, or fixing one whose numbers contradict each other"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sorts KPIs into strategic, tactical and operational levels by audience and update frequency, and limits a dashboard to 5-7 of them"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A dashboard plan, from a one-page executive summary down to department views and drilldowns"
            },
            {
              "label": "Troubleshoots",
              "text": "MRR that disagrees with finance, green dashboards while users complain, flat cohorts, live dashboards that overload the database, and ignored alerts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Guidance for business dashboards. KPIs should be specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound, and actionable rather than vanity metrics; each number needs context such as a trend, target or comparison; red means bad and green good; no 3D charts; calculations are documented; and the dashboard should work on mobile. The troubleshooting is concrete: normalize annual and quarterly plans to a monthly figure and show the formula, add user-facing metrics such as page load time and support tickets beside uptime, group cohorts by month rather than day, feed live dashboards from a summary table refreshed by a scheduled job instead of querying production, and alert on deviations from a 30-day rolling mean instead of fixed thresholds. A separate file lists common KPIs for sales, marketing, product and finance, layouts for executive, SaaS and operations dashboards, SQL for KPI calculations, and a dashboard in Streamlit.",
