          "text": "A reference for OpenAPI 3.1, the standard format for describing REST APIs. Writing the spec before the code suits new APIs and contracts, generating it from code suits existing APIs, and annotating code to generate it suits APIs that keep changing. Its rules: reuse schemas, parameters and responses with $ref, add realistic examples, document every error code, version the API in the URL or a header and the spec with semantic versioning, define every security scheme, state nullability explicitly, keep naming consistent and use server variables instead of hardcoded URLs. The separate file's spec has list, create, read, update and delete endpoints with pagination, schemas for users, requests, paginated lists and errors, shared parameters, standard responses for bad requests, missing auth, not found and rate limits, and bearer-token and API-key security. That file points to a third with code-first templates for FastAPI and for TypeScript with tsoa, linting with Spectral and Redocly, and generating TypeScript, Python and Go clients with OpenAPI Generator.",
