        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Translates a file, a URL or pasted text in one of three modes, from a single quick pass to a reviewed, polished translation.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want an article or document translated so it reads as if written in the target language, Simplified Chinese by default"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Analyzes the source, builds a translation prompt with a glossary, translates, and in refined mode critiques, revises and polishes"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "translation.md in a folder next to the source, with each intermediate step's file kept beside it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Modes",
              "text": "Quick translates in one pass; normal, the default, analyzes first; refined adds a critique, a revision and a final polish"
            },
            {
              "label": "Long texts",
              "text": "From 4,000 words, its script splits the text at Markdown blocks and subagents draft the chunks in parallel, when the agent has them"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "The Markdown formatting, facts and data, and consistent terms from your glossaries plus a built-in English-to-Chinese one"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "Target language, mode, audience, style and where to save preferences, before its first translation"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx, to split long texts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Its rule is to rewrite rather than translate word for word: natural word order, long sentences broken up, idioms rendered by meaning, specialized terms followed by the original in parentheses the first time, and a few bold explanations where the audience may lack context. Audience presets (general, technical, academic, business) set how much it explains; style presets such as storytelling (the default), formal, literal, humorous or elegant set the voice, and both accept your own description. Saying 快翻 or quick picks quick mode, 精翻 or refined the refined one. After a normal translation you can reply 继续润色 or refine to run the review steps on it. Source frontmatter is kept, with its fields renamed with a source prefix and translated values added. At the end it lists images that probably still carry text in the source language, and leaves them alone unless you ask. Glossaries can be set inline or as files in its preferences, or passed per run.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-translate"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:writing",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:cli",
          "by:community",
          "writing"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "jimliu/baoyu-skills/.claude/skills/release-skills",
      "name": "release-skills",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/jimliu/baoyu-skills/release-skills",
        "installs": 26000,
        "weeklyInstalls": [260, 196, 257, 135, 125, 142, 140, 149],
