              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx, Chrome or Chromium, and a Weibo account you log in to once"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Its scripts drive a real Chrome, which it says avoids Weibo's anti-bot detection, and the login from your first run persists. For an article, it converts the Markdown to HTML in the default theme, clicks 写文章 in Weibo's editor, fills in the title (32 characters at most, truncated with a warning) and summary (44 at most, regenerated from the content if longer), pastes the body, then swaps each image placeholder for its image through the clipboard. Title, summary and cover can come from the file's frontmatter or from options. If Chrome's debugging port doesn't answer, it kills only the Chrome instances running with its own profile, without asking, and retries. A preferences file can set a default Chrome profile.",
