          "text": "Test code written from a scenario's description alone is a guess about the page. This skill forbids that: the agent may not generate test code prematurely or from the scenario alone. It first performs every step of the scenario itself, one at a time, with the tools of the Playwright MCP server. Only once all steps are done does it write a Playwright test in TypeScript with @playwright/test, based on the session's history of those steps. It saves the file in the tests directory, runs it, and keeps iterating until the test passes. If you don't give a scenario, it asks for one first.",
