          "needs:none",
          "by:official",
          "stack:git",
          "git"
        ],
        "note": "Runs git commit as soon as the message is built, without asking you to confirm it.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "github/awesome-copilot/skills/chrome-devtools",
      "name": "chrome-devtools",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/github/awesome-copilot/chrome-devtools",
        "installs": 15400,
        "weeklyInstalls": [71, 92, 91, 68, 71, 53, 61, 52],
        "firstSeen": "2026-01-23"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Drives and inspects a live Chrome through the Chrome DevTools MCP server: navigation, clicks and forms, screenshots, console, network and performance traces.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want the agent to work in a real Chrome page: click through it, read its console and network traffic, or find out why it's slow"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Maps the chrome-devtools MCP server's tools for pages, input, inspection, emulation and performance tracing, with three worked patterns"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The chrome-devtools MCP server connected to your agent"
            },
            {
              "label": "Snapshot first",
              "text": "It finds elements in a text accessibility tree, whose element IDs the click and fill tools need, and keeps screenshots for visual checks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Patterns",
              "text": "Act on an element, troubleshoot a broken page from console and network errors, and profile a slow load for LCP and layout shifts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for the chrome-devtools MCP server, which lets the agent control and inspect a live Chrome browser. It groups the server's tools into four sets: opening, navigating, switching, closing and waiting on pages; input, such as clicks, form filling, hovering, key presses, drag and drop, dialogs and file uploads; inspection, through accessibility snapshots, screenshots, console messages, JavaScript run in the page and network requests; and emulation and performance, from resizing the viewport and throttling CPU or network to recording a trace and analysing its insights. Three patterns show how they fit together. To act on an element, take a snapshot, find its uid and pass it to click or fill. To troubleshoot a failing page, list console messages for JavaScript errors and network requests for failed 4xx or 5xx resources, then evaluate a script to check DOM elements or globals. To profile a slow page, start a trace that reloads and stops itself, then analyse its insights for LCP (Largest Contentful Paint, when the main content shows) or layout shifts. It reminds the agent to check which tab is active, take a new snapshot after navigation because uids change, and keep waits to reasonable timeouts.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/chrome-devtools"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:browser",
          "category:debugging",
