            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent asks for the URL if you haven't given one, then detects the framework and styling method from files such as package.json and tailwind.config, so it knows whether a fix belongs in plain CSS, SCSS, CSS Modules, Tailwind classes or CSS-in-JS. It visits the pages, captures screenshots and the DOM, and works through a visual checklist kept in the skill's references, rating issues such as overflowing or overlapping elements, small touch targets, low contrast, missing focus states and mixed fonts as high, medium or low. Fixes go in priority order, one at a time, as minimal changes that follow the project's existing style. After each one it reloads, compares screenshots and checks that nothing else broke, looping until no issues remain. A production site gets a read-only review. Any browser tool with navigation, screenshots and DOM access will do; Selenium, Puppeteer and Cypress are named alongside Playwright MCP.",
