      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Plans a multi-file refactor before any edit: affected files, phased steps with checks, rollback and risks, then waits for your go-ahead.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're about to refactor across several files and want the order of changes worked out before anything is edited"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Reads the code, tests, config and docs, maps affected files, dependencies and hidden coupling, then sequences changes: types first, then implementations, callers, tests and cleanup"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown plan: current and target state, a table of affected files, phased checklists each with a verify step, a rollback plan and risks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stops",
              "text": "After the plan to ask \"Shall I proceed with Phase 1?\", even if you asked it to implement, unless you said to continue without review"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The skill keeps the agent's hands off the code while it plans. It searches the codebase and reads enough implementation, tests, configuration and docs to make the plan specific to your repository, then identifies the files involved, ownership boundaries, dependencies and coupling that could break. Changes are ordered so each phase builds on the last: contracts and types, then implementations, callers, tests and cleanup, with a verification step between phases and a final validation command. The riskiest phases get rollback or recovery steps. If the request is too vague to plan safely, it asks short clarifying questions instead. It edits no files: it outputs the plan, and implementation starts only once you confirm.",
