      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds attack trees that split an attacker's goal into AND/OR steps rated by cost, skill and detection, exposing the easiest paths.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're mapping how an attacker could reach a goal, planning a penetration test, or explaining security risks and defensive priorities to stakeholders"
            },
            {
              "label": "Attack tree",
              "text": "A goal at the root, split into sub-goals; an OR node needs any one child, an AND node all of them, and leaves are single attack steps"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A tree whose attacks are rated by cost, time, skill and detection risk, exportable as a Mermaid or PlantUML diagram"
            },
            {
              "label": "Finds",
              "text": "The easiest, cheapest and stealthiest paths, the nodes most paths go through, open paths left by your mitigations, and which mitigations to do first"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An attack tree starts from what an attacker wants, such as taking over an account, and breaks it down into the ways to get there. This skill gives the agent the structure and the attributes to rate each attack: cost, time, skill needed and likelihood of detection. Its Python templates model nodes and trees, build them step by step with a builder (an account-takeover tree is the example), export them as Mermaid or PlantUML diagrams, and analyze them: every path to the goal, each path's difficulty and cost, the nodes that appear in the most paths, how many paths your mitigations block, and which mitigations block the most. The rules: start from clear attacker goals, consider every vector including insiders, respect what AND nodes require, have a red team review the tree, keep it updated, and use it to plan defenses rather than stopping at the diagram.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/security-scanning/skills/attack-tree-construction"
