      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs reusable UI components in React, Vue and Svelte: compound components, render props, slots, typed prop APIs and styling choices.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're building a component library or design system, designing a component's props, or refactoring old components into composable ones"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Gives the agent composition patterns (compound components, render props, slots), rules for prop APIs, and a comparison of five styling approaches"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Components built along those patterns; it adds no steps or files of its own"
            },
            {
              "label": "Examples in",
              "text": "React with Tailwind and class-variance-authority, a React compound accordion, Vue 3 provide and inject, and Svelte 5 runes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for component architecture across three frameworks. Compound components are related pieces that share state, such as a Select with Select.Trigger and Select.Option; render props hand rendering to the caller through a function; slots are Vue's and Svelte's named places for content. It compares Tailwind, CSS Modules, styled-components, Emotion and Vanilla Extract by approach and best fit. Prop APIs should use semantic names such as isLoading, sensible defaults, children for composition and className or style for overrides. Its quick start is a Button with class-variance-authority variants, forwardRef and a loading state. Framework examples show a React accordion that shares state through context, Vue 3 tabs with provide and inject, and a Svelte 5 button using $props and $derived. Best practices cover single responsibility, context instead of prop drilling, accessibility by default, supporting controlled and uncontrolled use, forwarding refs, memoization and error boundaries; common issues include too many props, style conflicts, re-render cascades and bundle size.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/ui-design/skills/web-component-design"
