          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "planning",
          "architecture",
          "handoff",
          "scope-control"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tw93/waza/skills/hunt",
      "name": "hunt",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/tw93/waza/hunt",
        "installs": 15300,
        "weeklyInstalls": [293, 265, 176, 265, 229, 156, 173, 132],
        "firstSeen": "2026-04-04"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "58217546cd94fcf5ddcde4265c00a9377ed3192c",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds and proves a bug's root cause before any fix, then checks the repo for the same bug pattern and verifies the fix.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Something errors, crashes, regresses or used to work"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Touches no code until it can state the root cause in one sentence with evidence, and runs the probe that would disprove it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The root cause and fix with file:line, a sweep for the same bug elsewhere, the evidence, and a regression test for bugs that came back"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "\"diagnose\" or \"why\" requests report-only; it fixes only when you ask, and a request to fix never covers committing or pushing"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stops",
              "text": "After three failed hypotheses, with a handoff of what was checked, ruled out and still unknown"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Hunt is Waza's debugging skill. A hypothesis has to name a file, function, line or condition and explain every symptom, including ones the reporter waved off; \"I'll just try this\" counts as having none. Regressions get their own mode: read the diff from the last good version first, or git bisect in a temporary worktree so uncommitted work stays untouched. Another mode treats a known-good screenshot or build as the reference to diff against, and after a fix it greps the repo for the same bug pattern and records each match as same bug, safe or unsure. Before calling a bug fixed it climbs an evidence ladder from source trace and repro to logs, tests and, for UI or visual bugs, a real runtime check. Rules cover logs that each answer a yes-or-no question, measuring performance before and after, and stopping after three rounds of tuning a magic number. A bug that came back isn't done until its regression test has run red on the old code and green on the fix. Native-app freezes, rendering bugs and IME issues load their own reference files.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/tw93/waza/tree/58217546cd94fcf5ddcde4265c00a9377ed3192c/skills/hunt"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:debugging",
