      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Adapts Argent's device control to a physical iPhone: which tools exist on hardware, how a backgrounded app behaves, and what to do instead.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The agent drives your app on a physical iPhone, not a simulator"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Lists the Argent tools that exist on a physical iPhone and how they behave when the app is in the background"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An agent that skips unsupported tools and records, profiles or debugs on a simulator instead"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "argent-device-interact, which still applies to everything this skill doesn't list, and the Argent MCP server"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Part of Software Mansion's Argent toolkit, which lets the agent control simulators, emulators and devices. A physical iPhone supports only some of Argent's tools, and this skill is the short contract for it, read alongside argent-device-interact. Observation never changes the screen: describe and await-ui-element fail on a backgrounded app instead of bringing it forward, while gestures and the keyboard bring it back, after which the agent describes again. Launching, opening or restarting an app makes it the app Argent automates; reinstalling clears that and a tool-server restart forgets it, so the agent launches it again. On hardware the agent has app launch and reinstall, describe, screenshots and screenshot diffs, gestures, the home and volume buttons, the keyboard, waits, run-sequence and the e2e tools. Any other device tool fails with a bare \"not supported on ios device\", and the skill's list, not the error, says what to do instead: with no orientation change, shake, paste, permission tool, screen recording, debugger or profiler, the phone is moved by hand, text is typed with the keyboard, permissions are changed in its Settings, and debugging, profiling and recording happen on a simulator. Cable, trust and signing problems go to argent-ios-device-setup.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/software-mansion/argent/tree/b965c94827d6167fd2912a7ca5ad5505040ae4e0/packages/skills/skills/argent-ios-device-interact"
        },
