      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews your current git changes for design, security and reliability problems, ranks them P0 to P3, and fixes only what you pick.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a senior-engineer review of your current git changes before they merge"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks the diff for SOLID and architecture smells, dead code, security and reliability risks, and error-handling, performance and edge-case bugs"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Findings ranked P0 (critical) to P3 (style), each with file, line and a suggested fix, plus an overall verdict: approve, request changes or comment"
            },
            {
              "label": "Then",
              "text": "Asks whether to fix everything, only P0 and P1, specific items or nothing, and changes no code until you choose"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It scopes the change with git status and git diff, looks up related modules when needed, and notes the critical paths the change touches, such as auth, payments and data writes. A diff over 500 lines is summarised by file first, then reviewed in batches by feature. It then works through four checklists that ship with it. SOLID and architecture smells, with a minimal, safe split proposed for any refactor, or an incremental plan when the refactor is big. Removal candidates, split into safe to delete now and deferred with a plan. A security and reliability scan covering injection, XSS, SSRF, auth gaps, leaked secrets, race conditions and unsafe defaults, rating both exploitability and impact. And a code-quality scan for swallowed errors, N+1 queries and boundary bugs. Findings are numbered across four levels, from P0, which blocks the merge, to P3, optional polish. A clean review still says what was checked, what wasn't, and what risk remains. It's review-first: nothing changes until you pick which findings to fix.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/sanyuan0704/sanyuan-skills/tree/08b6572ef108f22d4e8a3ecf9182a4bbef097744/skills/code-review-expert"
        },
