          "text": "The entry point for a broad 'make my application secure' request where the target is not yet one URL or repo. It maps the product's assets, source, running environments, APIs, authentication and constraints, then picks the matching Strix skill per asset: code review, web-app pentest, API testing, OWASP assessment, CI scanning, or the managed cloud. It recommends a first-assessment sequence, review the code first since it is cheapest and maps the authorization model, then pentest staging with the repo as a second target, then add CI, running one asset at a time and reading each report before the next. It consolidates findings into a single list ranked by proven impact rather than scanner severity, deduplicates issues that surface in both code and live runs, and states plainly what was not tested. It defers the actual flags and result-reading to the per-asset skills and hands remediation to the fix skill.",
