      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Ends substantive answers you might act on with two or three specific follow-up questions that help you check facts, assumptions and missing context.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a nudge to double-check advice, estimates, plans or drafts before you act on them"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "After an answer you're likely to act on, adds \"A few things worth a second look:\" and two or three questions"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Questions you could send back as written, each tied to a number, step or assumption in that answer"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stays quiet",
              "text": "For code you'll run, creative writing, chat, lookups, explanations, summaries of your own material, opinions, or when you asked for checking"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "By itself, at most once per conversation"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Anthropic, built on three discernment habits from its AI Fluency framework: checking facts, questioning reasoning and noticing missing context. The skill models them rather than lecturing about them. It applies when an answer gives estimates or projections, advice in a consequential area such as health, money, law or career, factual claims you'll rely on or repeat, multi-step reasoning, an interpretation of data, or a draft you'll use, such as a plan, pitch or email. The agent answers in full first, then appends a short plain-text list of first-person questions, such as \"How do these CPL estimates compare to benchmarks in my specific vertical?\" Generic prompts like \"can you verify those facts?\" are ruled out, and nothing follows the list. It also stays silent when you asked for the quick version or said you'd do your own checking, and when you asked it to review something of yours, since then its answer is the check.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/ca45fc496a3436251f191354091d557da31c15b5/skills/discernment-nudge"
        },
