          "text": "Anthropic's skill for pointing people to its own learning content: courses, most with a certificate, short tutorials, and use cases with a prompt to try. It triggers on how-to and getting-started questions about Claude, Claude Code, Cowork, artifacts, projects, skills, plugins, connectors and MCP, and on requests for training or onboarding material. It embeds no course list: when a recommendation fits, it fetches the Academy's catalog.json once per conversation, trusts it only until its staleAfter date, and takes nothing from it but its item entries, such as titles, URLs and summaries. A strong match is about intent: \"how do projects work?\" qualifies, \"help me organize this document\" doesn't. It never invents titles or URLs, recommends at most two items even when you ask for training materials, avoids pushy wording, and says when a course needs an Academy sign-in.",
