              "text": "Only when you call it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "One of Plannotator's extra skills. Plannotator is a local, browser-based review surface where you mark up an agent's plans, documents and diffs and send the feedback back to it. The plan path adapts its lead section to the task: data flow for backend work, mockups for frontend, before-and-after diagrams for refactoring. A PR explainer has a TL;DR card, why the change was made, a tour of each file with its key diff hunks, a risk map separating files that need careful review from mechanical ones, where to focus, a test plan and, if relevant, a rollout. Everything else, such as architecture diagrams, data tables, slide decks and project recaps, follows visual-explainer's structure and anti-slop rules with Plannotator's colors and fonts swapped in. Any Mermaid diagram must render cleanly in both light and dark palettes before the page is delivered. Across all paths: generous whitespace, one idea per screen, show rather than describe.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/backnotprop/plannotator/tree/a35cc47b50e1b42d3538638cb85f237da83660ce/apps/skills/extra/plannotator-visual-explainer"
        },
