      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Routes your request to the right gstack skill, such as office-hours, review, qa or ship, or answers directly when none fits.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've installed Garry Tan's gstack suite and want each request sent to the gstack skill that fits it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Matches your request against routing rules for dozens of gstack skills, from plan reviews and QA to shipping, security audits and retros"
            },
            {
              "label": "By default",
              "text": "Auto-runs only office-hours, review, qa and ship; otherwise it answers directly, unless you name a skill"
            },
            {
              "label": "Bugs",
              "text": "Makes one read-only check of the cause first, then fixes a narrow bug or hands it to investigate"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The full gstack install with its setup script; without it, it falls back to safe defaults and tells you to run setup"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also",
              "text": "Logs telemetry and session learnings through gstack's scripts, and asks once for privacy consent"
            }
          ],
          "text": "gstack is a large set of role-based skills, and this SKILL.md is only its router. Its rules cover new ideas (office-hours), specs and tickets, plan reviews from CEO, engineering, design and developer-experience angles, bug investigation, QA, code review, shipping and deploys, docs, retros, security audits, PDFs, scraping and iOS testing. A setting called proactive decides how far it goes: off suggests nothing, core, the default, auto-runs four skills, and all invokes whichever skill matches. Browser requests go to browse, which drives the Aside browser with your logged-in sessions first and gstack's own browser otherwise. It routes only to skills that are installed. It starts by running a preamble script, reports its outcome as DONE, DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, BLOCKED or NEEDS_CONTEXT, and sets a voice: direct, no em dashes, no stock AI vocabulary.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/garrytan/gstack/tree/688e3ab9d131bd4f9d7b173d81ed15c299d3387a"
        },
