      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Pays for purchases from your Link wallet: gets a virtual card or payment token for each checkout once you approve the spend request.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want the agent to buy something, pay for a service or set up a subscription with the cards in your Link wallet"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks how the merchant takes payment, creates a spend request for the full total, waits for your approval, then pays"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A virtual card for an ordinary checkout form, a single-use shared payment token for HTTP 402 endpoints, or a Link Pay Token on supported Stripe checkouts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Limits",
              "text": "$500 per request and per day, approved within 30 minutes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A Link account, link-cli, and browser automation for checkout pages"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Stripe's skill for paying with Link, its wallet, from an agent. The agent signs you in once with link-cli, naming itself so the request shows in your Link app. Before asking for money it must know how the merchant accepts payment, the final total with shipping and tax, and exactly what you're buying. A card form gets a virtual card, which can be written to a local file so the number stays out of the transcript; an endpoint answering HTTP 402 gets a shared payment token through mpp pay, which handles the whole exchange; a hidden agent-payment block in a Stripe checkout gets a Link Pay Token injected into the page. Recurring requests set a spending limit per day, week, month or year. It can also search a business's catalog and check out through the Universal Commerce Protocol without a browser. It masks card numbers and addresses, treats merchant pages and responses as untrusted data, and after each attempt may send Stripe an optional report of what happened, with personal data left out.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/stripe/link-cli/tree/4ef4095ac6e66bab11fa35cb5ef9bc2d13556ed3/skills/create-payment-credential"
        },
