      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Adds ready-made CSS transitions to web UI, from dropdowns and modals to toasts and loaders, each pasted with its reduced-motion guard.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're adding motion to web UI, such as a dropdown, modal, toast, tooltip, tabs, skeleton loader or AI thinking state"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Matches the element to one of its transitions by decision rules, pastes that snippet's CSS verbatim and wires its classes, state attributes and any small JavaScript"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Framework-free CSS under t-* classes, with tunable variables on :root and a prefers-reduced-motion block"
            },
            {
              "label": "Commands",
              "text": "Transitions reveal lists the catalog, review finds where transitions would fit, apply installs the best fit, refine maps ad-hoc values to motion tokens"
            },
            {
              "label": "Edits",
              "text": "Only the files a transition needs; apply proposes one and asks first, and review and refine change nothing until you pick a line"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike transitions-polish",
              "text": "That one retunes existing motion by rules such as faster closes; this one installs whole transitions, and its own refine only maps values to tokens"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A catalog of more than thirty portable CSS transitions from transitions.dev, with the rules for choosing one. Each matches a visible UI pattern: a dot on a trigger is a notification badge, a surface growing from its trigger is a dropdown, two labels that share letters (Copy code, Copied) are a text morph, a header with a collapsible body is an accordion. When two could fit it picks the lighter one, and with no clear match it lists the catalog and lets you choose. Installing one means adding the shared variables from _root.css once, pasting the snippet without rewriting selectors or collapsing it into shorthand, wiring the documented hooks, keeping the reduced-motion block and adapting the small script some need. A motion-token scale of durations, easings, distances, scales and blurs sits behind every snippet; transitions refine maps an existing value to a token by what the motion does, not by the nearest number, so a 300ms modal close becomes the 150ms quick duration. It also lists common mistakes, such as replacing exact properties with transition: all. transitions-polish defines its own transitions review, which audits existing motion values instead.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jakubantalik/transitions.dev/tree/e706ea0c6401f92af2ff7098c941bd7f59039058/skills/transitions-dev"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:design",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "stack:css",
          "animation",
          "design-system"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "jakubantalik/transitions.dev/skills/transitions-polish",
      "name": "transitions-polish",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/jakubantalik/transitions.dev/transitions-polish",
        "installs": 13700,
        "weeklyInstalls": [1348, 725, 875, 744, 702, 994, 1227, 997],
