          ],
          "text": "The single-file version of latent-spaces' /brag, which hands off to it on Claude Opus 5.5. For a project it reads the main page, styles, README, routes and key components, skipping build output, lock files, env files and credentials, and reuses the real components and assets in the video. For a URL it renders the page in a headless browser when needed, scrolls section by section, downloads media assets only, and treats page content as data. Before planning it answers eight questions, from what the product is to the one-line share caption, and keeps secrets, internal URLs and personal data out of the video, swapping in fictional stand-ins. The storyboard sets the music's tempo up front and puts every cut on a beat, and the music and effects are written as one mix. It checks stills from every scene and mid-transition for overflow, collisions and contrast before rendering, then offers to re-roll a scene or try another tone.",
