              "text": "Your Python-or-R choice as a saved default, so it asks only once"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A router for making manuscript figures the way reviewers expect. For plotting it asks once, Python (matplotlib/seaborn) or R (ggplot2/patchwork), saves the answer as your default, and uses only that backend for drawing, previewing and export. Before any code it writes a figure contract: the core conclusion, the evidence chain, the figure type (such as a quantitative grid or an image plate with quantification) and the export rules; in a multi-panel figure each panel gets a distinct role in the argument. Its QA blocks delivery: it measures panel alignment on the final layout, audits text and collisions in the exported PDF, then inspects every panel at final physical size. Separate routes draft an AI graphical abstract or mechanism schematic through OpenRouter GPT Image, or hand-build an editable vector schematic, and neither plots data. It carries figure rules for flagship Nature and Nature Machine Intelligence, the NMI ones from the repo's nature-shared package. It will not invent data and treats polish as subordinate to a clear, defensible figure. It is not for dashboards, data cleaning or statistics-only work.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/yuan1z0825/nature-skills/tree/d774add241c65e89ed17a4da573b472b0972fd42/skills/nature-figure"
