            {
              "label": "Unlike nature-writing",
              "text": "That one drafts new sections from your evidence"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The repo's nature-shared package installed alongside"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The polishing half of the Nature writing skills. You give it existing prose and it improves the language without changing the facts, terminology or evidence. It routes on four axes, paper type, section, language (English or Chinese-to-English) and target journal, tells you in one line what it detected, loads only the matching guidance, then applies fixes in a fixed priority: paper-type architecture, section job, journal framing, sentence rules last, with ethics throughout. A paragraph it cannot fix without inventing content is flagged, not papered over. For Results or whole-manuscript compression it applies a main-text discipline: classify each result, keep the shortest sufficient evidence chain in the main text, and pair every addition with a deletion or replacement check, reporting word counts before and after. It can also sweep a manuscript for terminology, unit and number drift. A separate route fixes LaTeX layout, such as sparse pages or oversized floats, by editing and compiling the source and inspecting the rendered pages. Its core rules come from the repo's nature-shared package. Use nature-writing to draft new sections and nature-response for post-review correspondence.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/yuan1z0825/nature-skills/tree/d774add241c65e89ed17a4da573b472b0972fd42/skills/nature-polishing"
