          "text": "Builds a literature-report deck, in Chinese by default, from a paper or your reading notes. It first classifies the paper into one of six types, discovery, methods, resource, clinical, materials or review, tells you which, and follows that type's narrative arc, then runs a nine-step workflow: extract metadata, abstract and figure legends, plan the argument, pick the figures that carry it, crop only the assets the deck will use, write each slide and author the deck directly with python-pptx. A shared terminology ledger, from the repo's nature-shared package, keeps model, gene and dataset names identical across every slide and note. Figure slides carry source labels, and it does not fabricate results or figure details. After the first draft it runs an audit script for layout bounds, text overload and template-sounding Chinese phrasing, fixes high-severity issues and records the result in a QA report. For an existing deck it changes only the requested slides; asking for just an outline gets an outline, not a deck.",
