              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The repo's nature-shared package installed alongside"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The drafting half of the Nature writing skills. It routes on task (manuscript text versus a first-submission package), paper type, section, language (including Chinese notes to English) and journal, tells you in one line what it detected, and loads the matching guidance. Before writing it surfaces the claim, evidence and boundary a section needs. For Results or a full main text it classifies each result and keeps the shortest sufficient evidence chain in the main text, moving the rest to captions, Methods or SI. Missing evidence becomes a labelled placeholder, never invented content, and each major claim is marked supported, needing evidence or inferred. The submission-package mode instead drafts the initial cover letter, title page, highlights, author contributions and declarations from facts you supply, with a readiness verdict, and fills LaTeX templates into your folder on request. It owns initial submission; nature-response owns post-decision correspondence, nature-reviewer simulates peer review, and nature-figure handles graphical abstracts. Its core rules come from the repo's nature-shared package.",
