            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Ready-to-paste statement text mapping each dataset to a concrete location, plus a list of fields you still need to fill"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "\"available upon request\" flagged as weak unless a specific restriction justifies it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An eight-step workflow for the data-availability side of submission. It identifies the journal, inventories every supporting dataset, and classifies each into one access route (public repository, controlled access, within paper, reused public, third-party restricted, justified request, or not applicable), then chooses a repository and identifier strategy before drafting. The statement maps each dataset to a concrete location, adds formal dataset citations, and passes a FAIR audit, a check that the data are findable, accessible, interoperable and reusable. It never invents DOIs, accession numbers, licences, embargo dates or access committees, and returns the statement text plus the fields you still need to resolve. Editing or auditing one existing statement keeps its identifiers and skips the full inventory. It carries exact rules for flagship Nature and for Nature Machine Intelligence, including NMI's separate Code availability section; the NMI rules come from the repo's nature-shared package. Chinese-speaking authors also get a Chinese check block. It is not for data cleaning or statistical analysis.",
