      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Drafts, audits or revises point-by-point responses to peer review, revision cover letters and marked-manuscript or LaTeX packages.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have an editor decision and reviewer comments and need replies, a full revision package, or an edit of an existing response"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Parses the decision letter, classifies every comment, and drafts a separate reply per reviewer that shows no other reviewer's comments"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An internal tracker, per-reviewer responses, an optional cover letter, red-marked manuscript and LaTeX files, and a readiness verdict"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike its siblings",
              "text": "nature-reviewer writes the reviews, and nature-writing prepares the initial submission"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The repo's nature-shared package whenever a reply edits the main text"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Turns a revision invitation into a complete response package. It parses the editor email for decision type, instructions, reviewer boundaries, required files and deadlines; if the decision is unclear it asks whether this is a Major or Minor Revision rather than guessing from the comments. The decision sets the overall strategy, evidence-first for Major, bounded corrections for Minor, while a serious concern stays serious in either. It assigns IDs to editor and reviewer items and keeps a master tracker, never shown to reviewers, where duplicates and conflicts are reconciled. Each reviewer gets a standalone reply that answers repeated concerns in full and reveals nothing from the other reports. Every claimed change maps to a manuscript location or a placeholder, and counts as done only when it matches revised text you supplied. Main-text edits stay as short as possible, with extra detail routed to SI. It can mark changes in red on a backed-up copy and fill LaTeX cover-letter, response and redline templates, rerunning a consistency script after each edit. A wording edit or an audit of one reply gets just that. It invents nothing and marks what you must supply.",
