          "text": "Creates a faithful bilingual reader of a paper rather than a summary. It detects the source format (text PDF, scanned PDF, HTML, a DOI/arXiv link to resolve, or pasted text) and loads the matching extraction guidance, then follows a source-map-first workflow: give every block a stable anchor, extract figures and tables, render equations, and translate prose for meaning while leaving math untouched. The output is paper.md with paired Original and 中文 blocks, a source_map.json of those anchors, a translation_notes.md and an assets folder, checked by a deterministic math validator before delivery, plus a reader.html preview only if you ask. If it cannot fully process the source it still produces a draft and labels the gaps, never switching to summary mode. A question about the paper or a requested excerpt gets just that, cited to the source, without rebuilding the reader. A shared terminology ledger from the repo's nature-shared package keeps recurring terms consistent, so install that package alongside it.",
