              "text": "You want a pre-submission referee view of a manuscript or excerpt"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs three reviewers in isolated contexts on the same manuscript and criteria, then a separate forensic consistency audit and a synthesis"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Three independent reviewer reports with major and minor concerns tied to the text, plus a cross-review synthesis"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Subagents or separate runs, so each reviewer works in its own context"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Produces a referee-side assessment package. It builds one immutable review packet (the supplied manuscript, verified anchors and common journal criteria) and gives each reviewer an emphasis brief, a lens set in advance rather than a persona, then runs each reviewer in a genuinely separate context so none sees another's work; without isolation it generates one report per invocation or states that blindness is not guaranteed. Each reviewer assesses the manuscript on five axes (originality, importance, interdisciplinary interest, soundness, readability) and files major concerns and minor comments with claim and evidence pointers, marking a major concern as blocking only when the paper's central case cannot stand without it. It never invents locations and sets no concern quota. After the reports are frozen it runs a separate forensic consistency audit (arithmetic, metric bounds, duplication) and a synthesis that marks consensus only when two reviewers independently raise the same concern. It does not claim the editor's decision or that the paper fits Nature. Use nature-response for the author's rebuttal.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/yuan1z0825/nature-skills/tree/d774add241c65e89ed17a4da573b472b0972fd42/skills/nature-reviewer"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:science",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:subagents",
          "by:community",
          "research"
        ],
        "note": "When checking the manuscript against itself it can load a consistency-sweep file from the repo's nature-shared support package; install that alongside for that check.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
