      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns research papers or inventor materials into evidence-grounded Chinese invention patent drafts and technical disclosures.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a Chinese invention patent draft, or a technical disclosure (技术交底书) for a patent attorney, from a paper or project materials"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Ties every claimed feature to a source passage, equation, figure or code, drafts claims first, then aligns the specification, figures and abstract"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "DOCX files for the claims, specification, abstract and abstract figure plus validation reports, or a disclosure as Markdown and DOCX"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "Features without source support out of formal claims; it is a drafting aid, not a legal opinion"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python; for disclosures also Node.js for diagrams and Playwright for the patent-office search"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A router for drafting Chinese patents from research. It detects the source format, the task (full draft, claim set, disclosure analysis, technical disclosure, disclosure revision or paper-patent audit) and the invention type, then gives every paper block, equation, figure and code item a stable ID. Every material feature in a formal claim must map to those IDs, and unsupported features are left out. Full applications go through stage gates: the source map, terminology and evidence ledgers and the invention concept must pass before claims are drafted, then the specification, embodiments, figures and abstract follow the claims' wording and step order. Formal documents are in Chinese, with formulas as editable Office Math and a main flowchart drawn from the principal method claim; validation scripts must pass before the DOCX package is built. The technical-disclosure route instead mines patent points, searches published Chinese patents on the CNIPA site, falling back to web search, and writes a timestamped Markdown and DOCX disclosure. It never infers inventorship, prior-art conclusions or legal sufficiency, and the package is for inventor and patent-professional review, not a patentability or infringement opinion.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/yuan1z0825/nature-skills/tree/d774add241c65e89ed17a4da573b472b0972fd42/skills/nature-paper-to-patent"
