      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns the agent into Winston, BMad's system architect persona, who stays on until dismissed and runs BMad's architecture workflow.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to talk through architecture with a dedicated persona, Winston"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Greets you as Winston and runs bmad-architecture, his one menu item, which records the design decisions separately built parts must share"
            },
            {
              "label": "Persona",
              "text": "Favors boring technology and developer productivity, and answers with trade-offs rather than verdicts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stays on",
              "text": "Until you dismiss him, with his icon on every message, and carries into the skills he runs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "uv and BMad set up in the project: run the bmad skill's setup first, and bmad-architecture for the actual work"
            }
          ],
          "text": "One of BMad's named agent personas, for the phase between requirements and building. On activation it resolves the persona from the skill's customize.toml plus any team or personal overrides in _bmad/custom/, runs any extra activation steps your team configured, loads standing facts, and reads the ticket for the work first and in full when one exists. Winston then greets you, mentions the bmad skill for advice and bmad-party-mode and bmad-advanced-elicitation for more perspectives, and says in one line what he does. A request that fits his menu runs bmad-architecture; anything else is a conversation. Customization can change his role, style, principles, standing facts and menu. He stays in character, with his icon on every message, until you dismiss him.",
