          "skill-authoring",
          "agent-workflows"
        ],
        "note": "Needs uv and BMad set up in the project: it runs scripts from the _bmad/ folder that the bmad skill's setup creates.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bmad-code-org/bmad-method/skills/bmad-walkthrough",
      "name": "bmad-walkthrough",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/bmad-code-org/bmad-method/bmad-walkthrough",
        "installs": 15000,
        "weeklyInstalls": [957, 1191, 2286, 2530, 1461, 1631, 1430, 1482],
        "firstSeen": "2026-08-28"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "e734d3ac3c0f4ea31cc2c2bbbe79e86e54f2cae6",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Walks you through a commit, PR, file or directory one block at a time, in a written narrative, until you call each part done.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to review a commit, PR, file or directory yourself, with the agent as guide, rather than have it review for you"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Splits the target into blocks: its intent, its broad strokes, one slice per concern, then the periphery, and stays on each until you say it's done"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A review narrative with a checkbox per block and a separate log of findings, decisions, edits and tests, in a walkthrough folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Moves",
              "text": "A second opinion, a formal review, testing, a demo, a diagram or driving the app; none starts unless you pick it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Only when invoked by name"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "uv and BMad set up in the project: run the bmad skill's setup first"
            }
          ],
          "text": "BMad's walkthrough treats your attention as scarce: it shows only what you need to see and keeps its bookkeeping out of the session. It first works out what the target is and what it's for, reading the ticket when one covers it, then the plan, PR description and commit messages, and asks until it knows. The narrative opens with the intent, quoted from the ticket when there is one, then three to five entry points to open first, then one block per concern that leads with the mechanism and links the exact places, and ends with docs and other small enablers. Every file reference is clickable. On each block it suggests one to three moves, answers your questions with references, and rewrites a block in another shape if you ask, remembering that for later blocks. When you finish a block it shows the next one, checks the finished one off, and asks whether to commit if the tree is dirty. A background subagent writes the files when one is available. At the end it guesses the follow-through, such as merging the PR, and asks before doing it.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/bmad-code-org/bmad-method/tree/e734d3ac3c0f4ea31cc2c2bbbe79e86e54f2cae6/skills/bmad-walkthrough"
        },
