          "text": "Lavish Editor is a local page in your browser for reviewing HTML that an agent wrote. Instead of describing a plan, comparison, diagram, table, code diff, report or prototype in prose, the agent builds it as an HTML file and opens it with the lavish-axi CLI, run through npx. You annotate the page and send feedback; the agent answers through the CLI's reply command. The skill itself holds almost no instructions. It tells the agent to read the CLI's help for its commands and the review-loop workflow, lavish-axi design for design direction and current snippets, and lavish-axi playbook for guidance on a given kind of artifact, so what it does follows the CLI's current version. Called as /lavish with a request, it builds that artifact; called with nothing, or picked up by the agent on its own, it works out what to show from the conversation.",
