              "text": "That one outputs editable PowerPoint files; this one makes static HTML, CSS and JavaScript with no build step"
            }
          ],
          "text": "html-ppt is a kit for slide decks as plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript, with no build step. Before writing anything, the agent confirms the content, audience and length, recommends two or three of its 36 themes by tone, and points to the closest of 15 full-deck templates, such as pitch-deck, product-launch, tech-sharing, weekly-report or a 3:4 Xiaohongshu post. A script scaffolds the deck so asset paths resolve; slides are copied from 36 layouts and filled in, with colors from theme tokens, images in frames that crop or letterbox, a logo declared once, and any of 27 CSS entry animations and 20 canvas effects such as confetti or a force-directed graph. Text meant for the presenter goes in notes, never on the slide. Decks run with arrow keys or swipes, T cycles themes, O shows an overview, and S opens a presenter window of draggable cards for the current and next slide, the script and a timer, kept in sync with the audience view. For a talk, it uses the presenter-mode template and writes a speaker script for every slide. A headless Chrome script exports slides to PNG.",
