          "text": "agent-device is a CLI for driving apps on Apple platforms, Android devices including Android TV and Fire TV, and Amazon Vega OS TV apps. The skill keeps the agent from wasting turns: it starts straight away with agent-device open, which returns an interactive snapshot of the screen whose elements carry refs such as @e12. It then loops: press, fill, scroll or go back with --settle, continue from the printed diff, confirm the expected text or state, and close the session, shutting down any simulator it booted unless you want it kept. It reaches an off-screen element with one scroll --until rather than scrolling and checking, copies refs exactly, and prefers refs and id, label or role selectors to coordinates. When the snapshot is sparse, it takes a screenshot, works from coordinates and snapshots again later. Error output carries fixes, which it follows instead of re-planning, and agent-device help covers specialized work such as gestures, scripting, TVs, macOS, remote devices and debugging.",
