      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Keeps AI writing patterns out of prose: filler, adverbs, formulaic contrasts, passive voice, em dashes and pull-quote lines.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The agent is drafting, editing or reviewing prose and you don't want it to read as AI-written"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Applies eight rules, such as cutting filler and every adverb, active voice with a human subject, no \"not X, it's Y\" contrasts and no em dashes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Checks",
              "text": "Each draft before delivery against a list of tells, and can score it 1–10 on five dimensions, revising anything under 35 of 50"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike unslop",
              "text": "You call that one to rewrite a finished text; this one is a rule set the agent applies whenever it writes or edits prose"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Stop Slop is a short rule set for prose that doesn't read as generated. Its eight rules: cut filler phrases and all adverbs; break formulaic structures such as binary contrasts, negative lists, dramatic fragments and rhetorical setups; use active voice with a human subject, never an inanimate thing doing a human action; name the specific thing instead of a vague declarative; put the reader in the room, with \"you\" over \"people\"; vary sentence length and paragraph endings, prefer two items to three and use no em dashes; state facts without softening; and rewrite anything that sounds like a pull-quote. Before delivering, the agent runs a checklist of the same tells, plus sentences that open with a Wh- word and meta-joiners such as \"the rest of this essay\". A score from 1 to 10 on directness, rhythm, trust, authenticity and density sends anything under 35 of 50 back for revision. Lists of phrases and structures to cut, and before-and-after examples, are in its reference files.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/hardikpandya/stop-slop/tree/8da1f030185bdfe8471220585162991eaeb970e9"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:writing",
          "type:guidelines",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "anti-slop",
          "writing"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
