          "text": "SVG is the main output; PNG, a single offline HTML page with pan, zoom and downloads, and GIF animation are made from it. For eleven of its twelve styles the agent writes a JSON description that a bundled script validates and renders; Style 8, Dark Luxury, is written as SVG directly. A check command looks at marker references, overlaps, geometry and composition, and a strict text mode makes sure every label shows in full. The agent then views the PNG at reading size, if it can view images, for missing text, contrast, spacing, clipping, arrow direction and crossings, and repairs failures by element ID, changing approach after two unchanged failures. It widens or splits a crowded diagram rather than shrinking the text. GIF motion works on the supported diagram layouts, at 960px and 20fps by default. Styles 9 to 12 check facts before layout and don't invent responsibilities, protocols or metrics. It ends by reporting file paths, dimensions, the visual review and remaining limits, and never publishes or sends a diagram without separate permission.",
