              "text": "Node.js with bun, pnpm, yarn or npm"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Its rule is that screenshots are advertisements: each slide sells one moment, outcome or solved pain instead of documenting the UI. The agent doesn't write the page by hand; it copies a bundled Next.js and shadcn template, drops your captures into the folders it expects, optionally seeds your app name, headlines and theme, and gives you the local URL. In the editor you reorder slides, edit text in place, switch layouts and themes, and place phones or captions across neighbouring slides on one connected canvas, which export as matching crops. You pick one of 18 named styles or describe your own. For copy, the agent draws on a headline library: three options per slide, the chosen one rewritten in that style's voice. It rewrites rather than translates for each market. A final check covers message, visuals and exports, including reading each slide at search-result size. It offers to migrate an older project made by this skill in place, backing files up first. For an iOS Swift app with no screenshots yet, it suggests a companion capture skill. It never uploads or submits anything to the stores, and its hand-off ends with a link to the author's showcase.",
