      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Copies anti-slop's Oxlint rules into your repository, installs matching Oxlint packages and enables every rule, or updates an existing copy without losing local changes.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want lint rules in a TypeScript or JavaScript repo that catch patterns such as chained type assertions, unknown parameters and filter-then-map chains"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Copies the bundled plugin to tools/oxlint/anti-slop/, installs @oxlint/plugins at exactly your Oxlint version, merges the config and enables every rule at error"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The rules as code your repository owns, plus an UPSTREAM.md recording where they came from and what you changed"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also",
              "text": "Rules for the Effect library when the repo depends on Effect directly, and an update path that keeps your local customizations"
            },
            {
              "label": "Then",
              "text": "Runs your lint and typecheck and reports findings; it fixes them only if you asked for a cleanup"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js, to run its install script, and your repo's own package manager"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Anti-slop is meant to be vendored: the plugin's source is copied into your repository, which from then on owns its rules, tests and configuration. For a fresh install the agent reads the repo's instructions and git status, finds the package manager and the Oxlint or Vite+ setup, and runs the bundled install script, which refuses to overwrite an existing copy. It installs @oxlint/plugins at exactly your Oxlint version, or the same current version of both, without touching unrelated dependencies. It merges the plugin into oxlint.config.ts, .oxlintrc.json or the Vite+ config, adds ignores for agent folders such as .claude and .cursor so installed skills aren't linted, and turns on all its rules, plus Oxlint's own no-accumulating-spread, at error. Then it runs lint and typecheck, and never silences a rule, lowers its severity or adds unsafe casts to make lint pass. Existing installations follow a separate update procedure instead. It ends by recording provenance and reporting the installed path, source, dependency and configuration changes, and check results.",
