              "text": "Distributing components through npm, shadcn-style registries and marketplaces"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The skill is an index to components.build, an open specification for building UI components for the web, split into fifteen reference files. Its definitions separate primitives, unstyled building blocks that handle behaviour and accessibility such as Radix or React Aria, from styled components, blocks and templates. Its principles favour composition over inheritance, accessibility as a baseline with semantic HTML, ARIA and keyboard support, styles that can be overridden through tokens or class names, few dependencies, and code users can read and change, the idea behind copy-and-paste distribution. Other files cover patterns such as as-child, polymorphism, slots and controlled state, plus publishing and documenting components. Its terms are framework-agnostic, with React for examples. It holds guidance only and changes nothing by itself.",
