          "text": "A reference the agent applies while it builds charts, from the data plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. A table matches thirteen kinds of question to a best chart and its alternatives: trends get lines, rankings horizontal bars, part-to-whole stacked bars or treemaps, flows Sankey diagrams. It warns against pie, donut, 3D and dual-axis charts. Code patterns set a clean house style and cover line, bar, histogram with mean and median, heatmap and small-multiple charts, number formatting such as $1.2M, and interactive plotly charts saved as HTML. Its design rules: color encodes data rather than decorating, one bright accent marks the key point against grey, blue and orange replace red and green, categories are sorted by value, panels share scales, and uncertainty is shown. An accessibility checklist runs before sharing: the chart works without color, text is readable, axes carry units, and the source and date range are noted, with alt text and a data table for screen readers.",
