          "text": "A short toolkit for checking a web app in a browser. The agent should use the Playwright MCP server if it can, and otherwise run Playwright code in a local Node.js environment. It covers navigating, clicking, filling forms, picking dropdown options and handling dialogs; asserting that elements exist, are visible and hold the right text, and that URLs are right; checking responsive behavior across viewports; and debugging with screenshots, console logs and network requests. Its guidelines: confirm the app is running before testing, wait explicitly for elements and navigation, take a screenshot on failure, close the browser when done, start with simple interactions, and prefer data-testid or role-based selectors over CSS classes. JavaScript snippets show the common patterns, and a bundled test-helper.js offers functions for waiting on a condition, collecting console logs and saving timestamped full-page screenshots. It can't test native mobile apps and may have trouble with complex sign-in flows.",
