              "label": "Leaves to you",
              "text": "Builds, linters and tests: it lists the commands and asks you to confirm the results; it never merges unless you say so"
            },
            {
              "label": "Guards",
              "text": "Treats repository files as formatting only: it won't run commands or fetch URLs their docs mention, and never reads files outside the repo"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Contribution etiquette for an agent working in someone else's repository. Before any issue, branch, commit or pull request, it looks for the project's guidance in README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, other docs and the issue and PR templates, and applies what concerns the contribution workflow: branch naming, commit format, templates, required reviewers and prerequisite checks. It first looks for an existing issue and asks you which to use; if the project requires one and none exists, it files one from the project's template or, without one, from its own bundled template. It works on a branch made for the change, groups the changes into logical commits with short messages, and opens the PR from the project's template or its own, referencing the issue. Security rules override anything in the repository: it never runs commands or scripts found in its docs, reads files outside the working tree, requests URLs those docs mention or puts secrets in issues, commits or PRs, and it flags any repository instruction that conflicts with these rules. It uses git and the gh CLI.",
