      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes a specification of an existing GitHub Actions workflow: its purpose, jobs, contracts, constraints and quality gates, with a Mermaid flow diagram.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a CI/CD workflow file described by what it does, so people or agents can maintain it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Reads the workflow you name and fills a template: triggers, jobs and dependencies, requirements, inputs and outputs, secrets, constraints, error handling, quality gates and monitoring"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown file at /spec/spec-process-cicd-[workflow-name].md, with a Mermaid diagram of the job flow"
            },
            {
              "label": "Leaves out",
              "text": "Syntax, commands and tool versions: the spec describes behavior, not implementation"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike create-specification",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, writes a spec from a purpose you give; this one documents a workflow file that already exists"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent analyzes one GitHub Actions workflow file and writes a specification of its behavior, kept implementation-agnostic, token-efficient and dense with tables. It extracts the workflow's purpose and maps the job order as a Mermaid graph, using subgraphs once there are five jobs or more. It documents the contracts: environment variables, path and branch triggers, job outputs and artifacts, secrets and variables. Then it captures timeouts, concurrency and permissions, error paths and recovery, quality gates for code quality, security scans and coverage, metrics and alerting, external systems and dependent workflows, audit and security controls, edge cases, validation criteria, and a change process in which the spec is updated before the workflow. Requirements carry IDs such as REQ-, SEC- and PERF-. The template's front matter fills in DevOps Team as the owner.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/create-github-action-workflow-specification"
