      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews a prompt for safety, bias, security and effectiveness, scores it, then rewrites it and proposes tests for the improved version.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've written a prompt, such as a system prompt or reusable template, and want it checked for harm, bias, injection risk and clarity"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Rates harmful-content, privacy and security risk and five kinds of bias, and scores clarity, robustness and token efficiency from 1 to 5"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Prompt Analysis Report, a complete improved prompt with each change explained, test, edge-case, safety and bias cases, and usage guidelines"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also adds",
              "text": "An educational section on the prompt-engineering principles applied and the pitfalls avoided"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A structured review for prompts written for AI systems. The agent classifies the prompt's task, complexity and domain, then works through eight lenses: harmful content, violence, misinformation and illegal activity; gender, racial, cultural, socioeconomic and ability bias; data exposure, prompt injection, information leakage and access control; effectiveness; best-practice compliance; the prompt pattern used (zero-shot, few-shot, chain-of-thought, role-based or hybrid) and whether another would work better; technical robustness; and performance, such as token efficiency and consistency across runs. Risks are rated low to high and other areas scored 1 to 5, each with an explanation, followed by the three most critical issues and three strengths. It then writes a complete improved prompt, lists what it strengthened for safety, bias, security and clarity, and proposes test cases, including edge-case, safety and bias tests. Safety comes before functionality throughout. The SKILL.md also tells the agent to follow a separate AI Prompt Engineering & Safety Best Practices instruction, which it doesn't include.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/ai-prompt-engineering-safety-review"
