          "text": "A short pattern guide for generate, evaluate, critique and refine loops. In basic reflection the model critiques its own output against your criteria as JSON pass/fail verdicts and refines until everything passes or it runs out of iterations. The evaluator-optimizer pattern splits generation, evaluation and optimization into separate steps, looping until an overall score clears a threshold, 0.8 in the example. Code-specific reflection writes code and pytest tests, runs them and feeds failures back until they pass. For judging it offers outcome checks against an expected result, an LLM comparing two outputs, and weighted rubrics such as accuracy 0.4, clarity 0.3 and completeness 0.3. Its best practices: define measurable criteria up front, cap iterations at three to five, stop when scores stop improving, log every iteration, use structured JSON for results and handle parse failures gracefully.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/agentic-eval"
        },
