      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes an architectural decision record to /docs/adr/, with context, the decision, positive and negative consequences, rejected alternatives and implementation notes.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've made, or are proposing, an architecture decision and want it recorded in a standard format"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Takes the title, context, decision, alternatives and stakeholders from you or the conversation, asks for anything missing, and fills a fixed ADR template"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "/docs/adr/adr-NNNN-title-slug.md, numbered after the last ADR, with status Proposed and coded items such as POS-001, NEG-001 and ALT-001"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An ADR, or architectural decision record, is a short document that captures one design decision: why it was needed, what was chosen and what it costs. This command writes one in a fixed format meant for both people and AI tools to read. It needs five inputs, a title, the context, the decision, the alternatives and the stakeholders, and asks you for any it can't find in the conversation before writing. The file goes in /docs/adr/ as adr-NNNN-title-slug.md, where NNNN is the next four-digit number. Its front matter holds the title, status, date, authors, tags and supersedes and superseded_by links. The body has the status (Proposed, Accepted, Rejected, Superseded or Deprecated, starting at Proposed), the context, the decision with its rationale, positive and negative consequences, each alternative with the reason it was rejected, implementation notes on rollout and monitoring, and references. Multi-item sections use coded bullets such as POS-001 or IMP-002.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/create-architectural-decision-record"
