      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns a meeting transcript or notes into concise minutes, with decisions and action items that each carry an owner and due date.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a transcript, recording or raw notes from an internal meeting of an hour or less and need the record written up"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks up to three questions about missing details, then fills a fixed 12-section schema, with decisions and action items right after the summary"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Minutes of one or two pages, every action item with an owner, due date and acceptance criteria, and unknowns marked TBD"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also suggests",
              "text": "Sending the draft to the organizer for review within 24 hours, then publishing it, and optionally creating tasks in your tracker"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A template-driven note-taker for short internal meetings such as standups, syncs, design reviews and triage. Before drafting it needs the title, date, time or duration and organizer, whether there's an agenda, transcript or recording, and who reviews the minutes; it asks up to three questions for what's missing, and with no transcript or agenda it marks the source as ad-hoc notes. The minutes follow a strict schema: metadata with ISO 8601 dates and UTC times, attendance, agenda, a summary of one to three sentences, decisions with who decided and why, action items with owner, due date, acceptance criteria and linked tickets, notes per agenda item, a parking lot for unresolved items, risks, the next meeting, references and a version log. It keeps opinion apart from fact, labels anything uncertain TBD rather than guessing, and leaves out personal data unless needed and authorized. A shorter template is included for quick minutes, and action items are written to convert easily into GitHub Issues or Jira tasks.",
