      "id": "github/awesome-copilot/skills/devops-rollout-plan",
      "name": "devops-rollout-plan",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/github/awesome-copilot/devops-rollout-plan",
        "installs": 9700,
        "weeklyInstalls": [22, 32, 27, 16, 9, 13, 16, 10],
        "firstSeen": "2026-02-25"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes a production rollout plan for an infrastructure or application change: preflight checks, deployment steps, verification signals, rollback, communications and contingencies.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're about to ship an infrastructure, application, configuration or data change and want a written plan for doing it safely"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Gathers what's changing, the environment, constraints and risks, then fills a ten-section rollout template"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A plan with go/no-go checks, step commands with validation and timings, timed verification signals, rollback criteria and steps, and a stakeholder communication schedule"
            },
            {
              "label": "Scales",
              "text": "Down for low-risk or staging changes, and up with extra gates for high-risk production ones"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A planning template for change management. Before writing, the agent needs the change and its from-to versions, the target environment and infrastructure type such as Kubernetes, VMs or serverless, affected services, downtime and change windows, approvals and compliance needs, and the risks: blast radius, data migrations and how hard rollback would be. The plan then covers an executive summary with risk level and expected downtime; prerequisites, approvals and backups; preflight health checks with a go/no-go checklist; the rollout in phases, with specific commands, validation after each step and duration estimates; verification signals at 0-2, 2-5, 5-15 and 15+ minutes; rollback criteria, steps and checks; a communication plan from 24 hours before, with a stakeholder matrix; post-deployment tasks; contingency plans for partial failure, degraded performance, data inconsistency and dependency failure; and on-call contacts and escalation. Its closing rules include always having a tested rollback, monitoring metrics and not only logs, and never deploying on a Friday afternoon unless critical.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/devops-rollout-plan"
        },
