          "text": "A four-step generator. It first checks the spec for completeness and correctness, lists every endpoint, method, schema and security scheme, and flags ambiguous or incomplete definitions. It then plans the folders, groups controllers or handlers by resource or domain, and lays out the service layer, data models and configuration. Code generation follows: build configuration such as pom.xml, build.gradle or package.json, models from the spec's schemas, handlers with route mappings, services for the business logic, a repository layer where one applies, and startup code, with authentication taken from the spec. Last come unit tests for services and controllers, example requests or integration tests, API documentation and a README with setup and run instructions. If the spec leaves out the project name, framework, naming conventions or auth method, it asks for them. It ends by listing the next steps: review the code, install dependencies, configure environment variables and database connections, run the tests and start the server.",
