          "text": "A short command for turning a plan into tracked work. You point it at a plan file, and it splits the plan into its phases, one issue each. Before creating anything it searches the repository's issues with search_issues, so a phase that already has an issue gets that issue updated with update_issue instead of a duplicate; new ones go through create_issue. Each issue takes the phase name as its title and the phase's details, requirements and context as its description, limited to the changes the plan requires, with labels that fit a feature or a chore. It uses the feature_request.yml or chore_request.yml issue template when the repository has one, and the default template otherwise.",
