      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes a feature's test strategy, test issue checklist and QA plan, applying ISTQB test design techniques and the ISO 25010 quality model.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A feature's PRD, implementation plan and project plan exist and you want its testing planned, with the test issues listed for you to create"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Picks test design techniques, ranks the ISO 25010 quality characteristics, sets coverage targets, quality gates and labels, and estimates test tasks"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "test-strategy.md, test-issues-checklist.md and qa-plan.md in /docs/ways-of-work/plan/{epic-name}/{feature-name}/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Terms",
              "text": "ISTQB is the international software-testing qualifications board's framework of test techniques; ISO 25010 is a standard list of eight software quality characteristics"
            },
            {
              "label": "Defaults",
              "text": "Over 80% line and 90% branch coverage on critical paths, Playwright for end-to-end tests, story-point ranges per test type"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Acting as a QA engineer and test architect, it reads the feature PRD, a technical breakdown, the implementation plan and the project plan breakdown-plan writes, and produces three files. Like breakdown-plan, it looks for the PRD at {feature-name}.md, not the prd.md breakdown-feature-prd writes, and for a technical-breakdown.md no step writes. The test strategy sets scope, quality objectives and risks, chooses among equivalence partitioning, boundary value analysis, decision tables, state transitions and exploratory testing, covers functional, non-functional, structural and regression testing, ranks the eight ISO 25010 characteristics from functional suitability to portability, and plans environments, test data, tools and CI. The test issues checklist lists the issues to create, from unit and integration tests to Playwright end-to-end, performance, security, accessibility and regression tests, with dependencies, coverage targets and story-point estimates per test type. The QA plan defines entry and exit criteria, issue template, labeling and priority standards, dependency checks and estimate reviews. Issue templates for a test strategy, Playwright tests and quality assurance come with it, along with success metrics such as catching over 95% of defects before production.",
