      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes an Epic product requirements document from your idea: problem, personas, user journeys, requirements, success metrics, out-of-scope items and business value.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a high-level idea for an epic and want it written up as a product requirements document before any architecture or code"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown PRD saved at /docs/ways-of-work/plan/{epic-name}/epic.md"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Plays a SaaS product manager, asks clarifying questions when details are missing, and fills an eight-section template"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike prd",
              "text": "That one interviews you for a five-section feature PRD; this one works at epic level and starts the breakdown chain"
            },
            {
              "label": "Next step",
              "text": "breakdown-epic-arch turns the PRD into a technical architecture spec"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The first step of the repo's breakdown workflow, which takes a product idea from epic down to tests. The agent acts as the product manager of a large SaaS platform: it reads your epic idea and, optionally, who it's for, asks clarifying questions if something is missing, and writes a PRD in eight sections. They are the epic's name; its goal, as the problem in three to five sentences, the solution and the expected impact on metrics; user personas; high-level user journeys; functional and non-functional business requirements; KPIs; what's out of scope; and a business value of high, medium or low with a justification. The file goes in a folder named after the epic, which the later breakdown skills write into: breakdown-epic-arch puts arch.md next to it, and breakdown-feature-prd writes each feature's PRD in a subfolder.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/breakdown-epic-pm"
