          ],
          "text": "A parameterized prompt: variables at the top decide which sections the agent writes. It scans files such as package.json, .csproj and pom.xml, build scripts and pipeline definitions to identify languages, frameworks and dependencies, with exact versions and licenses if you ask for them. For each stack it finds, it documents the specifics, such as NuGet packages and dependency injection for .NET, Spring Boot setup for Java, hooks and state management for React, or the web framework and ORM for Python. Optional sections cover naming and code-organization conventions; example code from the project for endpoints, data access, services and UI components; a technology map of integration points, tooling and infrastructure; diagrams of how the stack fits together; and, at the Implementation-Ready depth, file templates, snippets and a checklist for building new features. It ends with the apparent reasons behind technology choices, legacy parts marked for replacement and upgrade paths.",
