          "text": "A parameterized prompt for GitHub Copilot's repository instructions. You set the project type or auto-detect, architecture style, quality focus, documentation level, testing approach and versioning scheme. The agent first analyzes the codebase: exact language, framework and library versions from project files, folder structure and layer boundaries, naming, error handling, documentation and testing patterns, and the performance, security and accessibility practices in use. It then writes a copilot-instructions.md that tells Copilot to respect those versions, read architecture, tech-stack, coding-standards, folder-structure and exemplars files in .github/copilot if they exist, copy patterns from similar files, prefer newer or better-tested files when patterns conflict, and never introduce a pattern the codebase doesn't already have. Sections on quality, documentation, testing, versioning and guidelines for .NET, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Angular and Python appear according to your settings. Its rule throughout: only what's observed in the code, with consistency over outside best practices.",
