      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Converts a plain-text document into a Markdown copy beside it, guided by your instructions, an earlier converted file or preset options.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have documentation in plain text, such as a file with no extension, and want it as proper Markdown"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Copies the file to file.md unless one exists, then adds headings, lists and code blocks without changing the content"
            },
            {
              "label": "Options",
              "text": "Finalize to tidy spacing and indentation, a guide file to imitate, header levels, a pattern to apply, a stop line and a target platform such as GitLab"
            },
            {
              "label": "Presets",
              "text": "rm-head-digits strips numbers from headings, mv-head-level(x, y) moves headings from level x to level y, rm-indent(x) reduces indentation by x"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A conversion command with many switches. You point it at a plain-text documentation file: if file.md already exists it converts that, otherwise it copies the original to file.md and works on the copy. It can follow your written instructions, a preset, or a previously converted Markdown file, whose plain-text original it compares to learn the pattern. Options add headings at a given level, apply a pattern from your selection across the whole file, stop at a line number or the end of the file, and target GitHub (the default), GitLab, StackOverflow, VS Code or plain CommonMark. Saying finalize, or something like \"polish the converted file\", runs a cleanup pass that trims stray spaces and indentation, escapes HTML, fixes nested lists and labels code blocks with their language. When options are unclear it fetches Markdown references from GitHub, markdownguide.org and Microsoft, and it doesn't change the document's data unless told to.",
