          "text": "A scaffold for a new repository's Copilot setup. The agent asks for the primary language and framework, project type, other technologies, how strict your standards are, and whether you use GitHub Actions. Its mandatory first step is fetching awesome-copilot's lists of instructions, agents and skills to find ones matching your stack; it adapts those with a Based on or Inspired by comment linking the source, and writes simple guidelines of its own only where nothing fits. It creates .github/copilot-instructions.md with the project overview, stack, conventions and workflow; instruction files for the language, testing, documentation, security, performance and code review, holding principles and no code; skills for creating components, writing tests, reviewing, refactoring, docs and debugging; software-engineer, architect, reviewer and debugger agents; and, with Actions, a minimal copilot-setup-steps.yml for the Coding Agent, whose job must have that exact name. It checks every file's front matter, then explains how to enable and use the setup in VS Code.",
