          "text": "The skill is a configurable prompt. You set the migration type (framework version, architecture refactoring, technology migration, dependencies update or pattern changes), the before and after references, the scope, the main focus, an automation level from conservative to aggressive, and whether to generate examples and require validation. The agent compares the two states: moved, renamed or deleted files, configuration and dependency changes, and the code transformations typical of that migration type, then builds a before-and-after correspondence matrix. It writes the result to .github/copilot-migration-instructions.md: mandatory transformations, ones that need validation, an API correspondence table, new patterns to adopt and obsolete ones to avoid, examples per file type, checks to run after each change, situations for a person to decide, and metrics to track. A last phase applies the instructions to test code and adjusts the rules from the results. Its examples include Angular 14 to 17, .NET Framework to .NET Core, jQuery to React and monolith to microservices.",
