          "text": "A skill for retro computing and electronics hobby projects. The agent draws circuit layouts with HTML5 Canvas, each component an object with a grid position, size, rotation and properties, each wire a start, an end and a color. It follows set recipes: an LED circuit starts with the power rails, then the LED with its orientation, its current-limiting resistor and the wires; a 6502 layout centres the W65C02S, adds the EEPROM, the VIA and 7400-series address decoding, then wires the address bus, the data bus and the control signals, with a reset button and a clock crystal. Wires follow a color code: red for power, black for ground, yellow for clock, blue for address, green for data and orange for control. Two worked builds, a single LED and a 555 astable blinker, give exact steps. Pinout tables for the main chips and electronics formulas sit in the SKILL.md, with longer specifications in the bundled reference files.",
