      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Maps the resources of an Azure resource group and how they connect, and writes a Markdown file with a detailed Mermaid architecture diagram.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to see how the resources in one of your Azure resource groups fit together"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Lists your resource groups for you to pick, unless you named one, queries every resource's settings, network, identity and dependencies, and maps their connections"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "[resource-group]-architecture.md with a summary, a resource inventory table, the Mermaid diagram and notes on connections and issues"
            },
            {
              "label": "Reads only",
              "text": "It never modifies or deletes Azure resources"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The Azure MCP server or the az CLI, signed in to your subscription"
            }
          ],
          "text": "If you didn't name a resource group, the agent lists the available ones with their locations and waits for your choice. It queries every resource in the group with Azure MCP tools or az, noting type, SKU or tier, region, key settings, networking and managed identities, then maps relationships: VNet peering, subnets and NSG rules, private endpoints, data flows such as an app calling a database or a function using storage, identities reaching Key Vault, and settings that point to other resources. The Mermaid diagram groups resources into subgraphs by layer, such as network, compute, data and security, puts SKUs and address ranges in node labels, and labels every connection, with distinct arrows for optional and critical paths. The Markdown file follows a bundled template and goes in the workspace root, or docs/ if it exists. Groups of over 50 resources may be split into several diagrams by layer, and dependencies on other resource groups are noted.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/azure-resource-visualizer"
