      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Updates your repository's existing llms.txt to match its current docs and structure, following the llmstxt.org format.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Your repo already has an llms.txt and its docs, specs or structure have changed since it was written"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Compares the file's links with the repo, finds new, moved and removed docs, plans the changes, then edits the file"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An updated llms.txt: an H1 name, a blockquote summary and H2 sections of links with short descriptions, all valid relative paths"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike create-llms",
              "text": "That one writes an llms.txt from scratch; this one edits the one you have"
            }
          ],
          "text": "llms.txt is a file at a repository's root that tells language models where to find the content that explains the project, in a format set at llmstxt.org. The agent reads the existing file and the specification, examines the repository, and compares the two: new READMEs, docs, specs, configuration and examples to add, removed or relocated files to update or drop. It plans the changes, then edits the file, keeping the required structure: the project name as an H1, an optional blockquote summary, context paragraphs without headings, and H2 sections such as Documentation, Specifications, Examples and Configuration, each a list of links written as [name](relative-url): description. An Optional section holds secondary files that can be skipped for a shorter context. It leaves out implementation details, build artifacts and redundant files, and checks the format and every link before it's done.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/update-llms"
        },
