      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Researches a feature and saves a plan of one pull request split into testable commits, then pauses for your feedback before any code.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a feature planned as a single pull request before the agent writes any code"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Researches related code, docs and dependencies, in a subagent when it can, then splits the work into one commit or several testable ones"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "plans/{feature-name}/plan.md: a branch name, the goal, and for each step its files, the change and how to test it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Then",
              "text": "It asks about every [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] marker and pauses; your feedback sends it back to research and revise"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent acts as a planner and writes no code. It first gathers context: related features and patterns in the codebase, existing docs and architecture decisions, and the external APIs or libraries involved, reading their documentation first, through Context7 if available, and stopping once it's about 80% sure it can split the feature into testable steps. It hands this research to a subagent when it can, and otherwise does it itself. It assumes the whole feature lands as one pull request on its own branch: a simple feature becomes a single commit, a complex one several commits that each leave a testable step. The draft goes to plans/{feature-name}/plan.md, with [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] wherever it needs your input; it asks those questions and waits. Feedback sends it back through research and a revised plan. Its research guide was adapted from a specific project and still mentions ResizeMe and Windows APIs.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/structured-autonomy-plan"
