      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes a tldr-pages entry for a command from its upstream documentation: a one-line summary and its 5 to 8 most common examples.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a tldr page for a command-line tool, in the tldr-pages project's format"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Fetches the documentation URL you give, picks the most common uses and formats them in tldr's template"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown page with the command name, a short description, a link to the upstream docs and 5 to 8 examples"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A command name and a documentation URL; it asks for a missing URL, and confirms a command it had to guess"
            },
            {
              "label": "Strict on",
              "text": "tldr's placeholder rules, such as {{[-m|--message]}} {{message_text}} for an option and its argument"
            }
          ],
          "text": "tldr pages, from the tldr-pages project, are short command references made of examples. You call it as /create-tldr-page with a documentation URL and a command name; given a file instead of a URL, it uses the file's URL for that command, asking which one if there are several. It requires an authoritative upstream source and suggests acceptable URL patterns when you leave it out. The page follows tldr's template: the exact lowercase command name as the title, a one-line description, a note on subcommands with their own pages when relevant, a More information link, and 5 to 8 examples ordered by how often they're used. User-provided values go in {{placeholders}}, options are wrapped with their short and long forms, such as {{[-A|--all]}}, while subcommands and lone short flags aren't. Passing --help or --tldr makes it summarize itself in tldr format instead of writing a page.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/create-tldr-page"
