          "text": "It translates a whole MkDocs documentation set in one go. After you give the target language and its locale code, such as es or pt-BR, it creates a git branch named docs-translation-<language>, lists every file under docs/docs/en and docs/docs/includes/en, and translates them in order into folders named after the locale. It mirrors the English folder structure and keeps file names, headings, code blocks, metadata and links intact. Include references switch to the new locale, and mkdocs.yml gets a new locale entry under the i18n plugin with translated nav_translations and admonition_translations. It prefers standard industry terms, checks off each file as it goes and carries on without asking for confirmation, then compares the number of translated and source files and resumes if any are missing. It ignores Markdown linting problems rather than mentioning them, and ends every translated file with a line crediting GitHub Copilot and GPT-4o.",
