      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Questions you about a task's scope, deliverables and constraints until you have nothing to add, then shows a plan and does the task.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want the agent to pin a task down with you before it starts working"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks about scope, deliverables, success criteria and requirements, explores the project, and keeps asking until you have nothing to add"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A short plan and a todo list, then the agent carries out the task"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "VS Code with the Joyride extension, whose joyride_request_human_input tool it asks through"
            }
          ],
          "text": "first-ask makes the agent refine a task with you before doing it. It asks specific questions through joyride_request_human_input, a tool of the Joyride extension for VS Code: what the task covers and aims for, what it should deliver, how success is judged, and its technical and procedural requirements. Between questions it explores the project with its other tools, researches on the web when something calls for it, and organizes the task into sections or steps, keeping its understanding as simple as it can. Before starting, it asks whether you have anything more to add and keeps refining until you don't. Then it shows you its plan with little repetition, writes a todo list and gets to work. Unlike a planning skill that stops at a document, it goes on to do the task itself once the questions are answered.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/first-ask"
