              "text": "GitHub Copilot: it calls tools by name, such as #fetch, githubRepo, #runInTerminal and #todos"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Custom agents are GitHub Copilot's .agent.md files, each with a description and a list of tools in its front matter. This one fetches the list in github/awesome-copilot's README.agents.md, reads the description of each agent in your .github/agents/, and fetches the catalog's copy of each to see whether yours is current or how its description, tools or content differ. It weighs the catalog against your repo's languages, frameworks, project type and documentation needs, such as READMEs, specs and ADRs, and what you have discussed in chat, and leaves out agents that duplicate yours. You get one table with links, descriptions, status, any similar local agent and a reason for each suggestion, and nothing beyond it. It then waits for you to choose: new agents are downloaded and outdated ones replaced with the catalog's version, without editing them.",
