          "text": "Instruction files are GitHub Copilot's .instructions.md files, which apply to the files matched by the applyTo pattern in their front matter. This one fetches the list in github/awesome-copilot's README.instructions.md, reads the description and applyTo pattern of each instruction file in your .github/instructions/, and fetches the catalog's copy of each to see whether yours is current or how its description, pattern or content differ. It weighs the catalog against your repo's languages, frameworks, project type and workflow, such as testing, CI/CD and deployment, and what you have discussed in chat, and leaves out files that duplicate yours. You get one table with links, descriptions, status, any similar local file and a reason for each suggestion, and nothing beyond it. It then waits for you to choose: new files are downloaded and outdated ones replaced with the catalog's version, without editing them.",
