      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Carries out an implementation plan exactly as written, one step at a time, checking off items and stopping where the plan says to.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have the implementation file structured-autonomy-generate wrote and want it built without extras"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Picks up the next unchecked step, writes only the code the plan specifies, checks items off and runs the plan's build or test commands"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "That step's changes and an updated plan, then control back at the plan's STOP marker"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A plan passed in; without one it replies \"Implementation plan is required.\""
            }
          ],
          "text": "The last of the three Structured Autonomy skills. It acts as an implementation agent that must not deviate from the plan you give it. It starts at the next unchecked step, completes every item of that step without skipping any, and writes no code the plan doesn't specify. As it goes it checks items off in the plan document itself with Markdown checkboxes, then checks its work with the build or test commands the plan names. When it reaches the plan's STOP instruction it stops and hands control back to you, so each step can be tested and committed before you call it again for the next.",
