      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds features your project's docs promise but its code lacks, ranks them, and files a specification for each top one as a GitHub issue.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a project's missing features found, prioritized and written up as issues ready to build"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Compares what the README and docs promise with what the code does, lists 5 to 7 gaps, scores them and specifies the top 3"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "GitHub issues, each with scope, technical requirements, an implementation plan, acceptance criteria, dependencies and an effort estimate"
            },
            {
              "label": "Ranks by",
              "text": "(user impact × strategic alignment) ÷ (effort × risk), each rated 1 to 5"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A product-manager workflow for an existing codebase. The agent reads the project's structure, README, docs, entry points, modules and tests, then looks for what the documentation mentions but the code doesn't really implement: placeholder code, thin features and broken steps in the user journey, core functionality first. It lists five to seven gaps with their status, where the docs mention them and what users lose without them, scores each from 1 to 5 on user impact, strategic alignment, feasibility, effort and risk, and keeps the top three. For each it writes an MVP-first specification: scope and exclusions, technical requirements, an implementation plan with simple code examples, and acceptance criteria. Each becomes a GitHub issue with labels, a priority, blocks and blocked-by links and an effort size; large features are split into a parent issue with sub-issues of one to three days' work. It ends with a summary of the specifications, their dependencies and a suggested order to build them in.",
