      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "25eec57919aec2cfd87d4ef9ae5661832302585e",
        "updated": "2026-11-12",
        "skew": 1775
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides building visual novels: a branching script with flags, a typewriter text box, choices, and expected conveniences like save-anywhere, backlog, skip and auto-advance.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The game is mostly reading branching text over character art and backgrounds: a visual novel, dating sim or story-choice game"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sets out the script, text box, characters, backgrounds, choices, story flags, saves, conveniences and audio, with engine-neutral pseudocode"
            },
            {
              "label": "In Ren'Py",
              "text": "It keeps the engine's own save-anywhere, rollback, history, skip and auto-forward, and applies only its design advice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Leaves to others",
              "text": "The branching engine (Ink or Yarn Spinner), UI and saving, to the repo's dialogue-systems, game-ui-ux, engine UI and save-systems skills"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A genre playbook from a game-development collection. The game is the shape of the branching and whether choices feel consequential; the rest is presentation and convenience. Patterns cover a script of lines, choices and flag updates that the engine walks through; a typewriter reveal that a first press completes and a second advances, done by raising the label's visible-character count (the Godot 4.7 and Unity 6.3 calls are named) so words don't jump between lines; and choices that set flags which later lines and endings check. Pitfalls include saving only at checkpoints when players expect to save on any line (Ink restores the exact position, Yarn Spinner only the node), presentation baked into the script, a skip that passes unread text, choices that reconverge at once, branch explosion where branch-and-merge would do, and text hardcoded in one language.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/gamedev-skills/awesome-gamedev-agent-skills/tree/19d93f97c9c1ea0f8b306e77aa81e0d3e352d3e9/skills/genres/visual-novel"
        },
