        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Restructures resumes for software engineering, data, DevOps and technical PM roles: a categorized skills section, bullets with scale and stack, projects and GitHub.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're applying for software engineering, data, DevOps or SRE, or technical product roles"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Rewrites bullets as action, technical work, scale or impact, and the technology used, and groups the skills section by category"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A restructured skills section, improved bullets, projects to highlight, GitHub to-dos and ways to address technical gaps"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike resume-bullet-writer",
              "text": "That one covers any role; this one adds tech metrics such as latency, uptime and requests per second, plus projects and GitHub"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Resume advice for technical roles, written to pass ATS keyword screening and impress technical recruiters. The recommended order puts contact details with GitHub and portfolio links first, then an optional summary, technical skills, experience, projects, education and certifications. Skills can be grouped by category (languages, frameworks, databases, cloud, tools), by proficiency or as a flat list, leaving out Microsoft Office, skill bars and anything touched once. Bullets follow one formula, an action verb plus the technical work, its scale or impact, and the technology used, with metrics such as daily active users, requests per second, latency, uptime and cloud costs; examples cover software, data, DevOps and technical PM roles. Projects matter most for juniors, career changers and bootcamp graduates, and should have real users or depth, not tutorial apps. It also covers education formats for degrees, bootcamps and self-taught engineers, a GitHub profile with pinned repos and READMEs, and claiming only technologies you can discuss in depth in an interview.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/tech-resume-optimizer"
        },
