      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Structures an academic CV for faculty, postdoc, lecturer or research roles, with publications, grants, teaching, mentoring and service formatted to field conventions.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're applying for a faculty, postdoc, lecturer or research scientist position"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Orders the academic sections for the position type and formats each: publications, presentations, grants, teaching, mentoring, service and more"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A CV structure with formatted sections, notes on your field's conventions and a list of items to add or update"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike a resume",
              "text": "It's a complete record, not a selection: 2-4 pages for a graduate student, 15-30 or more for senior faculty"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An academic CV is a full record rather than a selection, and it grows with a career: two to four pages for a graduate student, ten to twenty for mid-career faculty. This skill lays out the standard sections, from contact details with ORCID and education with dissertation, advisor and committee, through appointments, publications, presentations, grants, teaching, mentoring, service and memberships to honors. Research positions lead with publications and grants, teaching positions with teaching, administrative ones with service. Publications can be numbered or grouped by type, with your name in bold, DOIs, and student co-authors marked. Grants list the agency, mechanism, your role, title, dates and amount, including your lab's share. It says what to emphasize for tenure-track, postdoc, lecturer and research scientist roles, and covers the conventions of the sciences (author order matters), the humanities (single-author work and books) and the social sciences.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/academic-cv-builder"
