      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Plans two resumes for creative roles: an ATS-safe version for online applications and a designed one for networking and portfolios, with design specs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You work in design, marketing, writing or another creative field and want your resume to show it without failing ATS screening"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Splits it into two versions and says when to send each: the plain one through portals and job boards, the designed one by email or at interviews"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A strategy with typography, color hex codes and layout specs, portfolio links and content adjustments for your field"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "Graphic and UX designers, marketing and brand roles, writers, and photographers or video makers"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Creative professionals want their resume to show their design skills, but applicant tracking systems (ATS) often fail to read heavily designed ones. This skill's answer is two versions. The ATS-compatible one goes through online portals and job boards and stays creative only through white space, typography, bold and italic, simple dividers, sparing color in the name or headers, and portfolio links, never columns, text boxes, icons or skill bars. The designed one is for networking, direct emails to hiring managers, your portfolio site, interviews and agencies that expect one, and can use two columns, a brand color, icons and a personal logo, as long as information stays easy to find. It gives approaches for graphic designers, UX designers, marketing and brand roles, writers and photographers, ways to link specific case studies from bullets, checklists for typography, layout and color, and tools to use (InDesign, Figma, Canva, Word) or avoid (PowerPoint, random online builders).",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/creative-portfolio-resume"
