        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a negotiation plan for a job offer: market range, total compensation, a counter-offer email or call script, and fallbacks for pushback.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a job offer and want to negotiate it, or a recruiter asks your salary expectations"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Builds a market range (25th to 90th percentile) from sources such as Levels.fyi and Glassdoor, totals the compensation, then plans the counter"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A negotiation strategy: market summary, their offer against your counter with reasons, a script, a Plan B, your walk-away point and questions to clarify"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "Negotiate once the offer is in writing, mention competing offers only if they're real, and get the final terms in writing"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It treats negotiation as expected, since companies budget for it. Research comes first: a market range from sources such as Levels.fyi, Glassdoor, LinkedIn Salary, Blind and public H1B data, what raises or limits your worth, and total compensation as base plus bonus, equity and benefits, with RSUs, options, vesting and refresh grants explained. The counter follows five steps: enthusiasm, your value, a specific ask, the justification, then an open discussion. It has an email template and a call script, and scripts for a low first offer, being asked for your expectations first (deflect, then give a range), a base that won't move (ask for a signing bonus, equity, an earlier review, vacation or a better title instead), competing offers, and questions about your current salary, which it notes are illegal in many states. A timeline runs from the verbal offer to a signed agreement over about ten days. For a fuller comparison of several offers, the repo has offer-comparison-analyzer.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/salary-negotiation-prep"
        },
