      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Organizes your resume versions: a master resume holding every bullet, tailored copies named by role, company and date, and an application tracker.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're applying to many roles and losing track of which resume went to which company"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Lays out a filing system: one master resume holding everything, with each tailored version made from a copy of it rather than by editing the master"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A version summary: the master's status, active versions by role type, an update queue and recommended actions"
            },
            {
              "label": "Suggests",
              "text": "A folder structure, file names like Smith_SWE_Stripe_Feb2024.pdf, and a tracker of version, date, status and notes for each application"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A filing system for job seekers juggling many resumes. The master resume holds everything: every job, every bullet you've written, grouped by focus, summary versions for each role type, all skills, certifications and projects, and the keywords each job covers. Tailored versions start from a copy of it: analyze the posting, pick bullets and a summary, reorder skills, add keywords, trim to length, save under the naming pattern and log it in the tracker. It suggests folders for the master, tailored versions by role, cover letters and an application spreadsheet, and versions by target role, industry or seniority. The master is updated right away after a new job, project, certification or award, and reviewed every quarter. Its rules: never edit the master for an application, no names like resume_final_v2, archive old versions instead of deleting them, and back up to cloud storage.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/resume-version-manager"
