      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reframes your experience for a new industry: finds transferable skills, swaps your field's terms for the target's, and drafts your career-change story.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're switching careers or industries and your experience doesn't map directly to the new role"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Translates your bullets and vocabulary into the target field's, so lesson plans become training curriculum and a platoon becomes a team"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Transferable skills with reasons, reframed bullets, a term translation table, gaps with ways to bridge them, a draft \"why I'm changing\" story and a resume structure"
            },
            {
              "label": "Worked examples",
              "text": "Teachers, military, retail, hospitality and healthcare moving into corporate roles, plus entry points into tech, finance and healthcare"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Career changers compete with people who have direct experience, so this skill rewrites yours in the new field's language. It groups universal transferable skills under leadership, communication, analysis and operations, and gives worked translations with term tables: teacher to corporate trainer, military to corporate, retail to account management, hospitality to customer success, healthcare to tech or pharma. The resume strategy leads with a summary built on transferable skills, uses a functional or hybrid format that groups bullets by skill rather than by job, and adds bridge experience: volunteering, freelance work, certifications, side projects or courses in the target field. It prepares the \"why are you changing?\" answer as discovery, connection, action and vision, and lists reasons not to give, such as burnout or money. For tech, finance and healthcare it names the best entry points and bridge activities, such as customer success from any client-facing role.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/career-changer-translator"
        },
