        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Drafts answers to job application form questions from your CV and the job description, sized to each field and ready to paste.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're answering text fields on Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workday or another applicant tracking system"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Reads the job description, your CV and the exact question, asking for whichever is missing, then answers in the format for that type of question"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Each answer in its own code block, labelled by field, to copy and paste"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "Fill in the form itself; it writes the text you paste"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "Honest years and ratings, every claim tied to a real project, and no trait statements like \"I'm passionate about\""
            }
          ],
          "text": "Despite the name, it writes answers rather than filling in forms: each comes in a plain code block, ready to paste into the field. Its premise is that a form answer isn't a cover letter in a text box: answer what the field asks, then stop. Before writing it reads the job description, your CV and the question, and asks for the CV or job description if you haven't given them. Seven question types get their own format: experience (technology, years, one project), why this company (something specific, linked to real work, under 150 words), portfolio links (most relevant first, live demo before GitHub), technical skills (years plus context, gaps acknowledged, honest ratings), tell us about yourself (current role first, 100-200 words), behavioral questions (condensed STAR without the labels) and opinion questions (commit to a view). A length table runs from one sentence for single-line fields to 300 words, and when in doubt, shorter wins. It warns against repeating the job description, generic traits, apologizing for missing years and padding with irrelevant projects.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/paramchoudhary/resumeskills/tree/74ae19e7c62b0516d1c298328e5544976c12da5d/skills/application-form-filler"
