          "text": "A high-level guide, not a step-by-step workflow. The pipeline runs data ingestion, data validation, feature engineering, training, model validation and deployment as a DAG, a graph of stages that each wait for the ones they depend on. The production workflow has four phases: prepare and version the data, train and track experiments, validate against a baseline and approve, then package, deploy and monitor. Its best practices: make each stage testable on its own and safe to re-run, log metrics at every stage, version data, code and models, validate data with Great Expectations or TFX, version datasets with DVC, keep training and serving infrastructure apart, start with shadow deployments, then canary releases and A/B tests, and roll back automatically. It ends with common issues and five debugging steps. The SKILL.md points to guides on data preparation, training, validation and deployment, a DAG template, a training config and a validation checklist, but none of these files exist in the repo, so its code examples stop at placeholder comments. The hyperparameter-tuning, experiment-tracking-setup and model-deployment-patterns skills it suggests next aren't in the repo either.",
