              "label": "Before each task",
              "text": "The agent reads the files, flags anything outdated and proposes updates before it starts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The Conductor plugin's /conductor:setup command for its setup steps; with the skill alone, the agent writes the files from the templates"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The context step of Conductor, a plugin in the same repo whose workflow runs context, then spec and plan, then implementation. Each file answers one question: product.md what is built and why, product-guidelines.md how the product speaks to users, tech-stack.md which languages, dependencies and infrastructure, workflow.md how the team works (TDD, commit conventions, review, coverage targets), and tracks.md which work units, called tracks, are active or done. The files stay in sync: a new dependency goes into tech-stack.md with its reason and version, and a finished feature moves from planned to implemented in product.md. For a new project, setup asks about vision, tech and workflow; for an existing one it reads the code and configs and pre-fills the files for you to review. Before each track the agent runs a validation checklist over product, technical, workflow and track context. At the start of a session it reads index.md, tracks.md and the current plan; at the end it updates the plan, notes blockers and commits work in progress. It warns against stale, scattered, unwritten and over-detailed context.",
