          "text": "A staged process with npm and yarn commands, using a React upgrade as the running example. It opens with semantic versioning and the ^ and ~ ranges, then audits with npm outdated, npm audit and npm-check-updates and traces why a package is installed. A compatibility matrix records which versions of related packages go together, such as React with react-dom, React Router and Testing Library. Phase 1 lists current versions, reads changelogs and migration guides, and writes the upgrade order to UPGRADE_PLAN.md: TypeScript, then React, React Router, testing libraries and build tools. Phase 2 upgrades one package, and one major version, at a time, running tests and the build after each. Phase 3 adds tests that check matching versions and no peer-dependency warnings. Breaking changes get codemods (jscodeshift scripts that rewrite code, tried with a dry run first) or a custom find-and-replace script. Testing covers unit, integration, snapshot and Cypress end-to-end tests. A rollback script upgrades on a branch and commits only if tests pass. It ends with a Renovate config that auto-merges minor and patch updates but not majors, a weekly Dependabot config, and commands for lockfiles, peer dependencies and workspaces.",
