          "text": "A forensic reference with two ready-made workflows. Acquisition covers live capture on Windows (WinPmem, DumpIt and GUI tools), Linux (LiME, /dev/mem, /proc/kcore) and macOS (osxpmem), and copying memory out of VMware, VirtualBox, QEMU and Hyper-V. A reference file holds Volatility 3's setup and its main plugins for processes, network, DLLs and modules, injection, the registry and files on Windows, and for Linux and macOS. The malware workflow surveys processes and connections, runs malfind to find injected code, inspects suspicious processes' DLLs and handles, dumps them, extracts strings and scans with YARA. The incident-response workflow builds a timeline, then checks command lines, Run-key persistence, services, scheduled tasks and recent files. It explains the Windows structures these tools read (EPROCESS, PEB, VAD), four injection techniques, rootkit checks such as comparing pslist with psscan to find hidden processes, credential extraction (password hashes, LSA secrets, cached domain logins), memory YARA rules, and FLOSS for obfuscated strings. Its best practices: hash the dump right away, keep a chain of custody, cross-check plugins and correlate with disk and network evidence.",
