              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A design along these patterns and Python/FastAPI templates in its reference file; it adds no steps of its own"
            },
            {
              "label": "Watch for",
              "text": "Eventual consistency between the two models — it shows read-your-writes handling and projection rebuilds"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for Command Query Responsibility Segregation, not a workflow. The SKILL.md diagrams the split: commands express intent to change state and go through command handlers that validate and emit events; queries read from a denormalized read model built by projectors that apply those events. Its do's and don'ts: separate the models, accept propagation delay, validate in command handlers, version events, don't query inside commands or couple the two schemas, and don't over-engineer. A reference file holds Python templates — a command base and bus with handlers, a query base and bus with paginated results, a FastAPI app wiring command endpoints (POST/PUT/DELETE) to query endpoints (GET), a read-model synchronizer that tracks a checkpoint and can rebuild a projection from scratch, and a query handler that waits for the read model to reach an expected version before returning, falling back to stale data with a warning after a timeout.",
