          ],
          "text": "The implementation step of wshobson's Conductor methodology (context → spec & plan → implement). For each pending task in a track's plan.md it follows red-green-refactor: write tests that fail, write the minimum code to pass, then refactor while tests stay green, checking coverage against an 80% target. It commits with a typed, scoped message, attaches a rich git note of decisions and files changed, and records the commit SHA back in plan.md. When a phase's tasks are done it runs a verification protocol — list changed files, confirm tests exist, run the full suite, lint and type-check, generate manual verification steps — then waits for explicit user approval before a checkpoint commit. It also covers deviations (scope added or cut, technical changes), error recovery, and TDD variations by task type. The quality gates, git conventions and checkpoint mechanics live in a reference file.",
