          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're writing a runbook for a service or database outage, or onboarding on-call engineers"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Gives a runbook structure and fill-in templates, with severity levels (SEV1–SEV4) and their response times"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A runbook written for a 3 AM responder, with triage steps, mitigation and rollback commands, an escalation matrix and status-update templates"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also has",
              "text": "Troubleshooting for why runbooks fail in a real incident — missing preconditions, steps run out of order, stale commands, delayed comms"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A template library for incident response runbooks. The SKILL.md sets out a nine-section structure (overview, detection, triage, mitigation, root cause, resolution, verification and rollback, communication, escalation) and a severity table. A reference file holds two full worked runbooks: a payment-service outage runbook with alert and dashboard links, a five-minute triage, mitigation paths for a down service, high latency, partial failures and traffic surges, verification and rollback commands, an escalation matrix and notification, status-update and resolution message templates; and a database incident runbook with SQL for connection-pool exhaustion, replication lag and disk-space emergencies. The SKILL.md itself adds troubleshooting advice: add a prerequisite check and failure note to each command, put a numbered checklist at the top, stamp a last-verified date and owner, assign a dedicated communicator, and guard destructive SQL with a dry-run count. It points to the postmortem-writing and on-call-handoff skills for the steps after resolution.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/incident-response/skills/incident-runbook-templates"
