            },
            {
              "label": "Also has",
              "text": "A meeting facilitation guide and a table of anti-patterns (blame, shallow analysis, no action items, no follow-up)"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A guide to writing postmortems that drive learning rather than blame. The SKILL.md contrasts blame-focused with blameless framing, lists what triggers a postmortem (SEV1/SEV2, customer outages over 15 minutes, data loss, near-misses, novel failures), and gives a rough timeline from incident to quarterly pattern review. A reference file holds a full standard template worked through a payment-service outage — summary, timeline, root-cause with a 5 Whys chain, detection, response, impact, lessons and action items — plus a 5 Whys template and a quick template for minor incidents. The SKILL.md adds a 60-minute meeting structure, facilitation tips (redirect blame to systems, document dissent, time-box tangents), an anti-patterns table, and do's and don'ts: start immediately, be specific, assign owners, share widely, never name and shame, don't skip small incidents or follow-up. It points to the runbook and on-call-handoff skills.",
