              "text": "Baseline scan first, adopt incrementally, block only on critical findings, exclude tests and generated code"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A configuration reference for static application security testing. It frames an initial assessment — identify languages, note compliance needs (PCI-DSS, SOC 2), pick a tool, run a baseline — then covers three tools. Semgrep: custom pattern rules, language-specific security rules, CI integration and false-positive tuning. SonarQube: quality gates, security hotspots, custom quality profiles, enterprise LDAP/SAML. CodeQL: GitHub Advanced Security, custom queries, SARIF output. It shows quick-start install commands, a GitHub Actions step and a pre-commit hook, a custom rule that flags a hardcoded JWT secret, and a PCI-DSS scan. Best practices stress starting from a baseline, incremental adoption, documenting suppressions, excluding test and generated code, and security champions. A troubleshooting section addresses high false-positive rates, slow scans and integration failures, and a table compares the three tools by language support, cost and integration. It points to the STRIDE-analysis and threat-mitigation skills.",
