      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs event stores for event-sourced systems — append-only streams, ordering, versioning, subscriptions — and compares EventStoreDB, Postgres, Kafka, DynamoDB and Marten.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're building event-sourcing infrastructure or choosing where to store events"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sets the requirements for an event store — append-only, ordered per stream and globally, versioned for concurrency, subscribable, idempotent"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A design along these rules; a reference file holds the templates and worked examples"
            },
            {
              "label": "Compares",
              "text": "EventStoreDB, PostgreSQL, Kafka, DynamoDB and Marten, with what each is best and worst at"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for designing the storage layer of an event-sourced system. The SKILL.md diagrams an event store as per-aggregate streams plus a global position, lists its requirements (immutable append-only events, per-stream and global ordering, optimistic concurrency via versions, real-time subscriptions, idempotent writes), and compares five technologies: EventStoreDB for pure event sourcing, PostgreSQL when you already run Postgres, Kafka for high-throughput streaming but weak per-stream queries, DynamoDB for serverless AWS, and Marten for .NET. Its do's and don'ts: stream IDs that include the aggregate type, correlation and causation IDs, version events from day one, deduplicate by event ID, index for your query patterns, never update or delete events, keep payloads small, don't skip optimistic concurrency, and handle slow consumers. The concrete templates and worked examples sit in a reference file.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/backend-development/skills/event-store-design"
