        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Coordinates distributed transactions across services with the saga pattern — ordered steps, compensating rollbacks, per-step timeouts and stuck-saga recovery.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You need a multi-service transaction without two-phase commit — an order, booking or approval flow that must roll back on partial failure"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Defines the saga as ordered steps, each with a compensating undo, run by an orchestrator or by choreography"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A saga definition, orchestrator or choreography code, idempotent compensation per service, per-step timeouts and monitoring; Python is in the reference file"
            },
            {
              "label": "Term",
              "text": "A saga is a chain of local transactions where each completed step has an undo that runs in reverse if a later step fails"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for managing distributed transactions as sagas. You provide service boundaries, which steps must be atomic, failure modes and SLAs; it produces an ordered saga with action and compensation commands, an implementation, idempotent always-succeeds compensation, per-step timeouts and monitoring. Its do's: make every step idempotent, design compensations as the critical path, thread a saga_id through every event and log, set per-step timeouts, log state transitions, and test compensation by injecting a failure at each step. Its don'ts: don't assume instant completion, don't skip compensation testing, don't couple services synchronously, don't ignore partial failures, don't use one global timeout. A troubleshooting section covers sagas stuck compensating, duplicate executions after a restart, lost choreography events, premature timeouts and wrong compensation order. Core concepts, templates and a timeout-aware orchestrator with Prometheus metrics live in reference files.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/backend-development/skills/saga-orchestration"
        },
