            }
          ],
          "text": "A decision framework for multi-cloud architecture. The SKILL.md tabulates equivalent services across AWS, Azure, GCP and OCI for compute, storage and databases, then lays out four patterns: a primary cloud with disaster recovery in another, best-of-breed (AI on GCP, enterprise on Azure, regulated data on OCI, general compute on AWS), geographic distribution for latency and data sovereignty, and a cloud-agnostic abstraction built on Kubernetes, PostgreSQL/MySQL, Kafka, Redis, S3-compatible storage, Prometheus/Grafana and a service mesh behind a Terraform layer. It compares pricing models and lists cost-optimization strategies (reserved and spot capacity, right-sizing, serverless for variable load, lifecycle policies, allocation tags) and a four-phase migration (assess, pilot, migrate with dual-run, optimize). Best practices: infrastructure as code, CI/CD, design for cross-cloud failure, managed services, monitoring, and training teams on several clouds. Fuller comparison and pattern detail sit in reference files.",
