            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for optimizing vector indexes in production. The SKILL.md maps data size to an index: flat exact search under 10K vectors, HNSW to 1M, HNSW with quantization to 100M, IVF+PQ or DiskANN beyond that. It explains the three HNSW parameters — M (connections per node), efConstruction (build quality) and efSearch (search quality) — each trading recall against memory or speed, and lists quantization options from full FP32 down through FP16, INT8 scalar, product quantization and binary, with their byte costs. Its advice: benchmark with real queries not synthetic, monitor recall continuously because data drift degrades it, start from defaults and tune only when needed, use quantization for large memory savings, consider tiered hot/cold storage, profile before optimizing, account for build and reindex time, and warm a cold index. The concrete templates and worked examples live in a reference file.",
