            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference rather than a step-by-step workflow. For AWS, Azure, GCP and Oracle Cloud it sets an IPsec VPN, cheaper but over the internet (up to 1.25 Gbps per AWS tunnel, 3 Gbps on GCP), against a dedicated private link with lower latency and up to 100 Gbps. It sketches three layouts: hub-and-spoke from on-premises through a transit gateway or Azure vWAN to production, staging and development networks; multi-region with a Direct Connect per region; and multi-cloud with one dedicated link per provider. Routing uses BGP with example AS numbers, route propagation and filtering. High availability means dual VPN tunnels and active-active links with ECMP routing and BGP failover. Security practices include private links, encrypted tunnels, VPC endpoints, flow logs and DDoS protection; cost advice is to right-size links and keep VPN for low-bandwidth traffic. It lists the metrics to watch: tunnel state, traffic, packet loss, latency and BGP sessions. A short reference file compares the four dedicated-link services and advises redundant circuits in separate facilities, with VPN as backup. It points to multi-cloud-architecture and terraform-module-library.",
