      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds read models from event streams in event-sourced and CQRS systems: projectors with checkpoints, rebuilds, search indexes and aggregated reporting tables.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have an event-sourced system and need query-friendly views, dashboards or search indexes built from its events"
            },
            {
              "label": "Terms",
              "text": "A projection turns a stream of events into a read model, a table or index shaped for queries; a checkpoint records the last event applied"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Explains four projection types, live, catch-up, persistent and inline, and nine do's and don'ts, such as idempotent projections so replays are safe"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Async Python templates for a projector with checkpoints and rebuilds, an order summary, an Elasticsearch search index, daily sales totals and a multi-table projection"
            }
          ],
          "text": "In CQRS with event sourcing, changes are stored as events and reads come from separate read models; this skill covers that read side. The SKILL.md shows the architecture (event store, projector, read model) and four projection types: live from a subscription for current state, catch-up over history to rebuild, persistent with a stored checkpoint to resume after a restart, and inline in the write's transaction for strong consistency. Its rules: make projections idempotent so replays are safe, use transactions for multi-table updates, store checkpoints, monitor lag and plan for rebuilds; keep projections independent, handle and alert on errors, process events in order and denormalize for the queries you need. A reference file holds the templates, in async Python, with asyncpg for Postgres: a base Projection class and a Projector that runs each projection from its checkpoint and can rebuild one from scratch, an order summary projection, a product search projection into Elasticsearch, a daily sales aggregate that subtracts refunds, and a customer activity projection across several tables.",
