            }
          ],
          "text": "Terms first: an SLI is a measurement such as the share of requests without a 5xx error, an SLO the internal target for it, an SLA the contract with customers. It writes availability and latency SLIs in PromQL over 28 days, plus a durability ratio, tabulates the downtime 99% to 99.99% allows, and lists what to weigh in a target: user expectations, business needs, current performance, cost and competitors. The error budget is one minus the target, so 99.9% leaves 43.2 minutes a month; a policy maps the budget left to action, from normal velocity to a feature freeze at zero. Prometheus recording rules compute the SLIs, compliance, the budget left and a 5-minute burn rate, how fast the budget is being spent. Alerts fire on a fast burn (14.4 times, over one hour and five minutes), a slow burn (6 times, over six hours and 30 minutes) and an exhausted budget, but the longer burn rates they use are left for you to record. A Grafana layout and queries show compliance, budget, trend and days until it runs out. A reference file adds a combined alert, the review cadence and ten best practices, such as never aiming for 100%.",
