        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes on-call shift handoffs that pass on active incidents, open investigations, recent changes and known issues, including mid-incident handoffs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Your on-call shift is ending, you're handing over mid-incident, or you're setting up or improving a team's handoff routine"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Has the outgoing engineer cover five things: active incidents, ongoing investigations, recent changes, known issues and upcoming events"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A handoff document from one of three Markdown templates: a full shift handoff, a quick async one or a mid-incident handoff"
            },
            {
              "label": "Timing",
              "text": "A 30-minute overlap: the outgoing engineer writes for 15 minutes, then both join a 15-minute sync call"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A handoff routine for human on-call rotations that the agent helps write. The SKILL.md names what every handoff carries and how to time it: the outgoing engineer writes the document and holds a sync call, and the incoming engineer reviews it, joins the call and checks their alerting works. Its troubleshooting covers incomplete handoffs (no section may stay empty: write \"none\"), time zones that rule out a call (use the async template plus a recorded walkthrough), inheriting an incident mid-response (the outgoing engineer stays reachable on Slack for 15 minutes), inconsistent formats across teams, and confirming alerts with a test alert before the overlap ends. The reference file's templates: a full shift handoff with incidents, investigations with their tickets, issues resolved this shift, deployments and config changes, workarounds, upcoming events, escalation contacts, common commands, links and checklists for both engineers; a short async handoff with a TL;DR and a watch list; and an incident handoff with current state, what's known, what's been done, next steps, key people and communication status. It points to incident-runbook-templates and postmortem-writing.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/incident-response/skills/on-call-handoff-patterns"
