      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Sets up metrics, distributed tracing, dashboards and alerts for Istio or Linkerd service meshes, using Prometheus, Grafana, Jaeger, Kiali and OpenTelemetry.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You run Istio or Linkerd on Kubernetes and need request metrics, traces across services, a dependency map or alerts on mesh traffic"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Frames mesh monitoring around the golden signals, latency, traffic, errors and saturation, with starting alert thresholds such as P99 over 500 ms or errors over 1%"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "YAML and commands that wire Prometheus, Jaeger, Kiali and an OpenTelemetry collector into Istio, PromQL queries, a Grafana dashboard and alert rules"
            },
            {
              "label": "Sampling",
              "text": "Trace every request in development and 1–10% in production"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Observability for the traffic between services in an Istio or Linkerd mesh. The SKILL.md sets out the three pillars, metrics, traces and logs, and the four golden signals with suggested thresholds, plus rules: sample appropriately, propagate trace headers consistently, alert on the golden signals, link metrics to traces with exemplars and tier storage; don't over-sample, let label cardinality grow, skip dependency dashboards or forget what observability costs. Its reference file is mostly Istio: a Prometheus scrape config and a Prometheus Operator ServiceMonitor; PromQL for request rate, 5xx rate, P99 latency, TCP connections and request size; Jaeger with Istio tracing turned on; a Grafana dashboard with request rate, error rate, P99 latency and service topology panels; Kiali to visualize the mesh; and an OpenTelemetry collector feeding Jaeger and Prometheus, with Istio sampling 10% of traces. For Linkerd it gives linkerd viz commands for top requests, per-route metrics, live traffic and service edges. Prometheus alert rules fire on errors above 5%, P99 latency over one second and mesh certificates expiring within a week.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/cloud-infrastructure/skills/service-mesh-observability"
