      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a single-file interactive HTML playground with controls, a live preview and a generated prompt you copy back to the agent.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A choice is easier to make by tweaking controls and watching a preview than by describing it, such as a layout, a query or a diff review"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Picks the closest of six templates, builds the page, then opens it in your default browser"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "One self-contained HTML file with controls, an instant preview, 3 to 5 presets and a copyable prompt"
            },
            {
              "label": "The prompt",
              "text": "A plain-language instruction naming only what you changed, ready to paste back into the chat"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Anthropic's playground plugin for Claude Code. A playground is a page with controls on one side, a live preview on the other and a prompt at the bottom with a copy button. Its six templates cover visual design decisions (components, layouts, spacing, color, typography), data and query building (SQL, APIs, pipelines, regex), concept maps for learning and scoping, document critique with approve, reject and comment, code review of diffs, commits and PRs with line comments, and codebase architecture maps. Every playground inlines its CSS and JavaScript with no external dependencies, re-renders on every change with no Apply button, uses a dark theme and looks good on first load. The prompt reads as an instruction rather than a dump of values, mentions only non-default choices and carries enough context to act on without seeing the page. After writing the file it runs open to launch it in your browser.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/tree/c07c748f1c680734a813eefd909bc073f8a9103f/plugins/playground/skills/playground"
