      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides writing a skill for a Claude Code plugin, from concrete use cases to a lean SKILL.md with references, examples and scripts.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're adding a skill to a Claude Code plugin, or tightening an existing skill's description and layout"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Walks six steps: gather concrete examples, plan scripts, references and assets, create the folder, write SKILL.md, validate, iterate"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A skill folder whose SKILL.md body stays around 1,500 to 2,000 words, with detail moved to references/, examples/ and scripts/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike skill-creator",
              "text": "That one, Anthropic's general version, has an init script and packaging; this one skips them: plugin skills live in the plugin's skills/ folder and ship with it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Anthropic's plugin-dev plugin for Claude Code, adapting the original skill-creator method to plugins. Its core idea is progressive disclosure: the name and description are always in context, the SKILL.md body loads when the skill triggers, and bundled files load only as needed, so the body stays lean and detail moves to references/. It asks for a third-person description packed with the exact phrases users would say (\"This skill should be used when the user asks to...\") and an imperative, verb-first body rather than second person. A validation checklist covers structure, description quality, writing style, referenced files that actually exist and working examples; testing means loading the plugin locally with --plugin-dir and asking questions that should trigger the skill. The plugin's own hook, agent and settings skills serve as worked examples, and it suggests the plugin's skill-reviewer agent for a final review.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/tree/c07c748f1c680734a813eefd909bc073f8a9103f/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/skill-development"
