      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Walks a smart contract project through Trail of Bits' five-step security workflow, from Slither scans and diagrams to properties and manual review.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to secure a smart contract end to end, on every check-in or before deployment, rather than hunt one bug"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs Slither's detectors and the upgradeability and ERC checks that apply, draws three security diagrams, helps write security properties, then reviews what tools miss"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A security report with findings and fixes, diagrams, documented properties, manual-review findings and a prioritized action plan with a step checklist"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Slither installed, plus Echidna or Manticore for the fuzzing or symbolic-execution setup"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Trail of Bits' secure development workflow for smart contracts, from its building-secure-contracts plugin. Step one runs Slither's 70+ detectors and triages the findings. Step two runs only the special checks that apply: slither-check-upgradeability for upgradeable contracts, slither-check-erc for token standards, slither-prop for ERC20 properties, and a pointer to the token-integration-analyzer skill. Step three generates an inheritance graph, a function summary showing visibility and access control, and a map of who can write each state variable. Step four, which it calls the most important, documents security properties such as invariants, access rules and arithmetic limits, and sets up Echidna fuzzing, Manticore symbolic execution or custom Slither checks. Step five searches the code for what tools miss: on-chain secrets, front-running and MEV, weak randomness and signature issues, and oracle or flash-loan risks. It refuses shortcuts such as marking a step not applicable without searching the code first.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/building-secure-contracts/skills/secure-workflow-guide"
