      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds APIs, configuration options and interfaces whose easy path leads to security mistakes, such as algorithm choice, dangerous defaults and silent failures.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're reviewing an API, library, config schema or auth interface for how easily developers could misuse it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Maps security-relevant choice points, probes zero, empty, negative and swapped values, and imagines a malicious, a lazy and a confused developer"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Findings rated Critical to Low by how easy the misuse is, each checked for real exploitability"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Implementation bugs or business-logic flaws, which it leaves to ordinary code review"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Trail of Bits' check for footguns: designs where the secure choice isn't the path of least resistance. It looks in six places: APIs that let callers pick algorithms or modes (the JWT alg: none problem), defaults that are insecure or where 0 or an empty string switches security off, raw-bytes APIs where keys, nonces and signatures can be swapped without a type error, configuration cliffs where one typo disables protection, silent failures such as verify functions that return true on bad input, and security values passed around as plain strings. It rejects excuses like \"it's documented\" or \"advanced users need flexibility\". Language guides cover footguns in C/C++, Go, Rust, Swift, Java, Kotlin, C#, PHP, JavaScript/TypeScript, Python and Ruby, with separate references on crypto APIs, configuration, authentication and real-world case studies. Its plugin also has a sharp-edges-analyzer agent that runs the whole four-phase analysis on its own.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/sharp-edges/skills/sharp-edges"
        },
