      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Scores a smart contract codebase's maturity across Trail of Bits' nine categories, with evidence for each rating and a prioritized improvement roadmap.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to grade how mature, tested and documented a smart contract or blockchain project is against a fixed rubric"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Explores the code, rates nine categories from Missing to Strong with file:line evidence, and asks you about processes the code can't show"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An executive summary, a scorecard, per-category analysis and a roadmap ranked Critical, High and Medium with effort estimates"
            },
            {
              "label": "Takes",
              "text": "About 30 to 40 minutes, plus your knowledge of monitoring, incident response and team practices"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Trail of Bits' Code Maturity Evaluation, from its building-secure-contracts plugin. The nine categories are arithmetic (overflow protection, precision, rounding), auditing (events, monitoring, incident response), authentication and access controls, complexity management, decentralization (centralization risk, upgrade control, timelocks and multisigs), documentation, transaction-ordering risks such as MEV, front-running and oracle security, low-level manipulation such as assembly and low-level calls, and testing and verification, including fuzzing, formal verification and CI. Each category is rated 0 to 4, and any criterion at Weak makes the whole category Weak. It presents its findings with file references, discusses borderline cases with you and settles the ratings together. It won't call the assessment done until all nine categories have evidence, and won't mark MEV or low-level risks as not applicable without searching the code first.",
