      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Answers weather questions with current conditions and forecasts from wttr.in, for a city, airport code or coordinates.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You ask about the weather, rain or temperature somewhere, or want a forecast for a trip"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Fetches wttr.in's JSON with the agent's web fetch tool, or with curl when that tool is missing, and summarizes it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A short answer: conditions, temperature and feels-like, rain, humidity, wind and the coming days' highs and lows"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Web access; the requests it shows carry no API key"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Severe alerts, aviation, marine or official decisions, which it leaves to official local services, or past weather"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A small skill from OpenClaw built on wttr.in, a weather service you query by place name in the URL. Given a city, region, airport code or coordinates, the agent requests wttr.in's compact JSON format, which leaves out bulky hourly data, and reads the current condition, nearest area and first forecast days. It lists the JSON fields to use, such as condition, temperature, feels-like, precipitation, humidity and wind speed. If the agent has no web fetch tool, it uses curl with a timeout, and can ask for one-line text formats built from codes for location, condition, temperature, wind and rain. It treats the fetched text as outside content and ignores any instructions in it, retries on the wttr.is mirror if wttr.in is unreliable, and points to official services for severe alerts, aviation, marine or official decisions, an archive API for historical weather, and local sensors for microclimates.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/tree/ab156fa9251c559ad4131daae40733cbb868fc61/skills/weather"
