        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes a long narrative report of a project's whole development history from the observations claude-mem recorded.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want the story of a project's development, as recorded by claude-mem across its sessions"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Fetches the project's full timeline from claude-mem's local worker and gives it to a subagent that also queries claude-mem's SQLite database"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown report of 3,000 to 6,000 words, saved as journey-into-<project>.md"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "Origins, architecture changes, breakthroughs, debugging sagas, technical debt, work patterns, statistics and lessons"
            },
            {
              "label": "Cost",
              "text": "It estimates the timeline's tokens first and asks before going on above 100K"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "claude-mem with its worker running, sqlite3, and an agent that can start subagents"
            }
          ],
          "text": "claude-mem records observations, short notes about what happened in each agent session, and this skill turns a project's whole record into a history. The agent works out the project name, using the parent repository when you're in a git worktree, and fetches every observation, session boundary and summary from the worker's local API. It estimates the size at about one token per four characters, reports it and waits for your go-ahead on large timelines. A subagent then writes \"Journey Into\" the project as a narrative, not bullet lists, citing observation IDs and dates. One section estimates how many tokens memory saved, from SQL queries plus fixed assumptions, such as 30% of injected context preventing rework, with a monthly table. The report is saved in the current folder unless you name another path, and the agent tells you where it is, the token cost, the date range and how many observations it covered.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem/tree/24802b13ef5e9bf61a84e650af446c4ff69ab399/plugin/skills/timeline-report"
        },
