          "text": "You run it from the repository and say which commits to cover: since the last release, the past week, a date range or a version. The agent scans those commits, sorts them into features, improvements, bug fixes, breaking changes and security, drops internal work, and translates developer phrasing into what changed for the user, in your brand voice or your style file's format. The example output is a dated update with short bold-titled entries under emoji headings. It suggests reviewing the result before publishing, and saving it to CHANGELOG.md, and lists other uses such as GitHub release notes, app store descriptions, update emails and announcement posts.",
