        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Cleans up a messy folder: finds duplicates, proposes a better structure, then moves, renames and archives files once you approve.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A folder such as Downloads, Documents, Desktop or Projects is a mess, or you suspect duplicate files"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Surveys the folder's file types, sizes and dates, finds duplicates by hash and by name, and proposes a new structure"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A plan to approve, then the files moved, renamed and archived, with a summary and maintenance tips"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks",
              "text": "Before deleting anything, and logs every move so it can be undone"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent first asks which folder, what the problem is, what to leave alone and how aggressive to be. It then lists the folder with shell commands, counting file types, finding the largest files and checking dates, and groups what it finds by type, by purpose such as work, personal or archive, and by age. For duplicates it shows every copy with sizes and dates and recommends which to keep. Before changing anything it presents a plan: the current state, the proposed folder tree, the folders it will create, the files it will move, rename or delete, and the files it needs you to decide on. Once you approve, it creates the folders and moves and renames files, preserving modification dates, handling name clashes and stopping when something unexpected comes up. It ends with what changed and a weekly-to-yearly maintenance routine. Examples include sorting photos into year and month folders from their EXIF dates.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills/tree/be2a406907dbc61b73e6827ded415c96139d13a2/file-organizer"
        },
