            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The data plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent first settles the dashboard's purpose, audience, key metrics, the dimensions to filter by and the data source. Data comes from a query when a data warehouse is connected, from pasted or uploaded data it cleans, or from a sample dataset it invents to match your description, with instructions for swapping in real data. The layout is a title with filters, two to four KPI cards, one to three charts, then an optional detail table. It writes one HTML file from its base template: card-based CSS, line, bar, doughnut, stacked and mixed charts with Chart.js loaded from a CDN, dropdown and date-range filters that update every chart and the table together, sortable columns, number formatting and print styles. For bigger data it pre-aggregates before embedding, and past 100,000 rows it points you to a BI tool instead. It saves the file under a descriptive name, opens it in your browser, checks that it renders, and explains how to update the data or the styling.",
