      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Walks a system design from requirements through high-level design, deep dive and scaling to a design document with explicit trade-offs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You ask how to architect a system or service, or need help with API design, data modeling or service boundaries"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Works through five stages: requirements, high-level design, deep dive, scale and reliability, then trade-offs"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A structured design document with ASCII or described diagrams, stated assumptions, trade-offs, and what to revisit as the system grows"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike full design methods",
              "text": "This one is a one-page checklist of what to cover, with no examples or templates"
            },
            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short framework the agent follows for design questions. It starts from requirements: what the system does, its scale, latency, availability and cost targets, and constraints such as team size, timeline and existing stack. The high-level design covers a component diagram, data flow, API contracts and storage choices. The deep dive covers the data model, endpoints in REST, GraphQL or gRPC, caching, queues and events, and error handling with retries. Scale and reliability cover load estimates, horizontal or vertical scaling, failover and redundancy, and monitoring. Every decision's trade-offs are made explicit, weighing complexity, cost, team familiarity, time to market and maintainability. The result is a design document with its assumptions spelled out and a note of what to revisit as the system grows.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/engineering/skills/system-design"
        },
