          "text": "Task tracking from the productivity plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins, in a plain Markdown file that you and the agent both edit. It always uses TASKS.md in the current folder. Asking what's on your plate gets a summary of Active and Waiting On, with anything overdue or urgent highlighted. A new task goes under Active as a bold title with who it's for and when it's due. A finished one is checked, struck through, dated and moved to Done, which is cleared after about a week. Asking what you're waiting on says how long each item has waited. On first use it copies dashboard.html into the folder, a board that reads and writes the same file, auto-saves, picks up edits made outside it and supports drag-and-drop reordering, and points you to /productivity:start for the full set-up.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/productivity/skills/task-management"
        },
