              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "As /productivity:start, or when you set up the plugin for the first time"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The set-up step of the productivity plugin. It checks the working folder for TASKS.md, CLAUDE.md, a memory/ folder and dashboard.html, and creates what's missing: TASKS.md from task-management's template, and dashboard.html copied from the plugin. It doesn't open a browser: it tells you to open the dashboard from your file browser. On a first run, with no CLAUDE.md or memory/ yet, it builds memory from your real task list, which it calls the best source of workplace language. It asks where you keep your todos, in a file or an app such as Asana, Linear, Jira, Notion or Todoist, then asks about each term it doesn't know: who Todd is, what PSR stands for, whether Phoenix is a project codename. It then offers a longer scan of your chat, email, documents and calendar through connected MCP servers, and sorts what it finds into ready to add, needs clarification, and unclear for later. Last, it writes CLAUDE.md, about 50 to 80 lines of tables on you, your people, terms, projects and preferences, and memory/ with a full glossary, a file per person and per project, and your company's teams, tools and processes. Sources that aren't connected are skipped and noted.",
