      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Syncs TASKS.md with your project tracker, triages stale tasks, fills gaps in workplace memory and can scan chat, email and calendar for missed todos.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want TASKS.md and your workplace memory caught up with your project tracker and recent work"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Offers to add tasks assigned to you in a project tracker or GitHub Issues, flags stale tasks, and asks about people and projects memory lacks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Triage",
              "text": "Tasks past due, Active for 30+ days or with no person or project; you mark each done, reschedule it or move it to Someday"
            },
            {
              "label": "With --comprehensive",
              "text": "It also scans chat, email, documents and calendar for todos you haven't captured and new people or projects to remember"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "Never adds tasks or memories without your confirmation"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "As /productivity:update, on the TASKS.md and memory/ that start sets up"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The upkeep step of the productivity plugin, run once start has created TASKS.md and the memory/ folder; without them it suggests start first. It fetches open tasks assigned to you from a connected project tracker such as Asana, Linear or Jira, or from GitHub Issues with gh when you're in a repo, and matches them to TASKS.md by fuzzy title. New ones it offers to add, ones finished elsewhere it offers to mark done, and ones only in TASKS.md it flags as possibly stale. With no source connected, it skips the sync. It then flags overdue tasks, tasks Active for 30 days or more and tasks with no person or project, for you to mark done, reschedule or move to Someday. It checks every person, project and term in your tasks against memory, asks about the ones it can't place, and files your answers in the glossary, people or project files, along with links, status changes, relationships and deadlines found in tasks. --comprehensive adds a scan of recent chat, email, documents and calendar: likely todos you haven't tracked, new people and projects with how often they're mentioned, and projects quiet for 30 days to mark completed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/productivity/skills/update"
        },
