          ],
          "text": "From the PM Skills marketplace's pm-execution plugin. The agent acts as an experienced product manager writing the shortest PRD that lets a team decide and start, roughly 600 to 1,000 words unless you ask for more. If the problem, the target users or how success will be measured is missing, it asks up to three short questions and writes nothing until you answer or tell it to go ahead, then marks the gaps as assumptions. When it helps, it searches the web for the market, competitors and regulations, cites sources beside claims, and keeps only findings that change a decision. Market segments, defined by problems rather than demographics, and a value proposition for each are always included; the solution has to deliver each proposition's how, and one to three key results measure its what after. Sections with little to say get a line, unknown contacts are left out, nothing is padded with TBD, and anything unproven goes under assumptions and open questions. The release section says what's in the first version, what comes later and what's out, in relative timeframes. It writes in short, plain sentences, and its reply lists what it left out so you can ask for more.",
