        "skew": 534
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Checks DXF and STEP files against SendCutSend's current specs before you order, and reports pass, fail or need-more-info for each cited rule.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're about to upload a DXF or STEP to SendCutSend for laser cutting, CNC routing, bending, tapping or another service and want it checked first"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Fetches SendCutSend's current ordering guide, catalog and specs, measures the exact upload file, and compares only where both a cited rule and a measured fact exist"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A report marking each check pass, fail or need more info, each row linked to its rule source, with the next edits to make"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks",
              "text": "For your material or SKU, thickness and services when they're missing or unclear, offering candidates with links and photos from SendCutSend's data"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "build123d and ezdxf in your project's Python environment; it uses text-to-cad's cad command for inspection when that's installed"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also",
              "text": "Diagnostic images with callouts for failures and ambiguous geometry, when the agent has an image tool"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Other fabrication services, or ordering: it never calls a file ready unless every required check passes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "SendCutSend is an online service that laser-cuts, CNC-routes, bends, taps and finishes parts from uploaded files, and this skill is a conservative preflight for it. It records the order intent first: file type, process, material or SKU, thickness, quantity, services, finish and hardware, and when that's unclear it lists candidates with links and photos from SendCutSend's data and asks you to choose. It fetches the ordering guide, catalog JSON and specs JSON fresh for each review, treats them as evidence rather than a stable API, and never turns missing or conflicting data into a pass or a fail. It inspects the exact file you'll upload, with text-to-cad's cad inspection where available and build123d or ezdxf for the rest: for DXF, units, closed profiles, duplicates, stray text, layers, and bend lines with the flange depth on both sides; for STEP, readability, solid bodies, units, thickness and bend radii. Missing or unexpected DXF units count as a scale error until you confirm them. Each finding is compared against the exact SKU's specs and cited by field path or guide section, or marked as direct file inspection.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/earthtojake/text-to-cad/tree/4099cac3ddc56a5e696138c53fd7bee685e8ad9d/skills/sendcutsend"
        },
