      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Catalogs AI-default UI patterns, from purple gradients and bento grids to invented dashboard numbers, each with why it reads as generated and a fix.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The agent builds or edits a website, web app or dashboard and you don't want it to look AI-made"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Lists AI-default UI patterns as Tell, Why and Fix across color, layout, decoration, app screens, motion and performance"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A UI checklist run alongside the core's Delivery Gate, from the palette's source to real numbers and sized media"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The core antislop skill, whose rules it cites by number"
            }
          ],
          "text": "antislop's UI skill. Each entry names a tell, explains why it reads as generated, and gives a fix, citing the core rule it falls under. Visual entries cover blue-purple gradients, glass, glow and big shadows on every surface, pill-shaped everything, background grids, dark mode by default and the sterile default left after over-filtering; most fixes keep the technique only with a written reason or cap it, such as glass on one or two elements. Layout entries cover the template landing page, identical feature cards, bento grids, three-step How It Works rows, Trusted By logo bars and a highlighted middle pricing tier; decoration entries cover sparkle icons, one Lucide-style icon look, emoji, arrows on every button, eyebrow badges and fake terminals. App screens get their own set: the default sidebar, stat cards, chart and table dashboard, invented numbers and deltas, filler activity feeds, charts that answer no question, John Doe filler data, and empty states that only say No data. Motion entries reject endless loops and stacked template animations, and performance entries cover unsized media, a lazy-loaded hero image and render-blocking scripts.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop/tree/9504989f162a92b1996853eccbb3d8a86e73df68/skills/antislop-ui"
