      "skillMd": {
        "version": "9504989f162a92b1996853eccbb3d8a86e73df68",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Cleans AI-slop comments out of code, such as banners, narration and signature echoes, keeps the ones that explain why, and never touches the code.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The agent writes or edits code comments, or you want generated comments cleaned out of a file"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Removes or shortens comments that add nothing: decorative banners, restated code, step-by-step narration, empty labels, vague TODOs, emoji and end markers"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "Comments on business logic, architecture, security, performance trade-offs, protocols, API contracts, workarounds, edge cases and legal notices"
            },
            {
              "label": "Never",
              "text": "Changes code, identifiers, imports, formatting or whitespace, only comments"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The core antislop skill loaded with it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "antislop's code-comment skill. Each pattern comes as a tell, why it reads as slop, and a fix: separators built from repeated characters, \"// Initialize the variable\" above the line it describes, Step 1, Step 2 narration, labels such as Main logic, TODOs that name no task, JSDoc that only repeats the signature, decorative emoji such as ✅ or 🚀, and \"// end if\" markers. It also targets how comments read: a comment on every trivial line, formal or shouting wording, and over-explained notes that pad a one-line fact with version history and issue numbers. The fix is one line, two at most when the second carries a new fact, in a short, sentence-case developer voice that explains why rather than what. Valuable content never earns extra length. A checklist confirms every remaining comment adds information the code doesn't show, and that only comments changed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop/tree/9504989f162a92b1996853eccbb3d8a86e73df68/skills/antislop-code"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
          "type:guidelines",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "code-quality",
          "anti-slop"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
