      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Makes layouts reflow from phone to desktop instead of shrinking: breakpoints set by content, mobile type and spacing, collapsing grids, no overflow, thumb-sized targets.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "The agent builds a layout that has to hold up at any screen width"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Lists responsive failures as Tell, Why and Fix, from the desktop layout squeezed onto a phone to sticky navs that take over the screen"
            },
            {
              "label": "Its principle",
              "text": "A mobile layout is a different layout that re-stacks, rescales and re-orders, not the desktop at a smaller size"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A mobile layout checklist run alongside the core's Delivery Gate"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The core antislop skill loaded with it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "antislop's responsive-layout skill. Breakpoints go where the content breaks, not at device widths such as 375 or 768px, with as many states as the content needs, typically three rather than a phone stack and a desktop grid. Mobile gets its own smaller type scale, padding and gaps, fluid type with clamp(), and sections sized to their content or dvh instead of 100vh. Grids collapse to one column instead of colliding, tracks use minmax() and auto-fit rather than fixed pixels, and a 12-column grid isn't forced onto content that wants one or two. Overflow entries find whatever leaks sideways, such as tables, code blocks and long strings, and replace clipping with reflow. Tap targets get at least 44 by 44px with space between them, and every hover-only interaction gets a tap equivalent. Navigation reflows into a bottom nav or a labelled menu rather than a bare hamburger, fixed bars reserve their space so they never cover the last item, and sticky headers stay compact. Fixes end in checking the whole width range, not two sample widths.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop/tree/9504989f162a92b1996853eccbb3d8a86e73df68/skills/antislop-layoutmobile"
        },
