          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills, a collection of skills for office work. You share a slide's content, its purpose and audience, and any problem with its current design, then pick a direction: minimalist, corporate, creative, data-focused or storytelling. The agent chooses a layout pattern and writes the spec in a fixed format: a wireframe, the placement of each piece of text with its font, size and hex color, icons with suggested sources, images, shapes, a palette, a typography table, animation suggestions and implementation notes. It applies a few principles throughout: one idea per slide, a clear visual hierarchy, the rule of thirds, contrast for emphasis and alignment to an invisible grid, and shows how a bulleted list of figures becomes a grid of metric tiles. Its frontmatter names two deck-building tools of the repo's office-mcp server, but its instructions never call them.",
