          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You give a ticker, such as AAPL, 600519.SH or 0700.HK, or paste financial data, and choose a quick analysis, a deep dive, a technical review or a peer comparison. The agent works from a fixed framework with a benchmark for reading each figure: valuation ratios (P/E, P/B, P/S, EV/EBITDA, PEG), profitability (gross, operating and net margin, ROE, ROIC), growth in revenue, EPS and free cash flow, and financial health (debt to equity, current ratio, interest coverage, FCF yield). The technical side covers 50- and 200-day moving-average crossovers, MACD, RSI, support and resistance, and patterns such as head and shoulders or double tops. The report follows one template: an executive summary with a rating and risk level, key metrics against the industry, business overview, financial performance, valuation, price trend and key levels, risk factors, bull and bear cases, and a disclaimer. It can't access real-time market data and works from publicly available information, so its tips ask for recent financials, your investment horizon and the peers to compare.",
