          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. A TikTok playbook the agent applies when you ask for a strategy or a script. Content splits into four pillars with target ratios, laid out in a weekly calendar that gives each day a format, a hook type and a call to action. Scripts open with a hook in the first three seconds, deliver one message with a pattern interrupt every few seconds, and end on a call to action, with templates for an educational video and for joining a trend within 48 hours of its sound taking off. Hashtags mix two or three niche tags, one or two trending, one branded and one community tag. It gives posting times for US, UK, Chinese and global audiences, at least one video a day and two or three at best, targets for watch time, engagement, shares, follows and profile visits with a fix for each shortfall, and where to spot trends early. The two n8n workflows, through Google Sheets and Drive, OpenAI, ElevenLabs, DALL-E, Airtable and Slack, are written as YAML outlines of their nodes, not as n8n files to import.",
