            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A report, from a 500-word brief to a 15,000-word PRISMA 2020 systematic review, or in Socratic mode a research plan built from your own answers"
            },
            {
              "label": "Modes",
              "text": "Full, quick, review, lit-review, three-way-scan (papers compared on why, how and what), fact-check, socratic, and systematic-review with optional meta-analysis"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "Every claim cited, and a reference it can't confirm is left out; Socratic mode only asks questions until you ask for suggestions"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The whole repo, as the plugin installs it: its report, three-way-scan and ethics steps read files from academic-paper, academic-paper-reviewer and the repo's shared/ folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike academic-paper",
              "text": "That one writes a journal-ready paper in several citation styles; this one produces a research report"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The research skill of Academic Research Skills (ARS), built from thirteen role prompts. Full mode runs six phases. A research-question agent scores the question on the FINER criteria (feasible, interesting, novel, ethical, relevant) and an architect designs the method; a Devil's Advocate checks both, and you confirm before the search starts. A bibliography agent searches systematically, and a verification agent grades each source on an evidence hierarchy, screens for predatory journals and flags conflicts of interest. A synthesis maps where sources agree and conflict, the Devil's Advocate checks it for cherry-picking and confirmation bias, a compiler writes an APA 7.0 report, and an editor, an ethics reviewer and the Devil's Advocate review it, followed by at most two revision rounds; what's left becomes acknowledged limitations. Critical issues stop progress. Before a literature review it asks which form you want (systematic, scoping, narrative, rapid or none) and recommends none of them. Systematic-review mode adds risk-of-bias assessment with RoB 2 and ROBINS-I, meta-analysis and GRADE. When you ask for a paper, its question brief, bibliography and synthesis hand over to academic-paper.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/imbad0202/academic-research-skills/tree/6d9388674de1ad0437ad95db3d52f92b92204d84/deep-research"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:science",
          "category:writing",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "research",
          "writing",
          "interview"
        ],
        "note": "Some steps read protocols from the repo's shared/ folder and the other ARS skills' folders, which a whole-repo install such as the plugin brings and a single-skill copy doesn't.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "imbad0202/academic-research-skills/academic-pipeline",
      "name": "academic-pipeline",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/imbad0202/academic-research-skills/academic-pipeline",
        "installs": 7700,
        "weeklyInstalls": [193, 176, 175, 158, 217, 239, 191, 160],
        "firstSeen": "2026-03-10"
