            {
              "label": "Runs in",
              "text": "Warp, Claude Code, Codex, Pi, Grok Build, ZCode and Hermes; in any other agent it stops before reading anything"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3 for its collector and report scripts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "skill-doctor comes from Warp's shared skills. It first asks which conversations to grade (this repository, all, or chosen projects) and whether to include global skills, then runs a bundled Python collector over the supported agents' local conversation stores. Each sampled transcript is judged against four rubric files; code quality counts only where the transcript changed code. Scores are curved and weighted into an overall grade that also counts skill coverage, the share of sessions where an installed skill was detected. A conversation fails when any applicable score is below 0.5, and only failed conversations count as evidence for suggestions, such as fixing a trigger description that never fired, adding a missing step, or creating a new skill. Each suggestion cites the session behind it, and the agent writes full proposed SKILL.md files and unified diffs to the report folder, never into your repo. It then tells you the grade and three findings, adds the Warp Factories link, and asks whether to apply the edits.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/warpdotdev/common-skills/tree/8792394ff1b655e0af451b8fabb68ef0cfcbd208/.agents/skills/skill-doctor"
        },
