          ],
          "text": "The YAML spec is the source of truth: Mermaid, CSV, config files, plain descriptions and imported .drawio files all become YAML before rendering, so edits happen on the spec and the diagram is regenerated. The skill routes each request to one of 19 paths, such as create, edit, replicate a screenshot, network topology, cloud and vendor stencils, formulas or edge audits, and loads only that path's references. Rendering runs offline through its bundled CLI, with validation that reports overlaps, edge crossings and avoidable bends; connectors are bound edges with open arrowheads by default. Themes and palettes carry colorblind and grayscale safety flags, and it asks about palettes only when color comes up. Cloud, Kubernetes and Cisco icons are checked against a bundled catalog first. It inspects the exported PNG itself before claiming completion and ends with a report of files, commands and checks. A live browser-refinement backend through an MCP server is optional; offline authoring never needs it.",
