      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns books and documents, from PDF and EPUB to Markdown, into an agent skill of the author's frameworks, principles, techniques and anti-patterns.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want an agent to apply a book's frameworks while you work, or to study and look up its chapters later"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Extracts the text with a bundled Python script, estimates the token cost, then writes chapter summaries, a glossary, patterns and a decision cheatsheet"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A new skill folder, by default in ~/.agents/skills with a Claude Code symlink, holding SKILL.md, chapters/, glossary.md, patterns.md and cheatsheet.md"
            },
            {
              "label": "Modes",
              "text": "Full conversion, analyze only, generate from an earlier analysis, or fold new sources into an existing book skill"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks",
              "text": "Whether the content is technical or prose, what the skill should help you do, its name, and to confirm the cost estimate"
            },
            {
              "label": "Publishes",
              "text": "Only if you agree, to a private GitHub repo unless you reply with the bare word \"public\" and may redistribute the content"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It extracts structure rather than summaries: named frameworks in the author's exact wording, actionable principles, step-by-step techniques, anti-patterns and the author's voice. Inputs can be one or many files, folders or globs in PDF, EPUB, DOCX, HTML, Markdown, plain text, RTF, or MOBI and AZW through Calibre. Technical mode tries Docling for layout-aware PDF extraction; text mode uses the fastest extractor. For books over about 50,000 tokens it pulls chapters with grep and sed instead of reading the whole text. Chapter files hold a core idea, frameworks, mental models and takeaways, plus code and tables for technical books, with depth set by whether you want study or reference. The cheatsheet holds decision rules, trade-offs and thresholds rather than definitions, and the master SKILL.md stays under 4,000 tokens with chapter and topic indexes. Before reporting success it runs a bundled security scan of the generated skill and stops for a human if it flags anything. It picks the right skill folder for GitHub Copilot CLI, Amp, Claude Code, Codex, Hermes Agent, OpenCode or OpenClaw.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/virgiliojr94/book-to-skill/tree/e7bb659d3261491c8b28793dcb9102fa64a46c22"
        },
