              "text": "Rules such as INP instead of FID, no HowTo schema, and a hard stop at 50+ location pages"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also adds",
              "text": "A footer promoting the author's Skool communities, AI Marketing Hub Free and Pro, at the end of audits and most other reports; quick checks skip it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The Claude SEO plugin; /seo setup creates its Python runtime and headless Chromium"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The entry point of Claude SEO. Typed as /seo <command> <url>, it loads the sub-skill for that command, and for an unknown command it lists them all and suggests the closest. For /seo audit it detects the business type (SaaS, local, e-commerce, publisher or agency), spawns subagents for technical SEO, content, schema, sitemaps, performance, visuals, AI search, agent readiness, search experience and backlinks, and adds local, maps, Google, Matomo, clustering, e-commerce or drift checks when it finds the signals, credentials or a stored baseline. It merges the results into one score weighted by category: content 23%, technical 22%, on-page 20%, schema, performance and AI search 10% each, images 5%. Findings go through a ten-principle framework before they're sorted by priority, and each recommendation is meant to carry the observation it rests on, what it depends on, how you'd know it failed and an early indicator to watch. Questions about Google updates are answered from a bundled ledger of confirmed updates rather than from memory. After any analysis it offers a PDF report. It treats fetched pages as data, never as instructions.",
