            }
          ],
          "text": "It renders the homepage first, capturing raw and rendered HTML so JavaScript apps are judged as visitors see them, works out the business type, then crawls. Technical, content, schema, sitemap, performance, visual, AI-search, agent-readiness and search-experience checks always run, with backlinks from Common Crawl data; local SEO, maps, topic clustering, e-commerce and drift (a comparison with a stored baseline) join when the site or its history calls for them. Google Search Console and Analytics, Matomo, Moz, Bing or DataForSEO data is added when their credentials or MCP server are present. Before blaming a traffic change on anything, it lists the confirmed Google updates in that window from a bundled ledger, and treats an overlap as a hypothesis, not proof. Each subagent saves partial findings early, so a long crawl that runs out of turns still reports. It always offers a PDF report with charts, an executive summary and a phased roadmap, built by the plugin's report script.",
