              "text": "COMPARISON-PAGE.md with sections and an outline of at least 1,500 words, comparison-schema.json, and a keyword strategy"
            },
            {
              "label": "Holds to",
              "text": "Claims verifiable from public sources, dated prices, your affiliation disclosed, and competitors' strengths acknowledged"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The four page types are head-to-head \"X vs Y\" pages, \"alternatives to X\" lists, \"best [category] tools\" roundups and comparison tables of several products. For each it gives keyword patterns such as \"is A better than B\" or \"A vs B pricing\", title formulas with the year, and where calls to action go: above the fold, after the table and at the end, but not inside competitor descriptions, where they cost trust. Schema comes as Product with AggregateRating, SoftwareApplication or ItemList JSON-LD. Its fairness rules forbid unverifiable or misleading claims about competitors, ask for a source link per competitor data point and \"as of [date]\" on prices, and mark missing data \"Not publicly available\" rather than guessing. It also plans internal links between related comparisons and suggests new comparison pages worth building. Unlike seo-programmatic from the same repo, which plans many pages from one template, it shapes individual comparison pages.",
