          "text": "Weights are Business Profile signals 25%, reviews 20%, local on-page SEO 20%, NAP and citations 15%, schema 10%, and links and authority 10%. Detection decides the checks: a service-area business skips address and map checks, and restaurants, healthcare, legal, home services, real estate and automotive get their own schema types and directories. Location pages face a swap test: if the city name could be swapped and the text still made sense, it's a doorway page. It flags review gating as prohibited, checks Yelp and BBB listings with site: searches, and puts claiming Apple and Bing listings first among its quick wins, saying Bing Places feeds ChatGPT, Copilot and Alexa and ChatGPT doesn't read Google's profiles. Checks come with ranking-factor figures from studies such as Whitespark's. The report ends with the top 10 actions by priority and what it couldn't measure, such as live map pack positions, with the paid tools that could. With DataForSEO connected it pulls live listings and local pack positions.",
