        "updated": "2026-11-11",
        "skew": 77
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Detects, validates and generates Schema.org JSON-LD for a page, and flags structured data types Google has retired.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want rich results, or need to know whether a page's structured data is valid"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Finds JSON-LD, Microdata and RDFa, checks required properties and common errors, and writes markup for the page type"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "SCHEMA-REPORT.md with a status per block, and generated-schema.json with ready-to-use JSON-LD"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps current",
              "text": "Never recommends HowTo or other retired types, and flags existing FAQPage markup only as Info, since Google dropped FAQ rich results"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Detection flags any block without @context or @type, since Google can't attach it to anything. Validation catches invalid types, wrong data types, placeholder text, relative URLs and bad dates. Its status list, checked in October 2026, sorts types into active, no rich results but worth keeping, deprecated with dates (HowTo, SpecialAnnouncement, ClaimReview for search and others), and still supported despite earlier notices, such as Book Actions. Generated markup uses only truthful data, with clear placeholders for you to fill, and review markup refuses fake or undisclosed incentivized reviews. Time-sensitive Product and Offer markup belongs in the server-rendered HTML rather than injected by JavaScript. It recommends JSON-LD as the main format and includes Organization, LocalBusiness and Article templates.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/tree/6be93f45064ffbadced572b5d5c95f55fd263af0/skills/seo-schema"
        },
        "tags": [
