        "updated": "2026-11-11",
        "skew": 544
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews one URL's titles, headings, content, metadata, schema and images, and returns a score card with prioritized fixes.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want one page checked in depth, such as a pricing or landing page"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks title and description length, headings, links, content quality, canonical and robots tags, social preview tags, schema and images"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An overall score with sub-scores for on-page, content, technical, schema and images, issues by priority, and JSON-LD for missing schema"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike seo-audit",
              "text": "This one stays on one URL"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Beyond length targets (titles of 50-60 characters, descriptions of 150-160), it runs a plugin script that catches templated metadata: a description that opens by repeating its title and closes on a stock call to action, the shape bulk generators leave across a site. Keyword use is judged as natural language, with no density target. Images are checked for alt text, size (a warning over 200 KB, critical over 500 KB), modern formats, dimensions and lazy loading, without faulting JavaScript lazy-loaders that drop the native attribute on purpose. Core Web Vitals can't be measured from HTML, so it only flags likely causes, such as huge hero images or render-blocking resources. With DataForSEO connected it adds live rankings and backlink data.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/tree/6be93f45064ffbadced572b5d5c95f55fd263af0/skills/seo-page"
