    {
      "id": "AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/skills/seo-plan",
      "name": "seo-plan",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/agricidaniel/claude-seo/seo-plan",
        "installs": 7600,
        "weeklyInstalls": [241, 221, 218, 226, 246, 253, 336, 310],
        "firstSeen": "2026-02-10"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "734998e5fdbb16cd96dbaafe2da24eee6fb0d291",
        "updated": "2026-11-11",
        "skew": 2
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes an SEO strategy for a new or existing site: competitor analysis, site structure, content calendar and a 12-month roadmap.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're starting SEO for a site, or need a plan rather than a list of fixes"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Starts from your business, audience, competitors, goals and budget, studies five competitors, then designs structure, content and technical foundations"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "SEO-STRATEGY.md, COMPETITOR-ANALYSIS.md, CONTENT-CALENDAR.md, IMPLEMENTATION-ROADMAP.md and SITE-STRUCTURE.md, with KPI targets at 3, 6 and 12 months"
            },
            {
              "label": "Templates",
              "text": "SaaS, local service, e-commerce, publisher, agency or a generic business"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The roadmap runs in four phases: foundation in weeks 1-4 (technical setup, core pages, essential schema, analytics), expansion in weeks 5-12 (content, a blog, internal links, local SEO), scale in weeks 13-24 (link building, AI search optimization, performance) and authority in months 7-12 (thought leadership, PR, advanced schema). Competitor analysis covers content strategy, schema, technical setup, keyword gaps and E-E-A-T signals (Google's experience, expertise, authoritativeness and trust criteria). Without a URL it plans a new site and skips the gap analysis. With DataForSEO connected it uses real competitor, traffic and keyword data. Its strategy file can seed seo-cluster from the same repo, which imports the plan's keywords into topic clusters.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/tree/6be93f45064ffbadced572b5d5c95f55fd263af0/skills/seo-plan"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:marketing",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "seo",
          "marketing"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/skills/seo-cluster",
      "name": "seo-cluster",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/agricidaniel/claude-seo/seo-cluster",
        "installs": 7600,
        "weeklyInstalls": [292, 329, 287, 258, 276, 271, 389, 322],
        "firstSeen": "2026-04-15"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "734998e5fdbb16cd96dbaafe2da24eee6fb0d291",
        "updated": "2026-11-11",
        "skew": 2
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Groups keywords by how many Google results they share and designs pillar-and-spoke content clusters with an internal link plan.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a seed keyword and want to know which articles to write and how they should link"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Expands the seed to 30-50 keywords, searches pairs and counts shared top-10 results: 7+ means one post, 4-6 the same cluster"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "cluster-plan.json and cluster-plan.md, an interactive cluster-map.html, and a link matrix giving every post at least three internal links"
            },
            {
              "label": "Then",
              "text": "/seo cluster execute writes the posts with claude-blog's blog-write skill if installed, or saves one brief per post"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike grouping by wording",
              "text": "This one groups keywords the way Google ranks them, not by similar wording"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Keywords come from related searches, People Also Ask questions, modifiers such as \"best\" or \"vs\", and question variants; navigational ones such as brand names are dropped. To save searches it pre-groups by intent and only cross-checks boundary pairs. A plan has one pillar page of 2,500-4,000 words and two to five clusters of two to four spoke posts of 1,200-1,800 words, each with a template chosen by intent, such as how-to, comparison or best-of, and no two posts sharing a primary keyword. Spokes and pillar link both ways with keyword anchors. It can import keywords from a seo-plan strategy file instead of a seed. Execution writes the pillar first, then spokes by search volume, fills in links back as posts appear, resumes where it stopped and ends with a scorecard on coverage, link density, orphan pages and keyword overlap. With DataForSEO it uses live search data, checking the cost before each batch and asking you when it needs approval.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/tree/6be93f45064ffbadced572b5d5c95f55fd263af0/skills/seo-cluster"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:marketing",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "by:community",
          "seo",
          "marketing",
          "needs:claude-code"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/skills/seo-programmatic",
      "name": "seo-programmatic",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/agricidaniel/claude-seo/seo-programmatic",
        "installs": 7400,
        "weeklyInstalls": [241, 218, 218, 214, 232, 247, 326, 305],
        "firstSeen": "2026-02-19"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "734998e5fdbb16cd96dbaafe2da24eee6fb0d291",
        "updated": "2026-11-11",
        "skew": 2
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Plans and audits pages generated at scale from data, with quality gates against thin content, templated pages and index bloat.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're building or auditing hundreds of pages from one template, such as location, integration or glossary pages"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Assesses the data source, template uniqueness, URL patterns, internal linking, canonicals, sitemaps and noindex rules"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A programmatic SEO score out of 100 across six areas, with issues from critical to backlog"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stops at",
              "text": "500+ pages without justification or under 30% unique content, until you approve; it warns at 100+ unreviewed pages"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It treats Google's scaled content abuse policy as the main risk. Each page should pass a standalone value test (would it be worth publishing if no similar pages existed?) and have at least 30-40% unique content against every other page in the set, measured on body copy with shared navigation excluded. It recommends human review of 5-10% of generated pages and publishing in batches of 50-100, watching indexing and rankings for 2-4 weeks before expanding. Metadata is checked separately by a plugin script, so a set whose titles and descriptions all share one generated shape fails even when the body copy passes. It lists page types that are safe at scale, such as integration pages with real setup docs or glossary entries of 200+ words, and ones that risk penalties, such as location pages that only swap the city. It also covers hub pages, breadcrumbs, related-item links, canonical rules and keeping noindexed pages out of sitemaps.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/claude-seo/tree/6be93f45064ffbadced572b5d5c95f55fd263af0/skills/seo-programmatic"
        },
