              "text": "A store's Universal Commerce Protocol profile at /.well-known/ucp, the open standard that lets AI agents buy from merchants"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Product pages are weighted schema completeness 25%, images and content 20% each, title and meta 15%, internal linking and technical 10% each. The checklist asks for titles under 60 characters with the brand, meta descriptions under 155 with a price and a call to action, one H1, at least three images with descriptive alt text and file names, breadcrumbs, a unique description of at least 200 words, a specs table and reviews on the page. Product schema needs a name, an image and an Offer with a price above zero, and scores from 50 for those fields to 100 with ratings, product identifiers, shipping, a return policy and three reviews; fake or undisclosed incentivized reviews are ruled out. Price analysis gives the median, quartiles and outliers more than two standard deviations out. Keyword gaps fall into four types, each with an action, such as a Merchant Center feed for keywords that only rank organically. Given a category page or homepage, it runs the store-level checks and asks for a product URL. Pages are fetched and parsed by the Claude SEO plugin's scripts.",
