      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Checks whether a page is the type Google rewards for its keyword, then scores it against personas and user stories drawn from search results.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A page is technically sound but won't rank, and you suspect it's the wrong kind of page for what searchers want"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Classifies the top 10 results by page type, finds the dominant one and flags a mismatch with your page, from aligned to critical"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An SXO report: the results landscape, a page-type verdict, 3-5 user stories, an SXO Gap Score out of 100, persona cards and priority actions"
            },
            {
              "label": "SXO means",
              "text": "Search experience optimization: whether a page fits what Google rewards and what the searcher needs, scored apart from the SEO Health Score"
            },
            {
              "label": "Wireframe",
              "text": "/seo sxo wireframe outlines the page as it is and as it should be, as HTML sections with concrete placeholders"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike the bundle's audits",
              "text": "The bundle's technical and content audits check a page on its own; this one judges the page against what ranks now"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A blog post up against product pages is a critical mismatch, and the advice is a dedicated product page; when no type dominates, it notes room to stand out. Consensus is strong above 60% of results, mixed at 40 to 60% and fragmented below. User stories come from People Also Ask questions, ad copy, related searches, featured snippets and AI Overviews, in the form \"As a…, I want to…, because…, but I'm blocked by…\". The gap score gives page type, content depth, UX signals, schema, media and authority 15 points each and freshness 10. Four to seven personas each get 25 points for relevance, clarity, trust and action, and recommendations start with the weakest persona. If you give no keyword, it takes one from the overlap of the title and H1. The page is rendered and parsed with the plugin's scripts, and results come from web search, or from DataForSEO after a cost estimate you confirm. A limitations section says what it couldn't assess.",
