            {
              "label": "Prints",
              "text": "An attribution line for the framework, licensed CC BY 4.0, before every run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps current",
              "text": "/seo flow sync pulls the latest prompts from the FLOW GitHub repo through the plugin's sync script"
            }
          ],
          "text": "FLOW is an SEO framework by the plugin's author, published separately under CC BY 4.0, and this skill carries its 41 prompts. With no stage named, it shows the stages and asks which fits your situation. For optimize, it picks 2 or 3 of the 21 prompts by your industry (SaaS leans to on-page and technical, local businesses to citations and Business Profile, publishers to E-E-A-T and freshness), by what other Claude SEO skills found earlier in the conversation, and by the kind of URL, and says why it chose them. Local prompts cover Business Profile optimization, title tags, meta descriptions and local audits. Each stage ends by pointing to the skill that goes deeper, such as seo-cluster after find or seo-sxo after win. /seo flow prompts lists every prompt with its stage and when to use it.",
