      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "7f8ae3435e5bc68a54efdca9f67797e905845562",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Hands a bounded coding task to the OpenAI Codex CLI, then reviews its diff, re-runs your checks and commits the work itself.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want Codex to write the code for a task, or a queue of tasks, while your main agent stays the reviewer"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Writes a self-contained brief, runs Codex through a bundled relay script, then re-runs your project's tests and lint and reads the diff against the brief"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Verified changes committed by your main agent, plus a result.json with Codex's report, the files it touched and the session id for follow-up fixes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike codex-rescue",
              "text": "That one, the openai-codex plugin's agent, forwards one task and returns the output; this one reviews and lands each result itself"
            },
            {
              "label": "Second opinions",
              "text": "A read-only run asks Codex to defend or concede each contested point without touching files"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The codex CLI signed in, Node 18+ and git"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Your main agent is the orchestrator and Codex is the implementer. Codex sees only the brief, so the brief carries the goal, the current state, what to change and what to leave alone, the project's real check commands taken from CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md or the Makefile, and a report format, and it tells Codex not to commit. The bundled relay.mjs wraps codex exec in a write-capable workspace sandbox, keeps its artifacts in a temp folder and blocks until Codex finishes, so Claude Code runs it in the background. The agent then distrusts Codex's self-report: it re-runs the checks, reads the diff for scope creep or gaps, round-trips migrations and greps for dangling references after removals. Only then does it commit. Rework goes back to the same Codex session as a short delta brief. It reports Codex's design choices instead of silently keeping them, and stops to ask before going beyond the brief. Flags add a time limit, web search or network access inside the sandbox.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/amelnagdy/delegate-skills/tree/7f8ae3435e5bc68a54efdca9f67797e905845562/skills/codex-delegate"
        },
