            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js for the player's dev server and a browser to inspect frames; with no player project it downloads one with npx degit"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Text-to-lottie pairs this skill with a local player built on Skia's Skottie renderer, where each animation is a scene at public/projects/<project>/<scene>/lottie.json, which the player's scene list picks up as soon as it is written. The skill reads only the references the task needs: one primary recipe, such as logo, typography, loaders and icons, SVG animation, camera moves, diagrams, data and stats, product promos or visual effects, plus guides to motion and design taste. It asks only when the answer changes the output, such as a transparent or full-frame background, brand constraints or supplied assets. It picks the target scene by authority, a file path first, then a browser route, then a known scene, otherwise a new one, and overwrites the starter scene only while it is still the untouched placeholder. Important values become slots with labelled controls. Native text renders when the scene ships its font file. Before finishing it validates the JSON, confirms the player lists the scene, and checks the first, middle and last frames for a blank canvas, missing assets, wrong layer order, bad easing, cropping and text overflow.",
