          "text": "A thin client for text-to-video and image-to-video generation. The agent first chooses the mode: a description alone becomes text-to-video, and a request to animate or move an image becomes image-to-video, which needs a public image URL. It rewrites the prompt to be specific about motion, such as a slow camera zoom or a character walking left to right, with reference files for prompt patterns and per-model details. It then runs tools/generate.js with the mode, prompt, duration and aspect ratio (16:9, 9:16, 1:1, 4:3 or 3:4), and optionally a model; the script returns JSON with the video URL, which the agent passes on. Other commands list the proxy's models and check an asynchronous job's status. All calls go through a hosted proxy, so by default there are no API keys to set up; environment variables point it at your own proxy or add a token.",
