      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Researches a question across many sources and writes a cited report in Markdown, HTML and PDF, with every claim checked against stored evidence.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A question needs many sources weighed, such as a technology comparison, market analysis or state-of-the-art review, not a quick lookup"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Scopes and plans the question, searches in parallel with 3 to 5 subagents, triangulates sources, drafts section by section and verifies each claim"
            },
            {
              "label": "Modes",
              "text": "Quick (3 phases), standard (6, the default), deep (8) and ultradeep (8 or more), from a few minutes to about 45"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A folder in ~/Documents with the report as Markdown, McKinsey-style HTML and PDF, both opened for you, plus source, evidence and claim ledgers and a run manifest"
            },
            {
              "label": "Report",
              "text": "Executive summary, 4 to 8 cited findings, synthesis, limitations, recommendations, a complete bibliography and a methodology appendix"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Subagents for parallel retrieval and WeasyPrint for the PDF; its makers' search-cli is optional, with the agent's web search as fallback"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A research pipeline that works on its own: it infers assumptions from context and states the important ones in the report's introduction instead of asking. Simple lookups and debugging are sent elsewhere. Retrieval, outlining, drafting and claim checks run as a loop per section: each source gets a stable ID in sources.jsonl, each quote and its location is appended to evidence.jsonl, and each factual claim in claims.jsonl must be supported before delivery. It aims for 10 or more sources and 3 independent ones per major claim, cites every factual claim inline, writes at least 80% prose and allows no placeholders or invented citations. Deep and ultradeep modes add a critique and a refinement pass. Bundled Python scripts validate the report and its citations and convert Markdown to HTML. Reports over 18,000 words follow a continuation procedure.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/199-biotechnologies/claude-deep-research-skill/tree/f2f2c0fa4e7617ca84c86b63f4bb40f77a746933"
