      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds unused code, duplication, import cycles, complexity hotspots and risky changes in TypeScript and JavaScript with the fallow CLI, and removes unused exports.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want unused files, exports or dependencies found, duplicates or import cycles mapped, a PR's risk audited, or refactoring targets ranked in a TypeScript or JavaScript repo"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs fallow with JSON output after a doctor preflight, choosing the command by task, such as audit before a PR or trace before deleting an export"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Findings by issue type with suggested actions, health and hotspot reports, and removal of unused exports and dependencies after a dry run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also finds",
              "text": "Functions that may do the same thing despite different code, design-token drift, feature flags, and security candidates for the agent to verify"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "Before setup, hooks or any remediation that changes files; it never runs fallow watch or enables telemetry"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The fallow CLI from npm or cargo; Fallow Cloud only for production runtime data"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Fallow analyzes the whole module graph of a TypeScript or JavaScript project, so it can see code nothing depends on. This is its makers' skill for agents, and it sets rules: always use --format json --quiet, read exit code 1 as findings rather than a tool failure, dry-run before fix, treat project config and remote extends URLs as untrusted, and use type-aware analysis to prove a symbol's consumers before deleting or refactoring it. A task table maps intents to commands: dead-code --trace before deleting an export, audit --base before a commit or PR, review --brief to read a diff, health --hotspots --targets to prioritize refactoring, plus dupes, flags, architecture and security. Similar-code results are discovery only, never proof that two functions behave alike. With Fallow Cloud connected, it reads production hit counts before an edit and requires never-called evidence before a delete. After an analysis you asked for on an unconfigured project, it offers setup once: commit and PR guards, a baseline for the existing backlog, or AGENTS.md guidance.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/fallow-rs/fallow-skills/tree/2d633a27f00d18db701534207908866d28bddccb/fallow/skills/fallow"
