      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds and maintains a personal Markdown wiki, compiling the sources you add into cited articles and answering questions from them.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a personal knowledge base that grows as you add articles, papers or pages, and answers from what you've collected"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Saves each source's original text under raw/, never edited afterwards, then writes or updates topic articles under wiki/, with an index and a log"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A folder of Markdown articles in which every number, date and quote can be found in a saved source"
            },
            {
              "label": "Three jobs",
              "text": "Ingest a source, answer questions from the wiki, and lint it for broken links, contradictions and facts it can't trace"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3 for the lint step's evidence check"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Based on Andrej Karpathy's idea of a wiki the LLM writes and keeps while you read it and ask questions. Ingest fetches a source into raw/<topic>/, which is never edited afterwards, then decides whether it's new, updates an article, contradicts one, or adds nothing, in which case it's kept and logged with no article. Compiling merges into an article with the same thesis or creates one, then searches the rest of the wiki for articles the source affects. Claims a newer source replaces or disputes stay, marked Outdated or Disputed, instead of being rewritten. Before writing a number, date or quote, the agent must find it in the raw file and copy it exactly; the skill calls this its grounding invariant. Query reads the index, searches the wiki and answers with links to articles, writing nothing unless you ask to archive the answer as a page. Lint fixes index entries and broken links itself, runs a bundled script that checks facts against the raw files, and only reports contradictions, orphan pages and missing cross-references. A research mode gathers several sources on a topic, deliberately including ones that argue the other side.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/astro-han/karpathy-llm-wiki/tree/eafcc77001e496cc43499e4923b663aec722c813"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:documents",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "notes",
          "research"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
