          "text": "Guidance from Resend for email that gets delivered, stays legal and is easy to read. A quick-reference table points the agent to eleven reference files: deliverability (SPF, DKIM, DMARC and spam fixes), transactional emails such as password resets and one-time codes, a catalog of the emails an app typically needs, email capture and validation, newsletters and promotions, CAN-SPAM, GDPR and CASL compliance, telling transactional from marketing email, retries and idempotent sending, delivery webhooks, bounce and complaint handling with suppression lists, and accessibility (lang and dir, presentational tables, headings, alt text, title and contrast). It also lays out paths through them: for spam problems, check authentication first, since Gmail and Yahoo reject unauthenticated mail; for marketing email, collect consent, check the legal requirements, then send; for production sending, add retries and idempotency, then webhooks to track delivery, then bounce handling.",
