          "text": "Billions Network's skill for \"Know Your Agent\": giving an AI agent a decentralized identifier (DID), an identity based on the iden3 protocol, that can be tied to a real person. A short router sends the agent to one of two references. Identity covers creating an Ethereum-based DID or importing a private key, listing local identities, linking the agent to its owner through the Billions ERC-8004 registry and an attestation registry that checks the person is unique, signing a challenge to prove ownership, and verifying someone else's DID by sending them a challenge and checking their signed token. x402 covers servers that answer 402 Payment Required: a first script call fetches the resource and lists payment options without signing; the agent shows what you'd pay for, the amount, asset and network, and links to any attestations you still need; only after you choose does a second call sign the payment and retry the request. Strict rules apply throughout: check that an identity exists first, stop on any script error, and never generate keys or edit the identity files by hand.",
