          "text": "A design workflow built to escape the familiar look of AI-made design. One author works from the subject, its language, place, people and purpose, and may not look at other designers, templates, design systems or font catalogues for inspiration. From a one-line purpose statement, usually with no questions first, it writes ten independent directions as dependency-free HTML pages: only words, fonts, sizes, spacing, flat text and background colors, and whitespace, with no shapes, images, icons or effects, and across the set at least one direction each with one, two, three and four text colors. Each gets a concept capsule recording its fonts, colors and rules, shown only after your first reaction. You open the pages and react before seeing any rationale, and can reject all ten and ask for another ten as often as you like. Praise doesn't lock a direction; you have to say so. Once you do, the other nine are dropped, the capsule goes into ROUND-2-CONTEXT.md, and Round 2 builds the real pieces, such as components and screens, a campaign family or publication spreads, where shapes, imagery and motion may enter. After you approve them, it writes an HTML style guide with prompts for asking for more.",
