          "text": "Instead of answering from its own knowledge, the agent queries NotebookLM, Google's notebook tool that answers from documents you upload. Bundled Python scripts do the work, run through a wrapper that creates a virtual environment and installs the dependencies and a browser on first use. You log in to Google once, by hand, in a visible window, and the session is saved for later questions. The browser runs through patchright, a Playwright fork built to evade bot detection, and a stealth setting, on in the sample config, types at human speed. You keep a library of notebooks, each saved with its URL, name, description and topics; when you add one without details, the agent first asks the notebook what it covers. Each question opens a fresh browser session, gets the answer and closes, so nothing carries over and the agent puts the context into each question. Every answer ends by asking whether that's all you need, and the agent is told to compare it with your request, ask follow-ups until nothing is missing, then combine the answers. You still upload documents to NotebookLM yourself.",
