          "text": "Its premise: a model's first three answers are the ones a senior engineer gives in thirty seconds, correct and forgettable. It splits the work into two phases. To diverge, it picks five of fifteen frames, such as hardware engineer, 10-year-old, attacker, ant colony or a $0, one-hour budget, and gives each to its own subagent, in parallel and with no shared context, forbidden to evaluate or give the obvious answers. To focus, the main agent scores every idea for novelty, viability and fit, flags traps such as hidden costs or premature abstraction, groups the ideas into three to six clusters by their underlying angle, and sends the top three non-traps to new subagents for a sketch, the load-bearing risk, a first step and child ideas. The reply follows a fixed order: a brief, the full set with score chips, a shortlist with the non-obvious pick starred and the traps listed, the three deepened branches, and a closing provocation. Unless you call it, it answers directly when a question has one canonical answer, low stakes, or words like \"just\" or \"textbook\".",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/uditakhourii/adhd/tree/47beee24e4842fb748bd30c55e66ae77d6bb22f9/skills/adhd"
        },
