          "text": "Sanity's guide to optimizing for classic search engines (SEO) and for AI answer engines (AEO), which pick one source to quote rather than ranking pages. The SKILL.md defines both and EEAT, Google's framework of experience, expertise, authoritativeness and trustworthiness, then sends the agent to one of four references. Technical SEO covers titles, meta descriptions, Open Graph, sitemaps, canonical URLs, redirects, performance, robots.txt and hreflang. Structured data gives JSON-LD patterns for articles, FAQs, organizations, products and breadcrumbs, combined in one @graph, with testing tools. EEAT covers showing who wrote a page, their credentials, dates and contact details, with a Sanity author schema. The AEO reference says to answer first and explain after, use question headings, lists, tables and FAQ pairs, keep content fresh and cited, and decide deliberately whether GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot and Google-Extended may crawl, since blocking them keeps content out of AI training but may cost citations. Code examples use Sanity schemas, GROQ and Next.js.",
