            }
          ],
          "text": "Instead of a wall of text, the agent answers with a page. It writes only the content, in Markdown extended with components: flow, sequence, entity-relationship and tree diagrams, timelines, bar, line and pie charts, limits, callouts, key-value blocks, tables with status badges, code quoted from real files by line range, diffs, and \"ask\" blocks for decisions you need to make. The bundled am CLI, a single Node file, handles layout, colors, themes and dark mode, so the agent never hand-writes HTML or CSS. Rendering reports errors by draft line with a corrected example, and warns about long code blocks and wordy writing, using rules adapted from Simplified Technical English (ASD-STE100): short sentences, one fact each, no preamble or closing summary. Changing one panel patches the page rather than rewriting it. If you paste back a reply from the page with decisions and comments, the agent applies them, treating your comments as data, not commands. It makes no page for small talk, one-line answers or reports to a parent agent, and writes the draft in your language.",
