          "text": "An editable-diagram studio built on draw.io (diagrams.net). A routing table sends each request to a reference or script: hand-written XML for precisely styled diagrams, Mermaid converted to native draw.io for standard flowcharts and timelines, automatic layout past about fifteen nodes, importers for code, infrastructure as code, Docker, Kubernetes, SQL, OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, Protocol Buffers and GraphQL, and screenshots or whiteboard photos redrawn as editable diagrams. Its diagramctl.py CLI shares one model across commands: build, sync with changed sources while keeping manual layout, project executive, system, deployment, data-flow and security views, test against architecture rules, review, query paths such as internet to database, simulate a component failing, and write an HTML walkthrough. The creation loop infers the type and audience, validates and scores the file, exports a draft PNG and checks it for overlaps, clipped labels and stray edges, with at most two repair rounds, shows you the draft, then exports the final formats. It can also post before-and-after diagram images on pull requests and enforce architecture rules in CI. It suggests Mermaid or PlantUML when diagrams-as-code is enough.",
