          "text": "Alibaba's skill for its open-source code review CLI, ocr. The agent first works out the business context of the change and passes it to the review as background. By default the review covers staged, unstaged and untracked changes; it can also take one commit or the diff between two refs. The result goes to a file the agent reads whole, since piping through head or tail would drop comments. Each comment carries a path, line range, a category such as bug, security or performance, a severity and often suggested code. The agent reports critical, high and medium findings in a fixed template, locates the code itself when a comment couldn't be placed, and applies safe fixes only with your go-ahead. Project rules live in .opencodereview/rule.json in the repo or your home folder, matched by file pattern, replacing or adding to the built-in ones. Other options exclude paths, cap the token budget, switch model for one run, resume an interrupted review, or output JSON or SARIF for code-scanning tools.",
