          ],
          "text": "ECC's video skill treats AI as a way to compress real footage, not to generate it. It lays out six layers, each with one job. You capture with Screen Studio or a camera. The agent organizes: it transcribes, finds the strongest segments, dead air and repeated takes, writes an edit decision list of timestamps, and scaffolds the code. FFmpeg does the deterministic work: cuts by timestamp or from a cuts file, concatenation, proxies, audio extraction, loudness normalization, and scene and silence detection for auto-cuts. Remotion handles overlays, titles, lower thirds, animated stats and reusable scenes. Generated assets come last and only where footage is missing: ElevenLabs voiceover, music, sound effects or b-roll through the fal-ai-media skill, or VideoDB when it's configured. A person then sets pacing, cleans captions, grades color and mixes audio in Descript or CapCut. It also gives FFmpeg crops from 16:9 to 9:16 and 1:1, and asks the agent to save and verify a project checkpoint before and after changing a live editor or DAW project.",
