              "label": "Examples in",
              "text": "TypeScript with Next.js, Supabase, Zod, DOMPurify and express-rate-limit, plus a Solana wallet section"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A checklist skill from ECC that comes into play when the agent touches security-sensitive code. Each of its ten sections pairs a FAIL and a PASS example with verification checkboxes: secrets in environment variables and out of git history; schema validation of every input and file upload; parameterized queries instead of string-built SQL; tokens in httpOnly cookies, authorization checks before sensitive operations and Supabase row level security; user HTML sanitized with DOMPurify and a strict Content Security Policy without unsafe-inline; CSRF tokens and SameSite cookies; rate limits, stricter on expensive endpoints; no passwords or card data in logs and no stack traces in error responses; Solana wallet-signature and transaction checks; and npm audit, committed lock files and Dependabot. It adds example tests for authentication, authorization, input validation and rate limiting, and a pre-deployment checklist that also covers HTTPS, security headers and CORS. It runs no scanner or tool of its own.",
