      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds an evidence-grounded 16-section deep-reading card for one scientific paper: methods, claim-evidence chains, limitations and testable research ideas.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to understand one paper's method, evidence and limits in depth, not translate it or review it formally"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Prepares the source with a bundled script, picks the paper type, inventories figures, experiments and limitations, then drafts and audits the card"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "paper-card.md with 16 fixed sections, from research question and method breakdown to evidence chain, critical analysis and research ideas, each point tied to its source"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike nature-reader",
              "text": "That one builds a full bilingual reader of the paper; this one can start from a nature-reader source map"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python for its scripts, and the repo's nature-shared package"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A deep-reading skill from the Nature skills repo. It first works out what it has: a full paper, text without reliable layout, only an abstract, or an existing nature-reader artifact, and makes a visibly partial card when material is missing. For a PDF or source map it must run its bundled preparation script, which sets one of three grounding modes: page-grounded, with real PDF page numbers; structure-grounded, citing sections, figures and tables; or source-limited, for an abstract or excerpt. It never invents page numbers. It picks one paper type, methods, discovery, resource, clinical, materials or review, with a second lens only for a genuine hybrid, and applies that type's checks. Before drafting it inventories the metadata, contribution, method components, every main figure and table, experiments, baselines and author-stated limitations, and links each central claim to its evidence. Web search is used only for background, knowledge connections, bibliographic checks or a novelty check. Unsupported sections say Not applicable or Not assessable, and research ideas are framed as hypotheses. A bundled auditor checks the card before delivery, and its errors block it. The card follows your language.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/yuan1z0825/nature-skills/tree/d774add241c65e89ed17a4da573b472b0972fd42/skills/nature-paper-card"
