            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Through its own bundled Python CLI, with pages dispatched to parallel workers when there are several"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3.10 or newer, and LibreOffice on Linux or macOS or PowerPoint on Windows for its rendered checks; a PaddleOCR token and an image model are optional"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A self-contained reconstruction tool from the Nature skills repo, run entirely through its bundled Python CLI and its own reference contracts. A doctor check comes first and must pass. OCR uses Baidu AI Studio's PaddleOCR when a token is configured; otherwise a local fallback measures where text sits without recognizing the characters, and it tells you so. prepare sets up one run with a job record per page; the agent then reconstructs a single page itself or dispatches page workers for a multi-page deck. Structured pages are planned as semantic regions. Measured circles, cards, lines and connectors become native objects, an arrow is always one connector or one Arrow shape, and only bounded complex subparts become transparent images, made with the agent's own image tool or, failing that, Codex OAuth or an OpenAI-compatible image API. A formula that fails to render fails the page unless you approve that exact omission. Every page is built, rendered and compared with its source in a visual-review record before it's accepted. Finalize rebuilds the deck from the page records, restores the speaker notes and reruns QA, and it won't call the deck complete while any check is pending or failed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/yuan1z0825/nature-skills/tree/d774add241c65e89ed17a4da573b472b0972fd42/skills/nature-image2ppt"
