      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes or updates a repo's AGENTS.md as a short, reference-backed file of verified commands and conventions, with CLAUDE.md symlinked to it.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're creating or updating a repo's AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md and want it short and accurate"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Inspects lock files, scripts, CI, docs and code conventions first, picks root or nested scope, writes the smallest useful file and checks every path and command exists"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An AGENTS.md under 60 lines, never over 100, of command tables, key conventions and pointers to existing docs, with CLAUDE.md as a symlink rather than a copy"
            },
            {
              "label": "Leaves out",
              "text": "Intros, rationale, quality slogans, restated linter config, lists of installed skills, and content copied from the README or CONTRIBUTING"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike claude-md-improver",
              "text": "That one, Anthropic's, grades existing CLAUDE.md files against a rubric; this one writes a minimal file from what the repo shows"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Sentry's skill for the instruction files coding agents read. Before writing, the agent inspects the package manager's lock files and manifests, the commands in package.json, Makefiles, task runners and CI workflows, the README, CONTRIBUTING, docs, specs and security policy, and the code's own conventions, generated files and legacy areas. Repo-wide defaults go in a root AGENTS.md; a nested file is added only where a subtree has different commands or rules, and stays shorter than the root. When a Claude-compatible entry point is needed, CLAUDE.md becomes a symlink, never a second copy that can drift. The file keeps only sections that add non-obvious value: the package manager, a table of file-scoped test and lint commands, a table naming the exact files for setup, architecture and policies, key conventions, and a commit-attribution line for AI commits. Its writing rules favor bullets and tables, one rule per bullet, repo-relative paths, and file-scoped commands over full builds.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/getsentry/skills/tree/e94f22214528d69899d09c627b3315ddc3544816/skills/agents-md"
        },
