          "text": "The main skill of CLI Printing Press, which drives its cli-printing-press generator. A preflight checks that the binary is installed and current, then it resolves the target from a name, URL, spec or HAR file and reuses earlier research when it's good enough. It writes a research brief and, when the docs fall short, offers to capture the site's hidden API in a browser, only with your consent, through browser-use, agent-browser, your Chrome via its extension, or a HAR you export. An absorb manifest then lists every feature of competing CLIs, MCP servers and skills, plus new ones a subagent proposes, for you to approve. It generates the Go code, builds every approved feature, runs shipcheck (dogfood, verify, skill and narrative checks and a scorecard), reviews the generated SKILL.md and README, has printing-press-output-review judge sampled command output, and runs a live test matrix against the real API, mandatory when you have a key. Every run calls printing-press-polish, then promotes the CLI to your library and archives the manuscripts. Secret values must never reach code, proofs or anything committed. The final menu offers publishing through printing-press-publish, another polish, or stopping.",
