          "text": "The last step of CLI Printing Press. It finds which CLI in your local library you mean, confirms its category, and runs the binary's publish validation: manifest provenance, live-test proof, go mod tidy, govulncheck, go vet, build, --help and --version, stopping on any failure. It won't rely on an old live test: it reruns the end-to-end gate against the real API on the exact tree it will publish, and asks before running destructive commands again. It then prepares a managed clone of the public library, forking it when needed, stages the CLI while keeping the library's existing release history, and scans for vendor tokens, your exact API key and personal data, redacting obvious tokens and asking about the rest. It never edits the registry, catalog or skill files the library regenerates after merge. Once the PR is open, it reads Greptile's summary and inline comments, fixes or answers every finding, waits for CI, and hands back without merging, since maintainers merge by hand. With --blocked-api-journal it instead adds a held API to blocked-apis.json.",
