          "text": "The quality pass of CLI Printing Press, which the printing-press skill runs on every generation and you can run yourself on a CLI in your library. It runs in a forked context, so its diagnostic noise stays out of the conversation that called it. First it compares your copy with any local clone of the public library and asks whether to sync when they differ. It builds the CLI, runs the press's dogfood, verify, workflow-verify, verify-skill and scorecard checks plus go vet and gosec, and asks the repo's printing-press-output-review skill for a plausibility review of the output. It then fixes issues in priority order: security static-analysis findings, verify failures, dead code, the CLI description and README, mismatches between the CLI and its SKILL.md, remaining dogfood issues, MCP tool quality and a customer-data check. It adds no features and doesn't touch the generator. A ship verdict needs at least 80% on verify and 75 on the scorecard with every hard gate clear; ship-with-gaps needs 65 and 65 and a Known Gaps section in the README. It is told never to add fake commands, tests or boilerplate just to raise a score.",
