          "text": "CLI Printing Press keeps your working copies in a local press library and published CLIs in the public mvanhorn/printing-press-library. This skill brings one back from the public side. It matches your argument, an API slug, a brand name like cal.com, an old -pp-cli name or something close, against the public registry, and asks you to pick when several match. If you already have a copy, it compares the run IDs and generation dates of both: for the same run or a newer public copy it asks before replacing yours; when yours is newer it stops, since you likely want to publish it first. It then fetches the CLI from GitHub, or from a local clone with --from-clone, zips a backup of whatever it would replace, reverses the publish step's module path rewrites and moves the result into place. Last, it checks that go.mod uses the local module path, that no source still points at the public one and that go build passes, and reports the run ID, manuscripts, backup and build status. When you came to polish a published CLI, it points you to printing-press-polish next.",
