          ],
          "text": "The feedback loop of CLI Printing Press, for the people who change the press: its generator, scorer, skills and binary. It picks the run from your manuscripts, gathers the research brief, absorb manifest, shipcheck proof, logs and generated CLI, and mines the session, live or from its saved transcript, for errors, manual edits, hand-built features, recurring friction and score penalties, checking penalties against the scorer's code first. Most candidates are meant to die in triage: iteration noise, fixes for one CLI, vendor API quirks, one-off observations and repeats of findings two earlier retros raised. A survivor must be evidenced in three named APIs and is ranked P1 (the printed CLI is broken or unsafe) or P2 (a generalizing defect in a working CLI), with no P3. The retro lists findings, skips, drops and what the press got right, and is scrubbed of secrets and personal data, stopping for hand redaction if a vendor token remains. On Submit it files each finding to act on as a public labelled issue on mvanhorn/cli-printing-press, or comments on a matching open one, and uploads scrubbed zips of the manuscripts and CLI source, and the retro itself, to catbox.moe, a public file host.",
