              "text": "Dimensions that need one show as N/A and leave the denominator instead of counting as zero"
            },
            {
              "label": "Changes",
              "text": "Nothing; printing-press-polish is the skill that fixes what the scorecard flags"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A read-only wrapper over the cli-printing-press scorecard command, which grades CLIs against what the press calls the Steinberger bar. With no argument it rescores the CLI of your current run, asking which when there are several; with a name it looks in your press library, also trying the -pp-cli suffix, then in past runs; with a path it scores that folder; with two names, as in \"notion-pp-cli-4 vs notion-pp-cli-2\", it scores both in parallel. It looks for the CLI's spec.json or the spec its run used, and scores without one when there is none. It renders Tier 1, twelve infrastructure dimensions out of 10 each, and Tier 2, six domain-correctness dimensions with type fidelity and dead code out of 5, then the total and grade, the gap report and a note on any unscored dimensions. A failed scorecard is reported with its full error output.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mvanhorn/cli-printing-press/tree/94ce80e35cbc516cbab1b80f54d96ca419958ca0/skills/printing-press-score"
