              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Only when printing-press or printing-press-polish calls it, in a forked context; it isn't offered as a slash command"
            },
            {
              "label": "Misses",
              "text": "Wrong numbers such as prices or ratings, stale data, matters of taste and commands that weren't sampled"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A plausibility check inside CLI Printing Press, for bugs a person would spot in five minutes with a printed CLI but that dogfood, verify and the scorecard's rules miss. It runs the scorecard's live check, which samples commands and records their redacted output, and returns SKIP without reviewing when that fails or no sample passed, since a skipped review is not a pass. A general-purpose subagent then reads the passing samples and the CLI's planned and built novel features from research.json, and may run more commands to confirm a finding. It checks four things: results match what the query meant, the output has no format bugs, commands that fan out to several sources show all of them or explain the missing ones, and rankings put a plausible best result first. Empty learning stores on a fresh print aren't flagged. Each finding comes back as a warning with a one-line description and a one-sentence fix; the calling skill logs them and you decide whether to fix before shipping. The forked context keeps the review's chatter out of the caller's conversation.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mvanhorn/cli-printing-press/tree/94ce80e35cbc516cbab1b80f54d96ca419958ca0/skills/printing-press-output-review"
