      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns friction you hit with a published Printing Press CLI, or your own asks, into a fix and a pull request to its library.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A published Printing Press CLI fell short while you used it, or you want its commands renamed, added or fixed"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Mines the Claude Code session transcript for friction or parses your typed asks, then plans, edits, validates and documents the fix"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An open pull request on mvanhorn/printing-press-library with a patch record, plus a plan and a list of deferred findings in your manuscripts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "To confirm the transcript, the scope (bugs, bugs and features, all, or your pick) and the PR draft before anything is pushed"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike printing-press-polish",
              "text": "That one improves a CLI before it's published; this one changes one already in the public library"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The cli-printing-press binary 4.0.0 or newer, Go and the GitHub CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Amend changes a CLI that's already in the public Printing Press library. In dogfood mode it confirms which session transcript to read, pulls out friction such as failed commands, hand-rolled API calls and missing flags, and classes each as a bug or a missing feature; in direct mode it turns asks like \"rename X\" or \"add these feeds\" into the same list, and on request sniffs the CLI's source site for new endpoints. It offers to skip findings that open or recently merged library PRs cover, and stops if the CLI binary you used is older than the published one. You pick the scope; deferred items are saved for a later run. It then edits the CLI in a managed clone of the library, records a patch file and runs publish validate up to three times, holding the work if it fails. User-facing changes must ship with README and SKILL.md updates. It asks whether a fix that belongs in the generator should wait for a retro, and a temporary patch gets a reused or new issue on mvanhorn/cli-printing-press. It scrubs credentials and stop-listed names, asks about other proper nouns, shows you the draft, then pushes and opens the PR.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mvanhorn/cli-printing-press/tree/94ce80e35cbc516cbab1b80f54d96ca419958ca0/skills/printing-press-amend"
