              "label": "Language",
              "text": "Instructions mostly in English, with some rules and the digest's fixed headings in Chinese"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A digest writer for WeChat groups, built on wx-cli, a separate command-line tool that reads WeChat's local data. On first run it asks for your WeChat ID and display name, the default version and where to save digests, and stores them in a preferences file. You name a group and a time range, or none, in which case it picks up where the last digest ended. It saves the messages to a temporary file and works in three rounds: a skeleton of every topic with who said what, the written digest, and an audit that greps each quote in the raw messages and fixes misattributions. It doesn't decode images, using a one-line description file only if you provide one. After saving, it updates history.json, an append-only log, each active member's profile, and memory.md, a file of facts members corrected so later digests don't repeat errors. Profiles leave out real names not used in the group, contact details, health and private family matters; the roast version also skips looks, family and identity. Questions members address to an @bot alias get their own section. It never installs wx-cli or runs sudo for you.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-wechat-summary"
