          "text": "A short cleanup pass. The agent checks the current branch's diff against main and removes what the branch introduced that reads as machine-written: comments that are unnecessary or don't match the file's style, defensive checks and try/catch blocks that are unusual for trusted code paths, casts to any that only get around type errors, deeply nested code that early returns would flatten, and other patterns out of keeping with the file and the codebase. It keeps behavior unchanged unless it's fixing a clear bug, prefers small focused edits to broad rewrites, and keeps its closing summary to one to three sentences.",
