      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "8a3bde8083bd121971f61cba4bdbe5fd8c0eee7d",
        "updated": "2026-11-10",
        "skew": 131
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Sets up, audits and fixes website conversion tracking for GA4, Google Ads, Meta and other ad platforms, and verifies test conversions arrive.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're setting up conversion tracking, or conversions stopped, double count, or GA4 and Google Ads disagree"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Settles what counts as a conversion, where it must land and what fires it, then builds the tracking or diagnoses the fault"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A GTM import file or snippet that fires on confirmed success, or an audit with every finding marked observed, reported or inferred"
            },
            {
              "label": "Insists on",
              "text": "A test conversion seen arriving at the platform before setup counts as done, or a named check for you to run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "Before firing a real test conversion or publishing a GTM container, and diagnoses before changing anything"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike analytics",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, plans events and UTMs; this one gets conversions to GA4 or ad platforms and proves they arrived"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It splits conversions into two kinds: lead generation (forms, bookings, chats, calls), where success often has to be detected in the browser and every form tool signals it differently, and ecommerce, where an order record exists and the hard parts are values, deduplication and refunds. Before asking you anything, it reads your product marketing context if you have it, the live page, the codebase or the GTM container. Setup finds the tool's real success signal, picks a delivery path (the platform's native integration first, then browser tags with hashed-email matching turned on, then server-side options, with prices, when you reach that choice), and builds it, generating one GTM import file with a bundled Python script for covered form tools. It ships paste-in success detectors for 22 lead-gen tools, plus patterns for phone-number clicks, downloads, thank-you pages and AJAX forms. Audits route on your symptom, check a calendar of dated platform changes such as Shopify's script removals, and treat a 10 to 30% gap between GA4 and Google Ads as normal. One server-side tool in its references is a partner of the repo, and the agent discloses that whenever it names it.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/96798cf38736ecdba015a1d2b0521b0c8f8f41dd/skills/conversion-tracking"
        },
