      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Audits one product surface against its own design system, reports at most three proven UI problems, and writes implementation plans for another agent.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want an interface reviewed or cleaned up without losing its identity, or you suspect design-system drift"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Traces one surface's routes, components and tokens, and keeps a finding only with a cited rule, a proven runtime path and one correction"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A table of up to three findings, one to improve first, then a self-contained plan for each finding you pick, in design-plans/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Never",
              "text": "Edits product source, installs, formats or commits; another agent carries out the plans"
            },
            {
              "label": "Skips",
              "text": "Accessibility and semantic HTML findings unless you ask for them"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A read-only design audit that would rather report nothing than guess. It picks one coherent surface, such as one app's main task flow, and follows what actually renders it: routes, layouts, shared components, variants, resolved tokens and styles. It reads DESIGN.md and other design docs only after proving they're current and govern that surface, and writes down the design language it found. A candidate becomes a finding only with three proofs: a binding design decision or a direct contradiction in what users see, evidence that the cited value reaches the surface, and the one correction the evidence requires. It then tries to falsify each finding and deletes any that fail, overlap or would invent product intent. Judgments about hierarchy, clarity or usability need screenshots or user evidence you provide, and functional bugs, performance and code quality are out of scope unless you ask. After the report it stops and asks which findings to turn into plans, each written so an agent with no context can carry it out.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/ibelick/ui-skills/tree/00db7d656719c399c091f3ea138c6f42a7fa4d98/skills/improve-ui"
