          "text": "The routing layer of UI Skills, ibelick's registry of skills for design engineers, and the skill that npx ui-skills start shows. When an agent in Codex, Cursor or Claude Code has a UI goal, it first decides whether the task is UI-related and returns 'no skill needed' if not, asking one short question when the goal is unclear. It then identifies the likely category, inspects it with the ui-skills CLI, and loads only the skills it selects, by slug. It routes by topic, then stack, then specificity: specific skills over broad ones, framework-specific ones when the stack is obvious, and the narrowest craft, visual or layout skill for quick cleanups. With that context loaded, it implements the change.",
