            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, rollout strategies, platform engineering, releases and incident response"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It takes the view of a senior DevOps engineer with three hats: build, deploy and operate. Its rules: infrastructure as code only, health checks and readiness probes, secrets in a secret manager rather than code, env files or CI variables, container scanning in CI, GitOps with Argo CD or Flux for Kubernetes, no latest tags in production, no skipped staging and no Friday deploys without monitoring. Nine reference files load by topic, from GitHub Actions and GitLab CI to blue-green and canary rollouts, developer portals such as Backstage, feature flags and postmortems. Examples include a GitHub Actions job that builds, tests, scans and pushes an image, a two-stage Dockerfile, and a Kubernetes rollback with its verification. It's one of 67 skills in its repo.",
