      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs system architecture from your requirements, with a Mermaid diagram, stated trade-offs and an Architecture Decision Record for each key choice.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're designing a new system, choosing between patterns or databases, or reviewing an existing design"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Gathers functional and non-functional requirements, matches them to patterns, designs with trade-offs stated, then reviews with you"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A requirements summary, a Mermaid architecture diagram, ADRs with alternatives and consequences, technology picks and risks"
            },
            {
              "label": "ADR means",
              "text": "Architecture Decision Record: a short note of a decision, its context, the alternatives considered and what it costs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Code-level design patterns or database-only design"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It acts as a principal architect who prefers pragmatic trade-offs to designing for hypothetical scale. Requirements must be fully covered before design starts, and a failed review sends it back to design with the feedback recorded. Its rules: document every significant decision, weigh trade-offs and not just benefits, plan for failure, count operational cost and complexity, consider security, and never pick a technology without comparing alternatives. Five reference files load as needed: monolith-versus-microservices patterns, an ADR template, a full system design template, database selection and a non-functional requirements checklist. Its examples are an API gateway diagram and an ADR choosing PostgreSQL over MongoDB and DynamoDB.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jeffallan/claude-skills/tree/078a25cc5bfd8011459be7b91d004e900c1d02d3/skills/architecture-designer"
