        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews a pull request or code for bugs, security holes, N+1 queries and design problems, and writes a prioritized report with a verdict.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a pull request or some code reviewed before merge, or a code quality audit"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sums up what the change is for in one sentence, then checks its structure, its security and performance details, and its tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A report of critical, major and minor issues, praise for what's done well, questions for the author, and an approve, request-changes or comment verdict"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike security-reviewer",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, goes deep on security; this one covers correctness, performance, maintainability and test coverage in one pass"
            },
            {
              "label": "Reads only",
              "text": "Its tools are Read, Grep and Glob, and its steps change no code"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It reviews as a senior engineer whose feedback should teach. If it can't state what a change is for in one sentence, it asks the author before going on. It asks whether the code follows the codebase's existing patterns and whether new abstractions are justified, looks for N+1 queries (a database query repeated inside a loop), hardcoded secrets and injection risks with the OWASP Top 10 as its baseline, and checks that tests cover edge cases and assert behavior rather than implementation. Critical issues are raised as soon as they're found. Suggestions come with code examples; it acknowledges an author's stated reasons before proposing an alternative, and won't block on personal preference or on style when a linter is configured. Reference files hold a review checklist, common issues, feedback examples and a report template, plus a two-stage review adapted from obra/superpowers that checks a change against its spec before judging code quality, and guidance on responding to review comments.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jeffallan/claude-skills/tree/078a25cc5bfd8011459be7b91d004e900c1d02d3/skills/code-reviewer"
        },
