      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds why PostgreSQL or MySQL queries are slow from execution plans, then applies index, query and config changes one at a time, measuring each.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Queries are slow, locks pile up, or a PostgreSQL or MySQL database needs tuning"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Captures a baseline with EXPLAIN ANALYZE, finds the bottleneck, applies one change at a time, and re-measures after each"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A before-and-after analysis with plan evidence, the SQL or config changes, validation queries and monitoring advice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Changes your database",
              "text": "It applies the index and config changes itself; it says to try them outside production first and revert if writes slow or replication lag grows"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "No change without a measured baseline, PostgreSQL indexes built CONCURRENTLY to avoid locking tables, no redundant indexes, statistics refreshed after bulk changes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It works as a senior database optimizer who measures before and after every change, since several changes at once make it impossible to tell which one helped. Its examples find the slowest queries with pg_stat_statements on PostgreSQL and performance_schema on MySQL, and read execution plans with buffer counts. A table maps plan symptoms to fixes: a sequential scan on a large table calls for an index, estimates far off the actual row count call for fresh statistics, a sort spilling to disk calls for more work_mem. It builds covering indexes, which hold every column a query needs so the table itself isn't read, then checks they're used. It weighs the write cost each new index adds and keeps up VACUUM and statistics maintenance. Reference files cover query optimization, index strategies, PostgreSQL tuning, MySQL tuning, and monitoring.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jeffallan/claude-skills/tree/078a25cc5bfd8011459be7b91d004e900c1d02d3/skills/database-optimizer"
        },
