          "text": "It treats every feature from three perspectives at once: frontend, backend and security. Its rules: validate input on both client and server, since a client check is never the only guard; parameterized queries against SQL injection; encoded output against XSS; error handling at every layer, not just the happy path; no hardcoded secrets; and no feature without acceptance criteria. Its example is an authenticated FastAPI profile endpoint that refuses with a 403 before touching the database when the user IDs don't match, with a TypeScript client that checks its input and handles errors. When the feature is built it hands off to the repo's test-master skill for QA and to DevOps for deployment. Reference files cover error handling, CRUD and form patterns, backend and frontend patterns, type sharing between them, API standards, architecture decisions and a deliverables checklist.",
