      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Applies REST API conventions for resource naming, status codes, response envelopes, pagination, filtering, auth, rate limits and versioning, with a pre-ship checklist.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're designing new REST endpoints or reviewing an existing API contract"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sets rules for URLs, methods, status codes, response and error shapes, pagination, filtering, sorting, auth, rate limits and versioning"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Endpoints that follow those rules, checked against a 12-item checklist before shipping"
            },
            {
              "label": "Examples in",
              "text": "TypeScript with Next.js and Zod, Python with Django REST Framework, and Go with net/http"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike api-design-principles",
              "text": "That one, wshobson's, also covers GraphQL; this one is REST only"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A REST reference from ECC. URLs are plural, lowercase, kebab-case nouns, with sub-resources for ownership and verbs only for actions such as cancel or login. A table says which methods are safe and idempotent, a reference says when to use each status code, and it warns against 200 for everything, 500 for validation errors and 200 for created resources. Responses wrap data in an envelope with meta and links; errors carry a code, a message and field-level details. It compares offset and cursor pagination and says when to use which, and sets query conventions: bracket operators for filters, a minus prefix for descending sorts, a q parameter for search and sparse fieldsets. It covers bearer tokens and API keys, ownership and role checks, rate-limit headers and tiers, and URL or header versioning, with a deprecation timeline that uses a Sunset header and a list of changes that do and don't need a new version.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/api-design"
