              "text": "Every slide fits one viewport with no scrolling, checked at five screen sizes from 1920x1080 down to a phone"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "python-pptx only to convert PowerPoint files; it asks before installing it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An ECC presentation skill, inspired by zarazhangrui's visual-exploration approach, for people who can't name the style they want. It works in three modes: a new deck from a topic or notes, a PowerPoint conversion, or improving existing HTML slides. Instead of a style questionnaire, it asks what the deck should make people feel, maps that to the 12 presets in its STYLE_PRESETS.md, such as Swiss Modern, Neon Cyber and Paper & Ink, and writes three single-slide previews to .ecc-design/slide-previews/. You pick one or mix elements. The deck is one HTML file with inline CSS and JS, theme values in CSS custom properties, type sized with clamp(), and density limits per slide type, such as four to six bullets or ten lines of code; content that doesn't fit is split into more slides. Conversions extract text, images and speaker notes with python-pptx and keep slide order. It bans generic purple gradients and template-looking decks, checks the result at five screen sizes, with browser automation when available, then deletes the previews unless you want them and can open the deck for you.",
