            {
              "label": "Unlike frontend-design",
              "text": "ECC tells you to install Anthropic's skill separately; this one adds content states and a rendered finish gate"
            },
            {
              "label": "Optional",
              "text": "UIZZE's paid MCP for real-world screen references, only with your consent and sending only sanitized design needs"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's design-direction skill, salvaged from a community pull request, with a content-state contract taken from UIZZE's anti-ui-slop workflow. Before coding, the agent chooses a direction: the job the interface does, who uses it, a tone such as utilitarian, editorial or dense, one memorable detail, and the constraints. A daily-use operations tool should be quiet and scannable; a launch page can be expressive. It records the product surface, primary action, hierarchy, target viewports and the reference behind each important choice, and for six states, loading, empty, error, partial, success and permission, what triggers them, what the user sees and the safe next action. It builds with the project's own components and tokens, and bans purple gradients, decorative blobs, cards inside cards and vague hero copy. The finish gate needs the rendered interface: keyboard and focus, contrast, reduced motion, touch targets, long content and each state, with screenshots kept in the workspace. A bundled Node checker rejects evidence records that are incomplete, failed or missing artifacts, though it can't judge the screenshots themselves.",
