          "text": "A prompt-rewriting skill contributed to ECC, and advisory only. It first reads CLAUDE.md and the project files to detect the stack, from package.json and go.mod to Cargo.toml and CMakeLists.txt. It classifies the request as a new feature, bug fix, refactor, research, testing, review, docs, infrastructure or design, and sizes it from trivial to epic, multi-session work. It then maps intent and stack to ECC components, such as tdd-workflow and the code-reviewer agent for a feature, or search-first for research. It checks the prompt for eleven kinds of missing context, from acceptance criteria and security needs to scope boundaries, and asks up to three questions when three or more are missing. Larger tasks start with /plan, and epic ones with the blueprint skill, split into one prompt per phase. The answer has five sections: a diagnosis, ECC components with a recommended Sonnet or Opus model, a full prompt with acceptance criteria and what not to do, a short version, and a rationale table. It replies in the language you wrote in.",
