      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes articles, guides, essays and newsletters that lead with concrete proof, cut AI clichés and match a voice from your examples.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a blog post, guide, tutorial, essay, launch post or newsletter longer than a paragraph"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Outlines with one job per section, opens each section with proof or an example, and deletes banned AI phrases"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A draft whose claims rest on the sources you gave, in your voice or, by default, a sharp, concrete operator voice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "ECC's brand-voice skill only to match a specific voice from examples"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short long-form writing skill from ECC. Its five rules: lead with the concrete thing (an artifact, number, anecdote or code), explain after the example, keep sentences tight, use proof instead of adjectives, and never invent facts or customer evidence. It bans phrases such as \"in today's rapidly evolving landscape\" and \"game-changer\", fake vulnerability arcs, closing questions added only for engagement and generic AI throat-clearing. The process is to clarify the audience and purpose, build an outline with one job per section, start sections with proof, conflict or an example, expand only where a sentence earns its space, and cut anything templated. It gives structures for technical guides, which open with what the reader gets and end with takeaways, for essays, which start from a tension and keep one argument per section, and for newsletters, whose first screen must do real work. A final check confirms claims are backed by sources and the voice matches the examples or the voice profile.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/article-writing"
