      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides safe database migrations: expand-contract renames, concurrent indexes, batched backfills and forward-only rollbacks, with workflows for Postgres, Prisma, Drizzle, Kysely, Django and golang-migrate.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're writing a schema or data migration, adding a column or index to a large table, or planning a zero-downtime deploy"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Applies five rules, such as forward-only production changes and schema kept apart from data, plus a seven-item safety checklist"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Migrations that avoid table locks and rewrites, using the commands and file formats of your migration tool"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "PostgreSQL SQL, Prisma, Drizzle, Kysely, Django and golang-migrate"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A migration reference from ECC. Its principles: every change is a migration, production only moves forward (a rollback is a new migration), schema and data changes go in separate migrations, test on production-sized data, and never edit a migration once it has run in production. The PostgreSQL section shows how to add columns without a table rewrite, build indexes with CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, rename a column through expand-contract (add, backfill, switch the code, drop), remove a column only after the code stops using it, and backfill in batches with SKIP LOCKED. For each tool it gives the commands and a sample: Prisma's migrate dev and deploy, with hand-written SQL for what Prisma can't generate, Drizzle's generate and migrate, Kysely's migration files and migrator, Django's data migrations and SeparateDatabaseAndState, and golang-migrate's up and down files. It closes with a zero-downtime plan that spreads one change across several deploys over a week, and a table of anti-patterns with better approaches.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/database-migrations"
