      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Checks finished work through build, type check, lint, tests with coverage, a secrets grep and diff review, then writes a PASS/FAIL report.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've finished a feature or refactor and want proof it's ready before opening a PR"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs the build, tsc or pyright, the linter or ruff, tests with coverage, a grep for keys and console.log, and a diff review"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A report marking each phase PASS or FAIL and the work READY or NOT READY for a PR, with the issues to fix"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also reports",
              "text": "Deployment checks separately, as verified, failed or not performed, and doesn't touch production without authorization"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A pre-PR quality gate from ECC for JavaScript, TypeScript and Python projects. It runs six phases in order and stops to fix a failing build before going on. Type checking uses tsc or pyright, fixing critical errors before going on, and linting uses npm run lint or ruff; the test phase reports totals and coverage against an 80% target. The security phase is a quick grep of .ts and .js files for strings like sk- and api_key, plus console.log calls left in src. The diff phase lists the changed files and reviews each for unintended changes, missing error handling and edge cases. When the task needs a deployment or other target environment checked, it reports that apart from the local checks: passing checks, a merge or a release don't count as acceptance there, and when it lacks access it names the next permitted step instead. In long sessions it suggests running again every 15 minutes or after major changes. It's meant to sit alongside PostToolUse hooks, which catch issues as they happen.",
