        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Researches a topic across many web sources through Firecrawl or Exa and writes a cited report with key takeaways and a confidence rating.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a deep dive, competitive analysis, technology evaluation, market sizing or due diligence rather than a quick answer"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks your goal, splits the topic into 3-5 sub-questions, searches each several ways, then reads 3-5 key sources in full"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown report with an executive summary, inline citations, key takeaways, a source list and its method; long ones are saved to a file"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "Every claim needs a source, single-source claims are flagged unverified, and scraped pages are data to cite, never instructions to follow"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The Firecrawl or Exa MCP server; both together give the widest coverage"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's research skill runs a fixed process through Firecrawl or Exa MCP tools. It asks one or two questions about your goal and angle, or skips them if you just say research it. It breaks the topic into three to five sub-questions, runs two or three keyword variations for each, mixing general and news queries, and aims for 15 to 30 unique sources, preferring academic, official and reputable news sources over blogs and forums. It then reads three to five key sources in full instead of relying on snippets. The report opens with the date, the source count and an overall confidence, followed by themed sections with inline citations, key takeaways, numbered sources and a methodology note. Recent sources are preferred, gaps are admitted and fact is kept apart from inference. Scraped pages are treated as untrusted: the agent never follows instructions in them, never lets them redirect the research or send data out, and flags any manipulation under the citation. For broad topics it can split the sub-questions across three parallel subagents in Claude Code. Short reports go in chat; for long ones the summary goes in chat and the full report to a file.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/deep-research"
