              "text": "Findings with a severity, file location, issue and fix, each tied to a specific page or asset rather than generic advice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Targets",
              "text": "LCP under 2.5s, INP under 200ms, CLS under 0.1, titles of 50-60 characters and meta descriptions of 120-160"
            },
            {
              "label": "Avoids",
              "text": "Keyword stuffing, thin near-duplicate pages, and schema for content that isn't actually on the page"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's SEO skill puts technical correctness ahead of content tweaks and gives each page one search intent. Its technical checklist covers crawlability (robots.txt, unintended noindex, shallow click depth, redirect chains of at most two hops, consistent canonicals), indexability (consistent URLs, hreflang, sitemaps that match the public pages, duplicates under canonical control), Core Web Vitals with common fixes such as preloading hero assets and reserving layout space, and which schema.org types fit which pages, with a JSON-LD example. On-page rules set lengths and formulas for titles and meta descriptions and ask for one clear H1. Keyword mapping goes from search intent to realistic variants, ranked by intent, value and competition, with one primary keyword per URL and a check for pages competing for the same one. Internal linking sends links from strong pages with descriptive anchors. Findings come as severity, location, issue and fix, and every recommendation has to point to a page or asset after reading the real page. It runs no crawler or tool of its own.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/seo"
