            {
              "label": "AI slop means",
              "text": "Gradients on everything, purple-to-blue defaults, purposeless glass cards, excessive scroll animation and generic centered heroes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's design-system skill has three modes. Generate scans your CSS, Tailwind or styled-components code for colors, typography, spacing, border radius, shadows and breakpoints, looks at three competitor sites through a browser MCP for inspiration, and proposes a token set as JSON and CSS custom properties, with a DESIGN.md explaining each decision and an HTML preview page with no dependencies. Audit scores the UI from 0 to 10 on color consistency, typography hierarchy, spacing rhythm, component consistency, responsive behavior, dark mode, animation, accessibility, information density and polish, with examples and a fix at a file and line for each. Slop check flags generic AI-generated design: gradients on everything, purple-to-blue defaults, glass cards with no purpose, rounding where it doesn't belong, excessive scroll animation, centered hero text over a stock gradient and fonts with no personality. Its examples show the modes called as commands, such as an audit of pages on localhost.",
