        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a reusable voice profile from real writing samples, so posts, emails and launch copy keep one author's voice without generic AI tropes.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want content or outreach for X, LinkedIn, email or launches to sound like a specific person, not generic AI copy"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Gathers 5-20 real samples, recent X posts first, and pulls out rhythm, density, capitalization, parentheticals, question use and claim style"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A structured VOICE PROFILE block, with preferred and banned moves and notes per channel, that other writing skills reuse"
            },
            {
              "label": "Bans",
              "text": "Fake curiosity hooks, \"not X, just Y\", \"Excited to share\", bait questions, thought-leader cadence and forced lowercase"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "The profile in the session; it saves it only where you ask, and never in your repo unless you say so"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's voice skill builds a profile once and reuses it, instead of guessing at style for every draft. It ranks source material: original X posts and threads first, then articles, essays and newsletters, outbound emails or DMs that worked, and last docs, changelogs and site copy, never generic platform examples. From 5 to 20 recent samples it notes sentence rhythm, how dense or explanatory the writing is, capitalization, parentheticals, how often questions appear, how sharply claims are made, how often numbers and mechanisms show up, transitions, and what the author never does, keeping a public launch voice apart from a private working voice when the samples split. The result follows a fixed VOICE PROFILE schema: author, goal, confidence, sources, those traits, preferred and banned moves, call-to-action rules and notes for X, LinkedIn and email. When live X access is available it pulls recent posts through ECC's x-api skill, which isn't on SkillHub. It also has default traits for the ECC author's own voice. Other ECC skills, such as content-engine and crosspost, take the profile as their source of truth.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/brand-voice"
        },
        "tags": [
