        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Scans your Claude Code configuration with the AgentShield CLI for hardcoded secrets, loose permissions, risky MCP servers, hook injection and prompt-injection risks.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You set up or change a .claude/ directory, onboard to a repo with Claude Code configs, or want a periodic security check"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs AgentShield over CLAUDE.md, settings.json, mcp.json, hooks and agent files, and grades the setup from A to F"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Findings ranked critical, high, medium and info, in the terminal or as JSON, Markdown or a standalone HTML report"
            },
            {
              "label": "Can also",
              "text": "Auto-fix safe issues, scaffold a locked-down .claude/ setup, or add a GitHub Action that fails CI on findings"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike ECC's security-review",
              "text": "That one is a checklist for writing app code; this one audits the agent's own configuration"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node to run the ecc-agentshield package; an Anthropic API key only for the --opus deep analysis"
            }
          ],
          "text": "AgentShield is a scanner for Claude Code configuration by ECC's own author, and this skill is how the agent runs it. It checks CLAUDE.md for hardcoded secrets, auto-run instructions and prompt-injection patterns; settings.json for overly broad allow lists, missing deny lists and bypass flags; mcp.json for risky servers, secrets in env and npx supply-chain risk; hooks for command injection, data exfiltration and silenced errors; and agent definitions for unrestricted tool access. The score maps to a grade from A (90 to 100) to F (under 40). Critical findings include API keys in config, Bash(*) in the allow list and shell-running MCP servers; high ones include missing deny lists; medium ones include `|| true` in hooks and `npx -y` in MCP configs. `--fix` replaces hardcoded secrets with environment variable references and narrows wildcard permissions, leaving manual-only items alone. `init` writes a fresh settings.json, CLAUDE.md and placeholder mcp.json. `--opus` runs three agents in turn, an attacker, a defender and an auditor, for a deeper verdict.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/security-scan"
        },
        "tags": [
