      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides shipping web apps to production: rolling, blue-green and canary rollouts, multi-stage Dockerfiles, CI/CD pipelines, health checks, rollback and a readiness checklist.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're setting up CI/CD, containerizing an app, choosing a rollout strategy or checking a release is ready for production"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Weighs rolling, blue-green and canary deploys, and gives Dockerfile, GitHub Actions, health check and Kubernetes probe templates"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Deployment config written to these patterns, plus rollback and production-readiness checklists to clear before shipping"
            },
            {
              "label": "Examples in",
              "text": "Node.js, Go and Python/Django Dockerfiles, TypeScript with Zod, and rollbacks for Kubernetes, Vercel, Railway and Prisma"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference from ECC for getting a web app into production. It weighs three rollout strategies: rolling as the default for backward-compatible changes, blue-green for instant rollback at the cost of double infrastructure, and canary for trying risky changes on a slice of real traffic. Docker gets multi-stage Dockerfiles for Node.js, Go and Python/Django that run as a non-root user with a HEALTHCHECK, plus lists of good and bad practices. The CI/CD section is a GitHub Actions pipeline that lints, type-checks and tests, builds and pushes an image to GitHub's container registry, then deploys from main, with the stages a pull request and a merge should each run. It covers simple and detailed health endpoints, Kubernetes liveness, readiness and startup probes, twelve-factor configuration validated at startup with Zod, and rollback commands. It ends with a rollback checklist and a production-readiness checklist across application, infrastructure, monitoring, security and operations. It runs no deployment itself.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/deployment-patterns"
