        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Records demo videos of a web app with Playwright, showing a visible cursor, natural pacing and subtitles, after exploring and rehearsing the flow.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You need a walkthrough, tutorial or feature demo video of a web app for docs, onboarding or stakeholders"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Maps each page's real fields, rehearses until every selector resolves, then records with a gliding cursor, visible typing, smooth scrolling and step subtitles"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Node Playwright script with rehearse and record modes, and a 1280x720 WebM video saved under a stable name"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike ECC's video-editing",
              "text": "That one cuts footage you already have; this one makes the footage by driving your app"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node and Playwright with headless Chromium"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Demo recordings break quietly when a script assumes a field is a textarea or a dropdown is a select, so this ECC skill never records first. In Discover, the agent visits each page of the flow and dumps its visible inputs, buttons, select options and required fields into a field map. In Rehearse, it runs every step without recording, checks each selector, prints the visible elements when one fails, and fixes the script until all pass. Only then does it Record, with Playwright's video capture at 1280x720 in headless Chromium, against the app at QA_BASE_URL, localhost:3000 by default. The script injects an SVG arrow cursor that moves to each target before clicking, types character by character, scrolls smoothly, pans across dashboards and shows short \"Step N - Action\" subtitles in a bar at the bottom. It plans the video as a story, entry, context, main action, a variation and the result, with set pauses after logins, navigation and clicks. Helpers log every skipped or failed step instead of swallowing it, and the finished WebM is copied to a stable file name. A pre-recording checklist and twelve common pitfalls round it off.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/ui-demo"
