            }
          ],
          "text": "An accessibility guide from ECC for React and Next.js, aimed at the problems code reviewers and tools such as CodeRabbit and ESLint's a11y rules flag most. Forms link every label to its input with htmlFor and id, mark required fields for screen readers, and tie error text to the field with aria-describedby, aria-invalid and role=\"alert\". It prefers native elements, buttons over clickable divs, real links and ordered headings, and uses ARIA only where HTML falls short: aria-label versus aria-labelledby, aria-live for updates, aria-expanded and aria-controls for disclosures. Full examples cover an accessible login form, a dropdown driven by arrow keys, Enter, Space and Escape, and a modal that moves focus in and restores it on close, with focus-trap-react suggested for full trapping. It also covers alt text for meaningful and decorative images, labels on icon-only buttons, a useReducedMotion hook, and anti-patterns such as positive tabIndex and aria-hidden on focusable elements.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/frontend-a11y"
        },
