      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Catches bugs AI agents keep reintroducing, with database-free sandbox API tests and a bug-check that runs tests before any AI review.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "An AI agent both wrote and reviewed a change, or a bug it fixed keeps coming back"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs the test suite and build before any AI review, then writes a regression test for each bug fixed, named after the bug"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Fast API tests that run in your app's sandbox mode with no database, and a bug-check command file for Claude Code"
            },
            {
              "label": "Watches for",
              "text": "Sandbox and production paths returning different fields, columns missing from a SELECT, stale state after errors, and optimistic updates without rollback"
            },
            {
              "label": "Examples in",
              "text": "TypeScript with Vitest and the Next.js App Router, plus Supabase queries"
            }
          ],
          "text": "When the same model writes a fix and reviews it, it carries the same blind spot into both steps; the skill's example is a missing field that slipped past AI review fix after fix until a test caught it on its first run. So it puts mechanical checks first. A bug-check command runs npm run test and npm run build, reports any failure as the top bug, and only then has the agent review with known AI blind spots in mind: sandbox and production consistency, response shapes, SELECT completeness, error rollback and race conditions. Each fix then gets a regression test. Tests force the project's sandbox or mock mode so API routes run without a database, using a request helper for Next.js routes and a list of fields every response must contain. Its strategy is to test where bugs were found rather than chase coverage: write the test right after finding a bug, assert the response shape rather than the implementation, and keep the whole suite under a second.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/ai-regression-testing"
