          ],
          "text": "A dashboard here exists to answer four questions: is it healthy, where is the bottleneck, what changed, and what should someone do. The agent organizes panels around health, latency, throughput, saturation and service-specific risk, never around visual layout or every metric available. Before building, it inspects the target platform's existing dashboards for their JSON structure, query language, variables, threshold styling and section layout. The board follows a fixed order: overview, performance, resources, then a service-specific section, and any panel that answers no real question is removed. Example panel sets cover Elasticsearch (cluster health, shard allocation, search latency, indexing rate, JVM heap), Kafka (brokers, under-replicated partitions, consumer lag, disk and network) and API gateways (request rate, p50, p95 and p99 latency, error rate, upstream health). A closing checklist asks for valid JSON, clear grouping, titles and units, meaningful thresholds, filter variables, a sensible default time range and refresh, and no vanity panels.",
