        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Has a failing agent stop retrying, record the failure, match it to a known pattern, take the smallest safe fix and report.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "An agent run loops, hits its tool-call limit, retries without progress, bloats its context or drifts from its task"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Records the failure, matches it to a known pattern, takes the smallest reversible fix, and only then retries"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A self-debug report: failure, root cause, recovery action, result, token or time burn risk, and a preventive change to encode later"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike code debugging skills",
              "text": "Those debug your code; this one debugs the agent's own run, such as a loop, a retry storm or the wrong working directory"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A four-phase loop the agent runs on itself before escalating to you. First it captures the failure precisely: the error, the last tool calls, the goal in progress, signs of context pressure, and assumptions about the working directory, branch and services. Then it matches the failure to a table of patterns, such as repeated identical commands pointing to a loop, ECONNREFUSED to a wrong port or a service that's down, 429s to a retry storm, a missing file after a write to the wrong directory or branch, and tests still failing after a fix to a wrong hypothesis. Recovery is the smallest action that tests the diagnosis: stop retrying and restate the hypothesis, trim low-signal context, re-check the real file and branch state, narrow to one failing command or test, or hand off to a human when the risk is high. It forbids claiming fixes it can't perform, like resetting agent state. It always ends with the failure pattern, hypothesis, action and evidence, never a bare \"I fixed it\".",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/agent-introspection-debugging"
        },
