          "text": "ECC's rewrite of a community production-audit idea, minus the external scanner and data sharing. The agent establishes what's being released, reads recent commits and the branch diff, and inspects the runtime, auth, data, payment, background-job, AI and deployment boundaries that actually exist in the repo, along with CI, tests, migrations, environment docs and the rollback path. A deployed URL, if in scope, gets only browser or HTTP checks, without credentialed actions unless you give it a safe test account. Five lenses guide it: security and auth (including prompt injection on agent features), data integrity, payments and webhooks (signatures, idempotency, replays), operations (clean start, fail-fast env vars, health checks, rollback) and user experience on desktop and mobile. Scores fall in four bands from Blocked to Strong, capped at 69 for issues such as missing authorization or non-idempotent payment webhooks, and at 84 when CI isn't green. It's engineering triage, not a compliance audit.",
