              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "ECC's market-research, brand-voice and content-engine skills, which it uses for research, voice and social posts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An end-to-end launch workflow in four phases. Research profiles the audience (jobs to be done, fears, language, alternatives), maps at least three competitors and picks one to three insights, using ECC's market-research skill. Positioning produces a one-sentence core benefit, a \"[Product] helps [audience] [achieve outcome] by [mechanism]\" statement, a campaign angle and a tone profile, and nothing gets written until you approve them. Production then goes in order, each layer informing the next: landing page copy section by section, an email sequence that runs from problem through proof and urgency to a final CTA, platform-native LinkedIn and X posts, timestamped short-form video scripts, three or four ad variants testing different angles, and a calendar with channels, timing and dependencies. Review gates every piece: a 5-second test on hero copy, one specific CTA per piece, matching claims between ads and the landing page, subjects that match email bodies, and no copy that would work unchanged for a competitor. Hype words and fake urgency are banned outright.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/marketing-campaign"
