              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A repo with one module per source, a Gemini client with model fallback, a feedback module, a config.yaml and a GitHub Actions schedule"
            },
            {
              "label": "Learns from",
              "text": "The items you mark saved or rejected, once you add a sync script that writes them to its feedback file"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A Gemini API key and a Notion token; Sheets and Supabase are named as options, but only Notion is wired in"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The skill frames every collector as three layers: collect, enrich, store. It starts with five questions: the data source, the fields to extract, where results go, how AI should enrich each item (score, summarize, classify or match) and how often to run. It then generates a fixed layout: a module per source with requests and BeautifulSoup, plus patterns for REST, RSS, paginated APIs and Playwright for JavaScript-rendered pages; a rule-based pre-filter; a Gemini REST client that falls back across four Flash models on quota errors; scoring in batches of five against your profile and priorities; deduplication by URL before each Notion push; and a GitHub Actions workflow, every three hours by default, that commits the feedback history. Scraped text is treated as untrusted: never followed as instructions, passed to the LLM as delimited data, and never allowed to change targets or config. A closing checklist covers keeping settings in config, .env hygiene, a schema setup script and backfilling scores on old rows.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/data-scraper-agent"
