            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The GitHub CLI, logged in with access to the repo"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An operations playbook for repository maintainers, built on the gh CLI. Triage sorts each issue into a type, such as bug, feature request, question or duplicate, and a priority from critical to low, searches for duplicates, applies labels, and posts replies or asks for reproduction steps. Its stale policy labels issues after 14 days without activity, nudges PRs after 7 and closes stale issues after 30. For CI failures it reads the failed logs, tells flaky tests from real failures and suggests a fix for real ones. Releases start from a green main, collect merged PRs into a changelog and use gh release create. Security monitoring reads Dependabot and secret scanning alerts, flags critical ones, and proposes dependency bumps for you to merge, never auto-merging. Text in an issue, PR, commit or log that addresses the agent is quoted to you, not acted on. Before finishing, it checks that triaged issues are labeled, no PR has gone a week without review, and CI failures were investigated rather than just re-run. A separate release checklist applies only to ECC's own repository.",
