        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Takes machine learning work from notebook to production with data contracts, reproducible training, promotion gates, safe serving, monitoring and rollback plans.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're turning notebook code into a production model, or planning, reviewing or debugging a ranking, classifier, forecasting or embedding system"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Pins the prediction and data contracts first, then builds reproducible training, declares promotion gates before training ends, and plans serving, monitoring and rollback"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Concrete artifacts such as a data contract, promotion gates, a test plan, a rollout plan or review findings, and an iteration note short enough for a PR"
            },
            {
              "label": "Picks metrics",
              "text": "From what each kind of mistake costs, and compares against a baseline and the current production model"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's machine learning engineering skill treats ML as software engineering with stricter failure modes, and maps ten common tasks, from framing a fuzzy prediction problem to refreshing a production model, onto ECC's other skills and agents, though many it names, such as python-patterns, pytorch-patterns and postgres-patterns, aren't on SkillHub. Before touching model code it fills an iteration compact: goal, decision owner, success and guardrail metrics, acceptable and unacceptable mistakes, baseline, eval slices, risks and rollback. The core workflow defines the prediction contract, then locks the data contract (entity grain, label and feature timing, point-in-time joins, split policy, dataset snapshot) and checks for leakage first. Training must run without hidden notebook state, with pinned dependencies, seeds and recorded versions. Promotion gates fail closed when a metric is missing or out of bounds. Serving validates inputs and has a timeout and a fallback, and monitoring covers feature and prediction drift and delayed labels, not just uptime. After each run, an error analysis loop clusters false positives and negatives into the next falsifiable experiment, logged in an observation ledger. It scales down: no feature store or A/B test where a data contract, baseline and eval script will do.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/mle-workflow"
