      "skillMd": {
        "version": "d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds the code context a subagent needs in up to three search passes, scoring each file's relevance and refining the search terms.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A subagent needs codebase context you can't predict up front, or agent tasks fail from too much or too little context"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Searches broadly, scores each file's relevance from 0 to 1, notes what's still missing, refines the search and repeats, at most three times"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A short list of the files that matter, those scoring 0.7 or higher"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike all-or-nothing context",
              "text": "This one doesn't send a subagent everything or nothing; the first pass often reveals the codebase's own terms, such as \"throttle\" for rate limiting"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Subagents start without knowing which files matter, what patterns the codebase uses or what it calls things. Sending everything overflows the context, and sending nothing leaves them blind. This skill gives the agent a four-phase loop instead. Dispatch runs a broad search by file patterns and keywords. Evaluate scores each result: 0.8 to 1 when it implements the target, 0.5 to 0.7 for related patterns or types, lower for tangential files, and excludes the irrelevant ones. Refine adds the patterns and terms found in relevant files, drops what was excluded and targets the gaps it noted. Loop repeats until there are at least three highly relevant files with no critical gaps, or three cycles have passed. It comes with JavaScript sketches of each phase, two worked examples and a five-step version to paste into a subagent's prompt.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/iterative-retrieval"
        },
