        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Drafts investor cold emails, warm intro requests, follow-ups and updates that are personalized, concrete and end in one clear ask.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're writing to angels, VCs, strategic investors or accelerators: a cold email, a warm intro request, a follow-up or an update"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Builds each message around why this investor, what the company does with its proof, and one concrete ask, and cuts stock phrases like \"I'd love to connect\""
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Short drafts, flagged as unfinished when there's nothing specific to personalize them with"
            },
            {
              "label": "Pairs with",
              "text": "ECC's brand-voice skill when your own voice matters"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Investor messages should be short, concrete and easy to act on, and none should be sendable to just any investor. A cold email has a short, specific subject line, an opener on why this investor, a pitch with what the company does, why now and the proof that matters, one next step, and a sign-off with a credibility anchor if needed. Personalization comes from portfolio companies, a public thesis, talk or post, a mutual connection or a clear fit with the investor's focus. Follow-ups default to day 4 or 5 with one new data point and a final one on day 10 to 12, then stop. Warm intro requests give the connector the reason it's a fit and a forwardable blurb under 100 words. Post-meeting updates cover what was discussed, the promised answer, a new proof point and the next step. Before delivering, it checks the draft is personalized, the ask explicit, the proof concrete and the filler gone.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/investor-outreach"
        },
