        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Compares coding agents like Claude Code and Aider on your own tasks by pass rate, cost, time and consistency, with the agent-eval CLI.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're choosing between coding agents, or want numbers on whether a model or setup change actually helped"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs each agent several times on tasks you define in YAML, each run in its own git worktree, and judges the result with tests, grep or an LLM"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A table per task of each agent's pass rate, cost, wall-clock time and consistency across runs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The agent-eval CLI, installed by you from its GitHub repository, and the agents you compare"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short manual for agent-eval, a third-party CLI for testing coding agents on your own work instead of on impressions. You write each task as a YAML file: the repo, the files to touch, the prompt, a commit to pin it to, and the judges that decide success, such as a pytest or build command, a grep pattern or an LLM-as-judge prompt. agent-eval run hands the prompt to each agent, such as Claude Code or Aider, in a fresh git worktree, so runs can't interfere with each other or the base repo, and records pass or fail, API cost when available, and time. agent-eval report then prints the comparison table. Its advice: start with three to five tasks from your real workload, run each agent at least three times since agents are non-deterministic, pin the commit, include at least one deterministic judge, and weigh cost against pass rate. The skill gives no install command: it asks you to review the source and install the tool from its repository.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/agent-eval"
        },
