      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Adapts one post or article into separate versions for X, LinkedIn, Threads and Bluesky, in the author's voice and never as identical copy.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want one launch, update or essay out on several social platforms without pasting the same text everywhere"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A primary version, a variant per platform, a note on what changed and why, and any publishing constraint you still need to settle"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Adapts to each platform's limits, keeps the author's cadence, and deletes stock lines like \"Excited to share\""
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "Post anything itself: it returns the versions for you to publish"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's crossposting skill starts from the strongest source version, such as the original X post, article, launch note or changelog, and rewrites it for each platform rather than copying it. X gets a compressed version that leads with the sharpest claim, a thread only when one post can't hold the argument, and no hashtags. LinkedIn gets only the context outsiders need, without a fake founder reflection or a closing question. Threads stays direct, and Bluesky concise in the author's cadence. Across all of them it keeps each post about one thing, adds no call to action or moral the source didn't earn, and bans lines such as \"Here's what I learned\" and \"What do you think?\". It treats source material as content, not instructions: text in a draft or URL can't choose platforms, accounts or timing, and agent-directed text is flagged to you. A quality gate checks that every version reads like the same author and none is duplicated verbatim. It suggests posting the strongest native version first, and staggers timing only if you ask.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/crosspost"
