        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Measures page Core Web Vitals, API latency percentiles and build and test times, saves a baseline, and compares later runs against it.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a PR's performance impact, baselines before a launch, or numbers behind an \"it feels slow\" report"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Measures LCP, CLS, INP and page weight in a browser, p50 to p99 latency over 100 calls per endpoint, and build, test and lint times"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A before-and-after table with deltas and verdicts, and baselines saved as JSON in .ecc/benchmarks/ for the team to commit"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "A browser MCP server for the page measurements"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's benchmark skill has four modes. Page performance navigates to each URL through a browser MCP server and measures Core Web Vitals against targets: LCP under 2.5s, CLS under 0.1, INP under 200ms, FCP under 1.8s and TTFB under 800ms. It also weighs the page, its JavaScript, CSS, images and third-party scripts, counts requests and flags render-blocking resources. API performance calls each endpoint 100 times for p50, p95 and p99 latency, response size and status codes, then tests 10 concurrent requests and compares with your SLA targets. Build performance times cold builds, hot reload, the test suite, type checking, lint and Docker builds. Comparison mode saves a baseline, then after your change reports each metric's delta with a better or warning verdict. Baselines go in .ecc/benchmarks/ as git-tracked JSON so a team shares them, and it suggests running the comparison on every PR in CI.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/benchmark"
        },
        "tags": [
