        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Makes the agent confirm destructive commands like rm -rf and force pushes, and confine its edits to one directory, until you lift it.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "An agent works on production systems, runs unattended, or should only touch one folder during a migration or deploy"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Careful mode pauses before rm -rf, force pushes, DROP TABLE and similar, and suggests a safer command; Freeze mode limits writes to one directory"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Until you tell the agent to stop applying the rules"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike hooks and denylists",
              "text": "Nothing blocks a tool call, as a hook or permission deny rule would; the agent follows the rules itself"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Three modes the agent applies to itself. Careful mode watches for destructive commands: rm -rf (especially on /, ~ or the project root), git push --force, git reset --hard, git checkout ., DROP TABLE or DATABASE, docker system prune, kubectl delete, chmod 777, sudo rm, npm publish and anything with --no-verify. Before running one, the agent says what it does, asks you to confirm and offers a safer alternative. Freeze mode locks edits to a directory you name, such as src/components/, and the agent explains when a change would need to go outside it. Guard mode combines the two: read anything, write only in one folder, and ask before anything destructive. You turn it off by telling the agent to stop. The skill says plainly that it's advisory: ECC ships no command or hook for it, so for blocking that doesn't depend on the agent it points to Claude Code's permission deny rules or a PreToolUse hook.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/safety-guard"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:security",
          "type:mode",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "guardrails",
          "scope-control"
        ],
        "note": "Advisory only: no hook enforces it, so nothing blocks a command the agent decides to run. It stays on until you tell the agent to stop.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
