      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Pressure-tests a product idea before you build it, with a YC-style diagnostic, a founder review, a new-user journey audit or ICE feature ranking.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're about to start a feature, are stuck choosing between ideas, or want a sanity check before a launch"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks who it's for, the pain, why now, the MVP and the anti-goal; or scores your repo's product-market-fit signals; or times onboarding as a new user"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A PRODUCT-BRIEF.md with risks and a go/no-go call, a scored founder review, three onboarding fixes, or a ranked roadmap"
            },
            {
              "label": "Comes before",
              "text": "ECC's product-capability, which turns a \"build it\" brief into an implementation plan"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's product skill decides whether something is worth building, and leaves the spec to product-capability. It has four modes. The diagnostic works like automated YC office hours: seven questions on who the user is, how often and how badly the pain hits, why now, the 10-star version, the MVP, what you're explicitly not building and the metric that shows it works, ending in a PRODUCT-BRIEF.md with risks and a go/no-go recommendation. The founder review reads your README, CLAUDE.md, package.json and recent commits, infers what the project is trying to be, scores product-market-fit signals from 0 to 10, and names the one thing that would 10x it and what you're building that doesn't matter. The journey audit installs the product as a new user, logs and times every friction point, compares with competitors' onboarding and recommends three fixes. Feature prioritization scores ideas by impact times confidence divided by effort and returns a ranked roadmap with rationale.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/product-lens"
        },
