      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Adds an API connector to a codebase by matching its existing connectors' layout, config, auth, errors, tests and registration.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're adding one more integration, such as a Jira or Slack provider, to a repo that already has several"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Studies at least two existing connectors first, narrows the target API to what the repo needs, then builds it in the same layers"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A connector that looks native to the codebase, with config validation, explicit auth and errors, registry wiring, tests and docs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike starting from docs",
              "text": "This one starts from the repo's current pattern, not the vendor's docs or a generic HTTP client"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short workflow for integrations that should look like they were always there. It first inspects at least two existing connectors or providers and maps their file layout, abstraction boundaries, config model, retry and pagination conventions, registry hooks and test fixtures. It then narrows the new integration to what the repo needs: the auth flow, key entities, core read and write operations, pagination and rate limits, and webhooks or polling. It builds in the repo's own layers, typically config, client, mapping, entry point, registration and tests, and finishes against a checklist: it matches an existing pattern, validates config, handles auth and errors explicitly, follows retry norms, completes registry wiring, mirrors the test style and updates docs where the repo expects it. Its guardrails: don't invent a second architecture, don't stop at transport code, and don't copy an old connector when a newer pattern exists. Reference shapes cover Python provider and connector layouts and a TypeScript plugin layout.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/api-connector-builder"
        },
