      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Saves, deduplicates, syncs and retrieves knowledge across Claude Code memory files, an MCP memory graph, a knowledge-base repo, GitHub and Linear.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You say \"save this to the KB\" or \"what do I know about X\", or want notes, sessions and plans in one canonical place"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Classifies each piece of knowledge, searches every layer for an existing entry, then stores it in the right layer and updates indexes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "Live project state in GitHub and Linear, quick recall in Claude Code memory, durable notes in a knowledge-base repo"
            },
            {
              "label": "Syncs",
              "text": "Conversation histories and workspace maps into the knowledge-base repo, with secrets redacted, then commits and pushes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "ECC's knowledge skill sorts what you know into six layers, each with a job. Active work lives in GitHub issues and PRs and in Linear. Claude Code's memory files under ~/.claude/projects hold quick-access preferences, feedback and project context. An MCP memory server holds a knowledge graph of entities and relations for semantic search. A knowledge-base repo holds durable notes, session exports and research; Supabase or Postgres holds large or structured documents; and a local archive folder holds human-facing notes. To ingest something, the agent classifies it, such as a business decision, roadmap state, preference or long document, checks memory files, the graph and the trackers for an entry to update instead of duplicating, writes it to the right layers and updates indexes. Sync jobs export Claude, Codex and other agent sessions and workspace maps into the knowledge-base repo, redact secrets, and commit and push; others pull in ChatGPT or Grok exports, bookmarks and GitHub activity. A quality gate checks for duplicates, redaction and updated indexes.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/knowledge-ops"
