      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Researches current questions from fresh evidence, labelling each claim as sourced fact, your context, inference or recommendation, with dates.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You ask for something current, a comparison, a look-up on people or companies, or a question you'll keep asking"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sorts the ask into a quick fact, a comparison, an enrichment pass or a monitoring candidate, then takes the lightest search that answers it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An answer split into evidence, inference and recommendation, with dates on time-sensitive claims and a call on whether it should become a monitor"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike ECC's deep-research",
              "text": "This one picks which research skill to use and how to label the result, and escalates to that one for multi-source synthesis"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "ECC's exa-search, deep-research, market-research, lead-intelligence and knowledge-ops skills"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An operator layer over ECC's research skills. The agent first sorts what you already gave it into established facts, things to verify and open questions, so it doesn't restart from zero. It picks a lane: a quick factual answer, a comparison or decision memo, a people or company enrichment pass, or a question likely to recur. Then it takes the lightest path that works: exa-search for fast discovery, deep-research when synthesis across sources matters, market-research when the result should be a recommendation, lead-intelligence when the real ask is ranking targets, and knowledge-ops to store the result afterwards. It skips a heavy research pass when local code or docs already answer the question. Every important claim is labelled as a sourced fact, user-supplied context, inference or recommendation, and freshness-sensitive answers carry concrete dates. If you're likely to ask the same question again, it says so and recommends a monitor instead of repeating the search by hand.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/research-ops"
