            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent first checks the size, colour and weight of the project's existing icons so new ones match. It then looks for candidates: a bundled shell script searches the Iconify API across 200+ open-source collections such as Material Design Icons, Phosphor, Tabler and Lucide, or the agent picks an Apple SF Symbol from a table of common names. An optional preview downloads an icon so the agent can look at it first. Generation writes a full Xcode imageset, a Contents.json and PNGs at 1x, 2x and 3x (68 points by default, so 68, 136 and 204 pixels), in grey unless you give a hex colour, to /tmp/icons or a folder you name, such as your asset catalog. SF Symbols go through a Swift script that also takes a symbol weight. Last, the agent views the 2x PNG, copies the imageset into the catalog if needed and builds the project to check Xcode picks it up.",
