            {
              "label": "Unlike TeamCreate agent teams",
              "text": "This one's agents work independently and never talk to each other"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An interactive menu for composing ad hoc agent teams. It finds agents with the claude agents command, which covers user, plugin and built-in agents, and reads persona files from ./agents and ~/.claude/agents. Domains come from subfolder names or, in a flat folder, from a filename prefix two or more files share; the rest go under General. Built-in agents like Explore and Plan are skipped unless you ask. You pick domains by number, agents by name, or everything in a domain; past five it asks you to narrow down. Each chosen agent then runs at the same time as a general-purpose subagent, prompted with its whole persona file and your task. A failed agent is noted and the others still report. With one agent it shows the output as is; with several it groups results by agent and adds a synthesis of agreements, conflicts between recommendations, and next steps. It never hardcodes the agent list, so new persona files appear on the next run.",
