      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Finds principles shared by two or more installed skills and proposes adding them to your rule files, applying only what you approve.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've installed many skills and want the principles they share written once into your rule files, such as monthly or after installing new skills"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Scans your skills and rules with scripts, has subagents cross-read clusters of skills, and keeps only principles found in 2+ skills that your rules lack"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A report with a verdict per principle (append, revise, new section, new file, already covered or too specific) and draft rule text"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "Your rules unchanged until you approve each candidate by number; results go to a results.json in its own folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Claude Code's ~/.claude/skills and ~/.claude/rules folders, subagents and jq"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A maintenance pass for people with many skills and a folder of rule files. Phase one is deterministic: two bundled scripts list every SKILL.md in ~/.claude/skills and the project's .claude/skills with its name and description, and index the second-level headings of each rule file in ~/.claude/rules. Phase two is judgment: skills are grouped into themed clusters, and each cluster goes to a subagent with the full text of all rules. A candidate survives only if it appears in two or more skills, can be written as do X or don't do Y, carries a clear risk if ignored, and isn't already in the rules, even in other words; language and framework specifics and code stay in skills. Candidates from all clusters are merged and deduplicated. You get a summary table and, per candidate, its evidence, risk and draft text linking back to the source skills, or a before-and-after for a revision. You approve, modify or skip each by number, and only then are rule files changed; the results are saved with a timestamp.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/rules-distill"
