        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides building clinical decision support: drug interaction and allergy checks, weight-, age- and kidney-adjusted dose validation, NEWS2 scoring and blocking alerts, with zero-miss tests.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're building drug interaction checks, dose validation, clinical scores such as NEWS2 or qSOFA, or safety alerts inside an electronic medical record"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Has the agent write the decision engine as pure functions with no side effects, which take clinical data and return alerts"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "TypeScript patterns for interaction checks, dose validation and NEWS2, an alert severity table and tests that demand 100% detection"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "Interactions work both ways, a missing weight blocks a weight-based dose, and critical alerts are never toasts or auto-dismissed"
            },
            {
              "label": "From",
              "text": "Dr. Keyur Patel of Health1 Super Speciality Hospitals"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Patterns for clinical decision support systems (CDSS), the software that warns clinicians about unsafe orders inside an electronic medical record. It treats every module as patient-safety critical, with zero tolerance for false negatives. The engine is a pure function library: checkInteractions compares a new drug with current medications and allergies and returns alerts sorted by severity; validateDose checks weight-based, age-adjusted, kidney-adjusted and absolute limits, and refuses a weight-based drug when the weight is missing; calculateNEWS2 returns the National Early Warning Score, a risk level and escalation advice, with tables that must match the Royal College of Physicians specification exactly. Alerts come in three tiers: critical blocks the action until the clinician records an override reason in the audit trail, major needs an acknowledgement, minor is for awareness. Its tests run every interaction pair in both directions and require a 100% pass. Anti-patterns include skippable checks, any types for clinical data, hardcoded interaction pairs and silently swallowed errors.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/healthcare-cdss-patterns"
        },
