      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Gates healthcare app deployments on five test suites: clinical decision logic, patient-data leaks and data integrity must pass 100%, workflows and integrations 95%.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're about to deploy an EMR or EHR app, or changed its clinical logic, patient-data schema or access control"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs five test suites in order; one failure in the three critical ones blocks the deploy, and the other two warn below 95%"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An eval report of tests passed per category, coverage and a verdict such as safe to deploy, plus a GitHub Actions safety-gate workflow"
            },
            {
              "label": "Expects",
              "text": "Your tests already sorted into folders such as tests/cdss and tests/security/phi; it doesn't write them"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "Jest as the example runner; it says to adapt the commands for Vitest, pytest or PHPUnit"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A deployment gate for healthcare software, where a missed drug interaction or a leaked record is a patient-safety event. It defines five test categories with pass bars. Three are critical, need 100%, run with --bail and block the deploy on any failure: clinical decision support accuracy (drug interactions both ways, dose rules, clinical scores against published specs), exposure of protected health information (in error responses, logs, URLs, browser storage, across facilities, without login) and data integrity (locked encounters, audit trails, no cascade deletes or orphaned records). Clinical workflows (encounters, templates, prescriptions, red-flag alerts) and integration compliance (HL7 v2, FHIR, lab mapping) need 95%, computed from Jest's JSON output with jq and bc, and only warn below it. It gives the commands to run the critical gates locally, a GitHub Actions workflow that runs all five on every push and pull request with an 80% coverage threshold on the decision-support suite, and a report format. Anti-patterns include lowering critical thresholds, mocking the decision engine in integration tests and deploying on a red gate.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/healthcare-eval-harness"
        },
