          "text": "An evidence-first workflow for operators asking about money: sales, refunds, MRR, pricing, or whether the product does what the sales copy says. It keeps four things apart: revenue facts, customer impact, code-backed product truth and the recommendation. It prefers live billing data, such as Stripe, and states the snapshot time when the data isn't live, then lays out paid sales, active subscriptions, failed checkouts, refunds, disputes and duplicates. Customer-specific questions are classified first, as duplicate checkout, real team intent, broken self-serve controls, unmet value or failed payment, before the broader product question. When the answer depends on implementation, it inspects the checkout, pricing page, entitlement calculation, seat or quota handling and billing portal support in the code. It won't call billing per seat unless the entitlement path enforces it, won't count failed attempts as revenue, and won't compare competitor pricing from memory when current evidence exists. It was written as ECC's own billing workflow and names other ECC skills to pull in, such as research-ops.",
