          "text": "A working method for Google Workspace files that are part of a larger system, such as trackers, plans, customer lists and decks. Drive is the entry point: the agent locates the exact file, sibling assets, likely duplicates and recent versions, and confirms by title, owner, modified time or folder when several look alike, instead of guessing from filenames. Before changing anything it summarizes the structure, such as tabs, headings or slide count, and decides whether the job is light cleanup or structural surgery, then picks the smallest tool that can do it safely. Edits stay precise: index-aware edits in Docs, explicit tabs and ranges in Sheets, and in Slides a split between content edits and visual cleanup or template migration, rechecked by inspection for layout work. It also points out duplicate trackers, outdated decks and stale copies of canonical docs, and whether each should be archived, merged or renamed. Example requests: condense the active planning doc, show the churn-risk rows in a customer sheet, import a deck into Slides and make it presentable.",
