      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Prepares a private project for public release: strips secrets in a staging copy, scans it, packages docs and license, publishes to GitHub on approval.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to open-source a private project without leaking secrets, personal data or internal references"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Chains three agents: a forker copies the project to ~/opensource-staging and strips secrets, a sanitizer scans it, a packager writes CLAUDE.md, setup.sh, README, license and contributing files"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A one-commit staging repo with fork and sanitization reports, then a public GitHub repo once you say yes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Gates",
              "text": "Stops on a failed scan after three fix attempts, scans again after packaging, and asks you to open any files the scanner couldn't read"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The three ECC agents, Claude Code and the gh CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A guarded release process for turning a private repo into a public one. You run /opensource fork on a project and choose a license, GitHub owner, repo name and description. The forker agent copies the project to a staging folder without .git or dependency folders, strips secrets, replaces internal references with placeholders, writes .env.example and starts a clean single-commit history. The sanitizer scans for secrets, personal data, internal references, dangerous files, missing config, git history and unreadable files, and writes a pass or fail report; failures come back to you to fix and rescan, up to three times. Every later change is folded into that one commit by amending, so a removed secret never survives in history. The packager adds CLAUDE.md, setup.sh, README, LICENSE, CONTRIBUTING and issue templates, and the sanitizer runs again on exactly what will ship. Only after your yes does it run gh repo create --public and push, and only if the commit is the one that was scanned. Other commands verify, package, list or show the status of staged projects.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/opensource-pipeline"
        },
