          "text": "A network cleanup and growth workflow for X and LinkedIn, treating outreach as part of who you follow rather than a one-way prospect list. It starts from your priorities, target roles and industries, platforms, a do-not-touch list and a mode, then pulls your following and connection lists. Positive signals are reciprocity, recent activity, fit with your priorities, bridge value (how well someone connects you to people you want to reach), role relevance and real engagement; negatives are abandoned accounts, stale one-way follows, off-topic noise and repeated non-response. Mutuals and real bridges are penalized less. On X it prunes only accounts you follow, never your followers; on LinkedIn it prunes outbound follows more freely and sends 1st-degree connections to review. Expansion candidates come from the lead-intelligence skill and research, each with a channel: X DM, LinkedIn message or an Apple Mail draft, written after running brand-voice so they sound like you. The result is a review pack, and nothing is applied before you approve it.",
