          "text": "A coordination workflow for maintainers who keep public work on GitHub and internal scheduling in Linear. It reads the public surface first: issue or PR state, author and branch, review comments, CI status and linked issues. Each item lands in one of four states: merge when self-contained and ready, port or rebuild when the idea is useful but should be re-landed by the maintainers, close when wrong, stale, unsafe or duplicated, and park when useful but unscheduled. Linear gets an item only when work is actively planned, spans repos or workstreams, needs internal ownership or belongs to a larger program lane, rather than mirroring every issue. While work is active, GitHub says publicly what's happening and Linear tracks owner, priority and lane; when it ships or is rejected, the resolution is posted on GitHub and the Linear task is marked. If the real blocker is product direction, it says so. It was written for ECC's own backlog, so its rebuild advice and examples name ECC.",
