      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Ranks your X or LinkedIn connections by who can best introduce you to your targets, with a weighted bridge score that decays per hop.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to know which of your connections can get you a warm intro to a list of people, companies or an ideal customer profile"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Weights each target, scores each connection by its paths to them, halving the value per extra hop, then adds second-order reach and a responsiveness bonus"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Top bridges with scores, best targets and a recommended ask, conditional one-hop paths, and the targets with no warm path"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike its outreach siblings",
              "text": "ECC's lead-intelligence and connections-optimizer build outreach and network pruning on top of this same scoring"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The scoring layer behind ECC's networking skills, usable on its own. You give it targets (people, companies or an ideal customer profile), your graph on X, LinkedIn or both, and what matters to you: role, industry, geography, responsiveness. Each target gets a weight. A connection's base bridge score sums those weights over its paths to the targets with a decay factor, usually 0.5, so each extra hop halves the contribution. It then adds second-order reach through people your connection knows and you don't, discounted by about 0.3, and boosts the result for responsive or close contacts. Connections fall into three tiers: direct paths become warm-intro asks, one-hop paths conditional asks, and targets with no viable bridge go to direct outreach or a gap to fill in your network. The output lists each top bridge with base and extended scores, best targets, a path summary and a recommended action. Its output is a ranking, not messages; it suggests running brand-voice before drafting any intro request.",
