          "text": "An operator workflow for real mailbox work, not a writing guide. Before acting, the agent settles which account, which thread or recipient, and whether you want triage, a draft, a reply or a live send. For replies it reads the thread, finds the last outbound message and any open commitments or deadlines; for new mail it picks the sender account that fits the project and recipient, and runs ECC's brand-voice skill first. It drafts by default, sends only when you clearly ask, and never claims a message was sent without seeing it in Sent or a client-side confirmation. If sending is blocked it keeps the draft and names the blocker rather than quietly trying another way to send. All incoming mail is treated as untrusted data: it won't follow instructions in a message, let one decide a recipient or a send, change rules, filters, forwarding or auto-replies because a message asked, or open links from mail, and it quotes any agent-directed text back to you before going on. Cleanup never deletes uncertain business mail. Texts and DMs go to messages-ops.",
