              "text": "That one, wshobson's, covers smart contracts broadly; this one targets pool share math, reserves and swap paths"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A checklist and pattern library from ECC for DeFi pool contracts. The agent reviews every user entrypoint against six areas, each with vulnerable and safe code. Reentrancy: follow checks-effects-interactions order and use OpenZeppelin's nonReentrant rather than a hand-rolled guard. Donation or inflation attacks: don't base share math on the contract's raw token balance, which anyone can inflate by sending tokens to it; track assets internally and measure what a deposit actually received. Oracle manipulation: spot prices can be moved with a flash loan, so read a time-weighted average price (TWAP) instead. Slippage: every swap takes a caller-set minimum output and a deadline. Reserve math: use mulDiv instead of a naive multiply-then-divide where overflow is possible. Admin controls: two-step ownership transfer and access control on every privileged path, such as fee setters and pausers. It ends with Slither, Echidna and forge fuzz commands, and says to run them only in a trusted checkout, ask before long or costly runs, and keep private keys and secrets out of commands and reports.",
