          "text": "A design workflow from ECC for fragmented notifications. It starts from what exists: GitHub issues, PRs, reviews and CI, Linear movement, local hook and session events, desktop notifications, and any email or chat that's actually connected. Each event goes through capture, classification by urgency and owner, routing, collapsing of duplicates and an attached next action. The default severity model treats critical events (broken default-branch CI, security issues, failed deploys) as interruptions, high ones (review requests, failing PRs) as same-day alerts, medium ones as digest items and low ones as noise to suppress. Before adding channels it looks for the same event arriving in several places, repeated hook alerts and raw comment churn, aiming for one canonical summary, one owner, one primary channel and one fallback. For each need it defines source, gate, shape, channel and action, preferring hooks for automatic emission, skills for triage, an MCP bridge only when one is missing, and desktop notifications when they're enough. It never exposes tokens or webhook secrets, and returns a design to act on.",
