      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Troubleshoots BGP sessions that are down, flapping or missing routes with read-only checks of neighbor state, transport, route policy and AS paths.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A BGP neighbor is stuck in Idle or Active, a session is up but prefixes are missing, or unexpected prefixes are advertised"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Pins down the neighbor, address family, VRF and ASNs, reads state and last reset reason, proves reachability, then checks route policy"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "What each BGP state most likely means, read-only evidence for the incident, and a Python parser for BGP summary output"
            },
            {
              "label": "Leaves out",
              "text": "Clearing sessions or changing policy, timers or authentication, which it keeps for a reviewed change window"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A diagnostics-only BGP skill from ECC. The default is read-only evidence: BGP summary and neighbor detail, the route to the peer, TCP state on port 179, BGP log lines and the configured prefix-lists and route-maps. A state table says what to check first: Active means the TCP session isn't completing; OpenSent or OpenConfirm points at ASN, authentication, timers or capabilities; Established with zero prefixes points at inbound policy, max-prefix or address family. Transport checks ping and traceroute from the right source, including loopback update sources. Policy checks compare advertised, received and installed routes, and AS-path regexes use token boundaries such as _65001_ so they don't match longer ASNs. It doesn't assume global IPv4 unicast when VRFs, IPv6, VPNv4 or EVPN are in play. Clearing a session, changing neighbor settings or relaxing ACLs are change-window actions it won't suggest as diagnostics; if a reset is approved, it prefers a soft reset or route refresh. A Python parser turns summary output into rows, kept alongside the raw output.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/network-bgp-diagnostics"
