          "by:community",
          "performance",
          "observability",
          "verification"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "affaan-m/ecc/skills/parallel-execution-optimizer",
      "name": "parallel-execution-optimizer",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/affaan-m/ecc/parallel-execution-optimizer",
        "installs": 5600,
        "weeklyInstalls": [262, 161, 143, 232, 406, 400, 477, 443],
        "firstSeen": "2026-05-25"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Speeds up a task by splitting it into lanes, running independent reads and checks at once, isolating writes, and ending with a verification table.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a task done much faster through parallel work: concurrent agents, batched tool calls, isolated worktrees or many verification lanes"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Turns the task into a dependency graph of lanes, marks each parallel, sequential or gated, and runs lanes together only when their writes can't collide"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A lane matrix of write surface, risk and verification before the push, and a report of lanes run, blocked and checks passed after it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "Repetitive work on a set of records: prepare shared inputs once, then check, write and verify each record in turn"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Parallelize destructive commands, migrations, writes to the same table or live deploys without an explicit gate"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Speed here comes from doing independent work at once, not from cutting checks. The agent defines the goal and its done signal, splits the work into lanes such as a repo scan, a backend patch, a frontend patch and a deploy readback, and batches file reads, searches and status checks. Writes stay separated by file, worktree, branch, service or dataset, long builds and tests run in separate sessions that it polls, and a lane that hits a blocker pauses the lanes that depend on it. Lanes merge only once evidence shows they fit together. A second part covers a bounded set of similar records, such as many updates through one mapping: shared inputs are prepared once and reused while still valid, but every record gets its own version, permission and prerequisite check, a write protected against conflicting changes, and a verified outcome before it leaves the remaining list. Uncertain outcomes are reconciled before any retry, and a changed contract or failed prerequisite triggers a review. It lists failure modes such as conflicting edits, forgotten background sessions and skipped checks hidden behind a success summary.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/affaan-m/ecc/tree/d2ef2680594f9a17526a6e1a2e18b3d242c5d17b/skills/parallel-execution-optimizer"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:agents",
          "category:engineering",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "multi-agent",
          "agent-workflows",
          "verification"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "affaan-m/ecc/skills/data-throughput-accelerator",
      "name": "data-throughput-accelerator",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/affaan-m/ecc/data-throughput-accelerator",
        "installs": 5500,
        "weeklyInstalls": [259, 159, 142, 231, 411, 402, 465, 439],
        "firstSeen": "2026-05-25"
