            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "OpenClaw's macOS app, which can host Peekaboo Bridge for its Computer Control; the skill keeps the socket already selected"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A guide to Peekaboo, a macOS command-line tool that lets an agent see and operate app interfaces, with examples in its version 4 syntax. The agent lists running apps, then captures the target window with see, which returns a screenshot annotated with the window's UI elements. It reads those elements, acts on the intended app and window, and inspects the UI again to confirm the result, refreshing its view whenever the window changes rather than reusing old element IDs. For a plain screenshot it skips element detection. Rather than a full command reference, the skill sends the agent to each command's --help in the installed version, and maps the commands version 4 removed to their replacements. When it runs through OpenClaw's macOS app, it keeps the Bridge socket already selected and reports a missing host instead of switching providers. Troubleshooting covers removed commands, permission and host status, stale targets, and macOS 15's separate window picker prompt.",
