          "text": "OpenClaw's guide to ClawHub, its registry of plugins, skills and agent Templates at clawhub.ai. Asked for a capability, the agent searches plugins first, with the plugins tool or openclaw plugins search, and searches before saying something isn't available. Skills are searched, verified and installed with openclaw skills, into the current workspace or, with --global, for every local agent; the same command lists, checks and updates them. Templates are found through the registry's public API, paging through every result before claiming a full list, and added in the Control UI after reviewing the workspace files, skills, plugins, MCP servers and automations they bring; a reviewed local package can be previewed and added with openclaw templates. Removing a skill, and publishing or syncing your own, go through the standalone clawhub CLI, which asks for confirmation before it uninstalls.",
