          "text": "A small OpenClaw skill on top of CodexBar, a tool that tracks Codex and Claude usage. The bundled script runs codexbar cost for the provider you pick, or reads a cost JSON from a file or stdin, then works in one of two modes. Current mode takes the most recent day that has per-model figures and reports its costliest model, falling back to the last model used when those figures are missing; --model names a model instead. All mode adds up each model's cost across every day. Output is plain text by default, or JSON. The figures are cost only, since CodexBar doesn't break tokens down by model.",
