          "text": "A local text-to-speech skill from OpenClaw, built on sherpa-onnx's offline command-line TTS. Setup downloads the sherpa-onnx runtime for macOS, Linux or Windows and a voice model, by default Piper's en_US lessac voice in high quality, then records both folders as SHERPA_ONNX_RUNTIME_DIR and SHERPA_ONNX_MODEL_DIR in OpenClaw's config file. The agent then runs the wrapper script that ships in the skill folder with the text and an output path, and gets a WAV file. If a model folder holds more than one .onnx file, you name the one to use; the tokens file and data folder can be overridden too. For another voice, you download a different model from sherpa-onnx's tts-models release.",
