      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Asks a second model, GPT-5.5 Pro by default, for a review, debugging, refactoring or design pass over selected files, through the oracle CLI.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a stronger model's second opinion on a bug, a refactor, a design or a code review"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Bundles a prompt with the fewest files that hold the answer, previews the token cost, then makes one run"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The other model's answer, which the skill says to treat as advisory and check against code and tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "Engines",
              "text": "The API when OPENAI_API_KEY is set, otherwise a browser session for GPT or Gemini; Claude, Grok and multi-model runs need the API"
            },
            {
              "label": "Long runs",
              "text": "Pro runs can take long; a timed-out run is reattached from its stored session, not re-run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The oracle CLI from npm, plus an OpenAI API key or a browser session"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Oracle is a command-line tool that packs a prompt and a set of files into one request to another model, GPT-5.5 Pro by default. The skill's path: pick a tight file set, preview the payload and token spend with a dry run, then run it, in the browser for long Pro thinking or through the API. Since that model starts with no knowledge of the project, the skill gives a prompt template: a briefing with the stack and build and test commands, where things live, the exact question with verbatim errors and what was tried, constraints, and the output wanted. It covers including and excluding files with globs, which skip node_modules, dist and dotfiles by default and reject files over 1 MB, keeping .env files and keys out unless you ask, readable session slugs, and reattaching to sessions stored under ~/.oracle/sessions when a run detaches. Runs are one-shot, so for long investigations the agent writes a standalone prompt and file set it can rerun days later.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/tree/f99d785d2ac6269b37a1c88eb8d5ef2283b76b99/skills/oracle"
        },
