          ],
          "text": "An OpenClaw guide to gifgrep, a command-line GIF search. The agent searches by keyword, caps the number of results, and prints URLs or JSON with each result's id, title, URL, preview URL, tags and size, or opens a terminal UI to browse. Downloads go to ~/Downloads, and --reveal shows the last one in Finder. From a GIF file it can save the frame at a given time as a PNG, or a sheet: one PNG grid of sampled frames, with the number of frames, columns and padding adjustable, which the skill suggests for quick reviews, docs, PRs and chat. Still previews in the terminal work only in Kitty and Ghostty. The skill also sets rules for using GIFs: check that a URL resolves, is served as image/gif and is really animated, record its source, license and attribution, and download it into the project rather than hotlinking when a local file is needed.",
