          "text": "An OpenClaw guide to camsnap, a command-line tool for RTSP and ONVIF network cameras and local webcams. Cameras are kept in ~/.config/camsnap/config.yaml and added by name, host, user and password, and discover finds them on the network. The agent takes a snapshot, records a clip of a set duration, or watches a camera for motion above a threshold with an action to run; doctor probes the connections. The skill says to make a short test capture before longer clips. On macOS it also lists local webcams, snaps from one by device number, and reads, moves or homes pan-tilt-zoom cameras. Those moves are checked against the position reached and exit with an error if the camera didn't get there; if moves keep missing, the skill suggests turning off the camera's own AI framing.",
