          "text": "A short OpenClaw guide to songsee, a command-line tool that renders pictures of audio. A plain run draws a spectrogram, which shows a sound's frequencies over time. Listing several views in --viz draws them as a grid of panels: mel, chroma, HPSS (harmonic and percussive separation), self-similarity, loudness, tempogram, MFCC and spectral flux. Flags pick a palette such as magma or viridis, the image size, the FFT window and hop, a frequency range, a start time and duration, and JPG or PNG output. WAV and MP3 decode natively; other formats go through ffmpeg if it's installed.",
