      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Rewrites brand messaging and website copy with Donald Miller's StoryBrand framework, casting the customer as the hero and your brand as the guide.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Your homepage, pitch or emails aren't landing, or you need a one-liner that says what you do"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Builds the message on Miller's seven-part story: a hero who wants one thing, a problem, a guide, a plan, a call to action, failure to avoid and success"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Copy built from those parts and a score out of 10 from seven checks plus a one-liner test"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike made-to-stick",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, makes any idea memorable; this one gives brand copy one story structure"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Based on Donald Miller's Building a StoryBrand. Its premise is that customers buy what they understand fastest, and a brand that casts itself as the hero competes with its own customer. Its seven parts, called SB7: the customer as hero with one specific want; a problem named on three levels, external, internal (how it feels) and philosophical (why it's wrong), with a concrete villain; the brand as guide, showing empathy and authority such as testimonials and logos; a plan of three or four steps plus promises that remove risk; one direct call to action, such as Buy Now, repeated down the page, with a lower-commitment one such as a free guide; a glimpse of what failure costs; and a vivid picture of success. Each part comes with copy patterns and examples for homepages, emails, ads and sales calls. The one-liner, \"We help [character] who struggle with [problem] to [solution] so they can [result]\", must pass the cocktail party test: someone can repeat it after hearing it once. Reference files hold a BrandScript worksheet, website wireframes, email sequences and sales scripts.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wondelai/skills/tree/d8d5d75f83da9f16d8aad5bab5f5b341a4770a30/storybrand-messaging"
        },
