        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a marketing plan on Allan Dib's nine-square 1-Page Marketing Plan, from target market and message to lead nurture, lifetime value and referrals.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You don't know where to start with marketing, or need a plan from finding customers to getting referrals"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Fills a three-by-three grid: target market, message and media; lead capture, nurture and conversion; experience, lifetime value and referrals"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A one-page marketing plan and a score out of 10 by how many squares pass their check"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike scorecard-marketing",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, covers quiz funnels, one way to capture leads; this one plans the whole customer journey"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Based on Allan Dib's The 1-Page Marketing Plan. It treats marketing as a process rather than scattered tactics, in three phases. Before: choose a niche with the PVP Index (personal fulfillment, value to the market, profitability), write a USP (unique selling proposition, why buy from you and not a competitor) that a rival's name couldn't fit, and pick channels by where the audience is, mastering one before adding another. During: capture leads with a lead magnet, something useful exchanged for contact details, nurture them, mostly by email, with about three value messages per ask, and convert with risk reversal such as guarantees and trials. After: deliver an experience worth talking about, raise lifetime value with upsells and tiers, and ask for referrals at the moment of peak satisfaction. Every ad follows direct response rules: trackable, with a specific offer and a reason to act now. Each square has copy patterns and most have an ethical line, such as one-click unsubscribe and only real deadlines. A square counts toward the score only when it passes its diagnostic question, such as completing \"We are the only ___ that ___\". Reference files hold a blank template, worked examples and a guide per square.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wondelai/skills/tree/d8d5d75f83da9f16d8aad5bab5f5b341a4770a30/one-page-marketing"
        },
