      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Speeds up web pages with Ilya Grigorik's High Performance Browser Networking: fewer round trips, layered caching, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3, and Core Web Vitals.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Pages load slowly, Core Web Vitals are red, or you're choosing caching rules, an HTTP version or WebSocket versus server-sent events"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Cuts round trips across DNS, TCP, TLS and HTTP, unblocks rendering, layers caches and picks the right real-time transport"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A score out of 10 from eight checks, weighted toward real-user metrics, with the fix for each failure"
            },
            {
              "label": "Its thresholds",
              "text": "Time to first byte under 800ms, LCP under 2.5s, INP under 200ms and CLS under 0.1"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Based on Ilya Grigorik's High Performance Browser Networking. Its premise is that latency, not bandwidth, is the bottleneck: every request pays for a DNS lookup, the TCP handshake and TLS negotiation before data flows, so the biggest wins come from fewer round trips. It covers preconnect and DNS prefetch hints, TLS 1.3 and connection reuse; HTTP/2 multiplexing, which makes old workarounds like domain sharding harmful, HTTP/3, and 103 Early Hints instead of server push; the critical rendering path, with critical CSS inlined, scripts deferred, key resources preloaded and images lazy-loaded; caching with Cache-Control, content-hashed file names, ETags, service workers and correct Vary headers on CDNs; Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP and CLS, for loading, responsiveness and layout stability), measured on real users; and WebSocket versus server-sent events for live data, with heartbeats and reconnection. Examples are HTML tags, HTTP headers and short server or JavaScript snippets. A page with any of the four field metrics in the red scores 3 or less. Reference files go deeper on each area.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wondelai/skills/tree/d8d5d75f83da9f16d8aad5bab5f5b341a4770a30/high-perf-browser"
        },
        "tags": [
