      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs quiz and assessment funnels that score prospects and turn them into qualified leads, after Daniel Priestley's Scorecard Marketing.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a quiz, assessment or grader that brings in qualified leads instead of a PDF download"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Designs four parts: a landing page hook, scored questions after an email form, results by tier, and follow-up by score"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A funnel design, a launch checklist and a score out of 10 from six checks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike one-page-marketing",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, covers a whole marketing plan; this one builds one lead-capture funnel"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Based on Scorecard Marketing by Daniel Priestley and Glen Carlson; Priestley co-founded ScoreApp, a platform built around the method. The premise is that a quiz scoring people on something they care about uncovers needs they hadn't acted on, and it cites 30-50% conversion against 3-10% for PDF lead magnets. The landing page leads with a concept hook, one of five types such as moving toward a goal or readiness for a decision, and says it takes under three minutes. The questionnaire asks for name and email first, so abandoned quizzes still yield leads, then 8-15 questions for cold traffic, grouped into two to seven scored categories, plus qualifying questions such as budget. The results page shows the overall and per-category score, with different content and a different next step per tier, from a free event for low scorers to a consultation for high ones. Follow-up emails send results at once and nurture each tier separately. Its ethical lines include never adjusting a score to steer someone to the offer. Six diagnostic questions set the score. Reference files hold 50+ concepts by industry, the psychology, building the tool and funnel analytics.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wondelai/skills/tree/d8d5d75f83da9f16d8aad5bab5f5b341a4770a30/scorecard-marketing"
