        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Helps a growing company adopt Gino Wickman's Entrepreneurial Operating System: a shared vision, 90-day priorities, a weekly scorecard and weekly leadership meetings.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A growing company feels chaotic, the same problems keep coming back, or leadership isn't aligned"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Puts the six EOS components in place, vision, people, data, issues, process and traction, each with its own tool"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A score out of 10 from six checks, a 1-5 checkup per component and the next action for each gap"
            },
            {
              "label": "Made for",
              "text": "Companies with $2M-$50M in revenue and 10-250 employees"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Based on Gino Wickman's Traction, which describes the Entrepreneurial Operating System (EOS), a way of running a business. Vision goes on a two-page Vision/Traction Organizer: core values, core focus, a 10-year target, marketing strategy, a 3-year picture, a 1-year plan, quarterly priorities and an issues list. People are placed on an accountability chart with one owner per seat, under a Visionary and an Integrator who runs the business day to day, and judged by fit with the core values and whether they get, want and have the capacity for their role. Data is a weekly scorecard of 5-15 numbers, each with an owner and a goal. Issues are solved with IDS: identify the root cause, discuss, then solve with assigned action items. Core processes are documented in 5-20 steps and followed by all. Traction comes from rocks, three to seven 90-day priorities that are either done or not, and the Level 10 meeting: 90 minutes every week, same agenda, 60 of them for solving issues, rated 1 to 10 at the end. It sketches a two-year rollout and when to hire a certified EOS Implementer.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wondelai/skills/tree/d8d5d75f83da9f16d8aad5bab5f5b341a4770a30/traction-eos"
        },
