          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. A paid-search playbook the agent applies when you ask for a campaign structure, keywords, ad copy or a performance review. Accounts split into brand, non-brand, competitor and Performance Max campaigns, with search ad groups of at most 15 to 20 keywords that share intent and a similar landing page. Keyword research starts from seed terms (your product, competitors' ads, customer and support language), expands with Google Keyword Planner and tools like SEMrush, and assigns broad, phrase or exact match, with negatives such as \"free\" or \"jobs\". Responsive search ads get 15 headlines of up to 30 characters, pinned as keyword, value proposition and call to action, and 4 descriptions of up to 90, from templates by angle. A selection guide says when to use Maximize Conversions, Target CPA (30+ conversions a month), Target ROAS, Maximize Clicks or manual CPC, with suggested bid adjustments by device, location, schedule and audience. Its report template tables spend, clicks, conversions, CPA and ROAS per campaign, checks CTR and conversion rate against benchmarks and lists keywords to pause, and weekly and monthly checklists cover search terms, quality scores, landing pages and budget shifts.",
