          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You describe the calendar routine you want automated and the agent writes it up as a workflow: a trigger, such as 6 AM on weekdays or an hour before a meeting of 30 minutes or more, then numbered steps and the message to send. Its five workflows count meetings, hours, free time and back-to-back slots for a Slack morning digest; draft a meeting prep doc with attendee profiles from LinkedIn and your CRM, recent emails, a suggested agenda and talking points; block deep work, admin time and buffers for the coming week around high-priority tasks from Todoist, Asana or Notion; turn Calendly bookings into calendar events, HubSpot records, a confirmation email and a Slack alert; and report time spent by category, meeting fragmentation and a productivity score each Friday. Its example for the digest ends with the n8n nodes to add, from a schedule trigger to Google Calendar, a code node and Slack, and an offer to generate the full n8n workflow JSON. The workflows are outlines for you to build, not files to import.",
