          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You paste raw notes, a transcript or a description of the meeting, say what kind of meeting it was and any format you need, and the agent restructures it. It picks out action items from phrases like \"we need to\", \"can you\" or a name followed by a verb, decisions from \"we've decided\", \"agreed\" or consensus language, and owners when someone is named or a role is given, otherwise defaulting to the organizer and flagging unassigned items for follow-up. Its default output gives date and attendees, a two-to-three sentence summary, key points, decisions, an action table with owner, due date and priority, next steps and a parking lot for items to handle later. It also has templates for standups (yesterday, today and blockers per person), client meetings (their requests, your commitments and theirs) and project reviews (status, metrics against targets, risks and decisions needed). You can ask for bullets, tables, prose or formal minutes, at executive, standard or detailed length. It warns that it can't verify commitments or deadlines, so review the notes before sending them.",
