          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You name the product and platforms, and the agent writes copy that fits each format's limits. For Google, a responsive search ad's 15 headlines of 30 characters and 4 descriptions of 90, with the keyword, brand, a call to action and numbers each in several headlines, plus Performance Max and display formats. For Meta, feed primary text with the first 125 characters visible, a 40-character headline and a call-to-action button, plus Stories and Reels. For TikTok, 100-character in-feed text and Spark Ads captions with 3-5 hashtags; for LinkedIn, sponsored content and message ads. Copy follows one of three frameworks: AIDA (attention, interest, desire, action), PAS (problem, agitation, solution) or BAB (before, after, bridge), with headline templates by angle and three Facebook templates: problem-solution, story and direct offer. For testing, it writes 3-5 variants per ad group, with example tests that pit an offer, social proof and a problem headline against each other, or a free start, a discount claim and a how-it-works call to action.",
