            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You share the contract as PDF, Word or text and say what kind it is, which party you are, the jurisdiction and any concerns. The agent reads it against 15 risk patterns, each with the wording to look for and a fix: six high risks (unlimited liability, broad IP assignment, unilateral termination, one-sided indemnification, broad waivers of rights, missing data protection), eight medium ones such as auto-renewal traps, excessive penalties, broad non-competes, perpetual confidentiality, an unfavorable venue or payment terms, uncontrolled scope changes and missing force majeure, and one low (no audit rights). A completeness checklist covers parties, dates, term, scope, payment, termination, key clauses and signatures. Jurisdiction notes cover US at-will employment, overtime and California's ban on non-competes, EU data protection and notice periods, China's labor contract rules and paid non-competes, and UK statutory rights. The report ends with must, should and nice-to-have changes and a disclaimer, and you can follow up to have a clause explained or plan a negotiation. Its frontmatter points to knowledge files in the repo's office-mcp server, but its instructions never load them.",
