      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Tailors your resume to a job posting, matching its requirements and keywords for applicant tracking systems, and rewrites bullets around quantified results.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're applying for a specific job and don't want to send the same generic resume"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A table of the job's requirements against your experience, keywords to add, the full tailored resume, each change with its reason, and tips for the cover letter, LinkedIn and interview"
            },
            {
              "label": "Its rules",
              "text": "Use the posting's exact keywords and standard headers, avoid tables and graphics that trip up applicant tracking systems, and write bullets as verb, what, number and context"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Invent experience: it asks about gaps, such as a skill the posting wants that your resume doesn't mention"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You paste your resume and the full job description, plus any context such as a career change or an internal transfer. The agent lists the posting's key requirements, marks which you meet and which are gaps, and asks about experience you may have left out. It then rewrites the resume: keywords copied exactly from the posting, acronyms both spelled out and abbreviated, standard section headers and plain formatting so applicant tracking systems can parse it, and bullets rebuilt as power verb, what you did, a quantified result and context. It lists power verbs by category, and must-have sections and keywords for tech, business, marketing, healthcare and finance roles; for a career change it maps your old field's terms to the new one's, such as lesson plans to learning curricula. Its answer includes the full tailored resume with every change explained and suggestions for the cover letter, LinkedIn and interview prep, and it answers common questions such as page length by years of experience. It can't see your formatting, so you apply the changes yourself.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/claude-office-skills/skills/tree/9c4c7d5cd2813a8936bf2c9fdb174ea883b85a11/resume-tailor"
