            {
              "label": "Limits",
              "text": "Simplified taxes, no currency effects, no complex corporate structures or automatic one-off items; it isn't accounting advice"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You provide two or three years of historical income statements and balance sheets (cash flow optional), set the drivers, and choose the model's scope. The agent links the statements the standard way: net income flows into retained earnings, cash is the balancing item on the balance sheet, changes in balance sheet items drive the cash flow statement, and ending cash flows back. It spells out each formula, for example revenue as last year's times one plus growth, receivables as revenue times DSO over 365, PP&E as prior PP&E plus capex minus depreciation, and operating cash flow as net income plus D&A less increases in working capital. The output is a fixed set of Markdown tables, a base year plus five projected years. Its tips suggest asking for scenarios and sensitivity tables. Its frontmatter lists spreadsheet and chart tools of the repo's office-mcp server, but its instructions never call them, so you get tables in the reply, not a spreadsheet.",
