            {
              "label": "Needs from you",
              "text": "The job posting's text, since it can't open postings, and your real achievements and figures; its own example adds numbers the request never gave, so check every one"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You share the job posting or describe the role, tell the agent about your relevant experience and anything to highlight, and it writes a tailored letter of three or four paragraphs on one page. Its rules: open with a specific achievement, connection or referral instead of \"I am writing to apply\" or \"To whom it may concern\", turn duties into numbers (\"grew sales 45% YoY, adding $2M in revenue\" rather than \"increased sales\"), show research into the company's news, products or values, and focus on what you offer rather than what you want. It warns against repeating your resume, being generic, typos, the wrong company name, raising salary and negative language. A worked example writes a letter for a senior software engineer applying to Stripe and fills it with figures the request never gave, such as $50M a month processed and transaction failures cut by 40%. Its frontmatter lists Word and PDF tools of the repo's office-mcp server, but its instructions never call them.",
