          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You give the main question and any sub-questions, why you need the answer, and the scope, perspectives (technical, business, social, legal), time frame and depth. The agent then works in five phases: scoping (key terms, boundaries, what success looks like), gathering (subtopics, diverse perspectives, facts and quotes), analysis (themes, patterns, comparing viewpoints, judging reliability and bias), synthesis (insights, conclusions, gaps, recommendations) and reporting, with balanced perspectives and cited sources. The report template runs from an executive summary with key findings and a recommendation to appendices, and ends with a reminder to verify findings with primary sources before critical decisions. Unless the agent has search tools, it works from what the model already knows, which has a training cutoff. Its frontmatter lists document and spreadsheet tools of the repo's office-mcp server, but its instructions never call them.",
