              "text": "Markdown for Marp, a Markdown slide tool, in its gaia theme with page numbers; its example is a ten-slide introduction to Docker"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike ppt-visual",
              "text": "That one, from the same repo, specs the design of one slide; this one drafts the content of a whole deck"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "Know your audience, one idea per slide, at most six bullets of six words, suggest images or diagrams, open with a hook and close with a call to action"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "Write a PowerPoint file: the office-mcp slide tools in its frontmatter are never called in its instructions"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You give a topic, outline or rough notes, the audience and how many slides, and the agent drafts the whole deck. Its structure: a title slide with subtitle and presenter, an agenda of three to five topics, an introduction with a hook and why it matters, three to five main sections each with a heading, three to five bullets or a visual and supporting data, a summary of takeaways with a call to action, and a closing slide with thanks, contact details and a prompt for questions. The skill shows this as Python pseudo-code that outlines, expands each section, adds visual suggestions and converts the slides to Marp Markdown, plus a finished ten-slide Docker talk as an example. It points to Marp, Slidev and reveal.js as tools for Markdown and HTML slides.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/claude-office-skills/skills/tree/9c4c7d5cd2813a8936bf2c9fdb174ea883b85a11/ai-slides"
