          "text": "From Claude Office Skills, based, it says, on n8n's AI workflow templates. You describe the agent you want and the agent drafts its design. It sorts agents into five types by complexity: reactive, conversational, tool-using, reasoning and multi-agent. Tools are grouped into data retrieval, actions, computation and generation, each defined with a name, description, parameters and the API it calls. Memory can be a buffer of recent messages, a rolling summary, a vector store or an entity tracker, and the context window is managed by a sliding window, relevance ranking or tiers, within a sample 8,000-token budget split across system prompt, tools, memory, query and response. Reasoning follows ReAct (thought, action, observation) or a plan, execute and synthesize loop. Platform outlines cover a Slack bot that reads thread history, a Telegram bot that handles voice, images and documents, and a streaming web chat with sessions in Redis.",
