      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reads, filters, deduplicates and merges SARIF results from scanners such as CodeQL and Semgrep, resolving each finding's severity correctly.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have SARIF output from CodeQL, Semgrep or another scanner and need to query, merge, deduplicate, diff or gate CI on it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Picks jq for quick queries, or Python with pysarif, sarif-tools or its bundled helpers for scripts, aggregation and CI checks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Catches",
              "text": "Severity gates that only read result.level, which CodeQL never sets, so a repo full of errors passes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Running scans or writing rules; it points to the Semgrep and CodeQL skills for those"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits' static-analysis plugin, alongside its semgrep and codeql skills. SARIF is the standard JSON format static analysis tools use to report findings. The skill's central warning is that a result's severity often lives on its rule: CodeQL records it as the rule's default level, so a CI gate that reads result.level counts zero errors. It resolves severity in the spec's order, from the result's kind and level to the matched rule's default and finally \"warning\", and every query it gives starts from that. For deduplication it prefers the tool's own fingerprints and falls back to hashing rule, full normalized path, line and message, keeping the directory so two files with the same name stay two findings. It also covers normalizing paths across tools, validating against the schema, streaming files over 100MB with ijson, diffing a baseline against a new run, converting to CSV or HTML with sarif-tools, and GitHub Actions steps that upload SARIF and fail on errors. Bundled resources hold 40+ jq queries, a standard-library Python helper module, and two fixtures with exactly one error each to test a gate against.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/static-analysis/skills/sarif-parsing"
        },
