      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews a smart contract project against Trail of Bits' development guidelines, from documentation and upgradeability to dependencies and tests, with prioritized recommendations.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want to know whether a smart contract project follows development best practices, or need advice on its design, upgrades or tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Explores the code, drafts a plain-English system description and diagrams, reviews architecture and implementation across 11 areas, and asks about design choices"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "System documentation, an architecture and implementation review with file and line references, and recommendations ranked Critical to Low"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works on",
              "text": "Mainly Solidity, using Slither for diagrams and upgradeability checks when available; it adapts to Rust, Cairo and other platforms"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Trail of Bits' Building Secure Contracts development guidelines, applied to your codebase. The 11 areas are documentation and specifications, including NatSpec; what runs on-chain versus off-chain; upgradeability, weighing migration against upgrades; delegatecall proxies, such as storage layout, initialization and function shadowing; function composition; inheritance; events; common pitfalls such as reentrancy, overflow and access control; dependencies, including copied code; testing and verification, from coverage to fuzzing and formal verification; and platform guidance such as compiler version and inline assembly. A section that seems not to apply, such as upgradeability in a project without proxies, is skipped only after searching the code, since upgradeability can hide in ownable patterns or delegatecall. It rejects generic best-practice advice in favour of project-specific findings with file and line references, and ends with a prioritized roadmap. Detailed criteria, deliverable templates and an example report live in separate resource files.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/building-secure-contracts/skills/guidelines-advisor"
