          "text": "Trail of Bits' token integration checklist, from its building-secure-contracts plugin, combined with its database of weird ERC20 behavior. Weird tokens are real tokens that break assumptions: USDT returns no value from transfer, STA and PAXG take a fee on transfer, Ampleforth changes balances outside transfers, USDC and USDT can block addresses or be upgraded, DAI can be flash-minted, and decimals range from 2 to 24. Its ten categories cover general considerations such as audits and security contacts, contract composition, owner privileges like minting, pausing and upgrades, ERC20 conformity, risks from extensions such as hooks and rebasing, token scarcity, the weird patterns, integration safety such as safe transfer wrappers and measuring balances before and after a transfer, and ERC721 conformity and risks. It rejects shortcuts such as trusting a passing ERC20 check, a reputable team or OpenZeppelin to cover integration risks, and if Slither can't run it checks those criteria by hand or documents why it couldn't. Detailed criteria and report templates live in separate resource files.",
