          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits. The scanner pulls the Firebase config from google-services.json, XML resources, assets, smali code and DEX strings, then checks for open sign-up, anonymous auth and email enumeration, unauthenticated reads and writes on the Realtime Database, document access and collection listing on Firestore, bucket listing and write access on Storage, unauthenticated Cloud Functions, and exposed Remote Config. It writes test entries to the live backend and removes them afterwards. Unauthenticated database reads or writes, storage writes and open sign-up on a private app rate critical; anonymous auth, bucket listing and collection listing high; email enumeration, reachable functions and exposed Remote Config medium. APKs that failed to decompile or had no Firebase config are reported separately instead of counted as clean, since an app may not use Firebase or may hide its config beyond what the scanner extracts. If the scanner writes no report, the agent falls back to manual tests from a reference file. It rejects excuses such as \"the API key is public anyway\", since a public key doesn't justify open rules, and \"it's an internal app\", since APKs can be extracted from any device.",
