    {
      "id": "trailofbits/skills/plugins/building-secure-contracts/skills/cosmos-vulnerability-scanner",
      "name": "cosmos-vulnerability-scanner",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/trailofbits/skills/cosmos-vulnerability-scanner",
        "installs": 5700,
        "weeklyInstalls": [102, 105, 95, 119, 121, 157, 159, 174],
        "firstSeen": "2026-01-19"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Scans Cosmos SDK modules and CosmWasm contracts for chain-halting, fund-losing bugs with parallel subagents, writing each finding to its own markdown file.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're auditing custom x/ modules, IBC integrations or CosmWasm contracts on a Cosmos chain, especially before launch"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "A discovery subagent inventories the chain and its threat model, then three to six scanner subagents check their patterns in parallel, on consensus-critical code only"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A CLAUDE.md at the repo root with the inventory and threat model, and one markdown file per finding in .bughunt_cosmos/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "25 core SDK patterns, 16 IBC, 10 EVM and 3 CosmWasm, updated for SDK v0.53"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "An agent that can spawn subagents"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits' building-secure-contracts plugin. Its principle is that a bug matters for a chain halt or fund loss only on the consensus path: BeginBlock, EndBlock, FinalizeBlock, message handlers and the AnteHandler. A map iteration in a CLI command or a panic in a query handler isn't reported. Non-determinism that makes validators compute different state is the top class, because it halts every validator at once. The discovery step reads go.mod for the SDK and IBC versions, since patterns changed across v0.47, v0.50 and v0.53, and decides whether the EVM, IBC and CosmWasm scanners run. Core, state and advanced scanners always run, covering non-determinism, ABCI, signers, AnteHandler security, bookkeeping, bank misuse, pagination, governance, arithmetic, storage keys and crypto. Severity runs from critical for fund loss and high for chain halts to medium for denial of service and low for logic issues. Every scanner must report on each of its patterns, and one that skips any is asked again. It rejects excuses such as \"ValidateBasic catches this\" or \"the IBC counterparty is trusted\".",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/building-secure-contracts/skills/cosmos-vulnerability-scanner"
        },
