        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Generates a .devcontainer for your project with Claude Code, sandboxing tools and the toolchains for the Python, Node, Rust or Go it detects.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want Claude Code to work in an isolated container instead of directly on your machine"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Reads the project name and languages from package.json, pyproject.toml, Cargo.toml or go.mod, then fills its templates with matching extensions, settings and setup commands"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Dockerfile, devcontainer.json, post_install.py, .zshrc and an install.sh that adds a devc command, all in .devcontainer/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Inside",
              "text": "Claude Code without permission prompts, Python 3.13 via uv, Node 22, ripgrep, fd, fzf, tmux, ast-grep, bubblewrap, and iptables for network rules"
            },
            {
              "label": "Starts with",
              "text": "VS Code's Reopen in Container, or devcontainer up from the command line"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits. The project name comes from the first of package.json, pyproject.toml, Cargo.toml or go.mod that has one, falling back to the directory name, and its slug names persistent volumes that keep shell history, Claude's config and GitHub CLI auth across rebuilds. Python projects get the Python, Pylance and Ruff extensions and uv sync; Node projects get ESLint and Prettier and an install command matched to the lockfile; Rust and Go add their devcontainer features. Several languages are merged into one configuration. Inside the container, .devcontainer/ and your ~/.gitconfig are mounted read-only, the NET_ADMIN capability lets you restrict outbound traffic with iptables, npm install scripts are off and packages must be a day old before npm installs them. Claude Code is set to bypassPermissions, so it acts without asking inside the container, and your CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is forwarded in from your machine. Its image also adds the anthropics/skills, trailofbits/skills and trailofbits/skills-curated plugin marketplaces. It is for development environments, not production containers, and not for changing a devcontainer you already have.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/devcontainer-setup/skills/devcontainer-setup"
