      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Audits Cairo contracts on StarkNet for six vulnerabilities, from felt252 overflow to unchecked L1 handler senders and signature replay, with a verdict for each.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're auditing a StarkNet contract, an L1-L2 bridge or signature verification code written in Cairo"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Greps for felt252 arithmetic, checks every L1 handler, signature nonce and bridge path against checklists, then runs Trail of Bits' Caracal analyzer"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A coverage table giving all six patterns found, clear or n/a with evidence, then findings with attack scenario and recommended fix"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "felt252 overflow, L1 address conversion, failed L1-to-L2 messages, overconstrained L1-L2 coupling, signature replay and unchecked from_address"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits' building-secure-contracts plugin, one of its per-chain scanners. An unchecked from_address in an L1 handler is rated critical, because any L1 contract can then drive it, for example to mint tokens without a deposit. felt252 values wrap silently, so balances should use u128 or u256; L1 addresses must be checked against the StarkNet field prime before they cross; messages need a cancellation path for when they can't be consumed; and signatures need a nonce and a domain separator naming the chain and contract. Every row of the coverage table needs a verdict, clear names what was searched for and n/a needs a reason, because a report silent on four patterns reads like a clean contract. It rejects trusting a clean Caracal run, which reaches only some of the patterns, assuming Cairo 1's overflow checks cover felt252, and accepting \"the L1 side validates that\" without reading the L1 contract. It suggests unit tests, full L1-L2 roundtrip tests and Caracal in CI.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/building-secure-contracts/skills/cairo-vulnerability-scanner"
