      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Interprets Culture Index behavioral profiles for one person or a team: traits, burnout risk, hiring profiles, manager coaching, onboarding and conflict.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have Culture Index survey results, as a PDF or extracted JSON, and want to know what they mean for a person or a team"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Extracts trait scores from the PDF with its script, then takes on one of 11 tasks, from reading one profile to mediating a conflict"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An interpretation with key findings and recommended actions, such as a team's gas, brake and glue balance or a burnout flag"
            },
            {
              "label": "Reads traits",
              "text": "By their distance from the red arrow, the population mean, rather than their 0-10 values, except Logic and Ingenuity"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also",
              "text": "Predicts traits from an interview transcript, before a candidate has taken the survey"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits. Culture Index is a behavioral survey with two graphs: Survey traits, which the skill treats as hardwired, and Job behaviors, how someone adapts at work. A large gap between them means behavior modification that drains energy; energy utilization, Job EU divided by Survey EU, flags stress and burnout risk above 130% and frustration and flight risk below 70%. Gas, brake and glue are its team roles: high Autonomy drives results, high Conformity controls quality and high Social holds relationships together. Its other workflows compare profiles, suggest motivators, define the trait profile a role needs, coach a manager on a direct report, debrief a candidate and plan a new hire's first 90 days. It never estimates scores by eye from a PDF, which it says is off by 20-30%, and stops if uv isn't installed. It calls no trait good or bad, treats CI as one data point, never the sole basis for hiring or firing, and isn't for DISC, Myers-Briggs or other assessments.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/culture-index/skills/interpreting-culture-index"
