      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Improves a Claude Code skill in an autonomous loop of reviews and fixes until a review finds no critical or major issues, without committing.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A skill you're writing has quality problems and you want them fixed until it passes review, or to resume after the loop escalated"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Starts the code-improver plugin's background workflow, which alternates the plugin-dev skill-reviewer agent with a fixer agent round after round"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Fixes in your working tree, a findings ledger on disk, and a result: converged, capped but not converged, escalated or halted"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stops",
              "text": "On a clean review, at 5 rounds by default, when fixes stop converging, or when a change falls outside the skill's plugin folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike a one-time review",
              "text": "The skill-reviewer agent reviews once; this one keeps fixing and re-reviewing until a review comes back clean"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Claude Code's Workflow tool, the code-improver plugin it ships in, and the plugin-dev plugin from claude-plugins-official"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Trail of Bits' code-improver plugin. The skill finds the target skill, by path or by name among the repo's SKILL.md files, hands it to the plugin's workflow and relays the outcome; if the Workflow tool or the reviewer is missing it stops instead of improvising, because an inline loop has none of the guarantees. The ledger gives each finding a stable id and one verdict, fixed, rejected with a reason, or deferred, and is saved every round, so an escalated or interrupted run resumes without starting over. The loop escalates when blocking counts stop falling over three rounds, the same finding stays open three rounds in a row, or a finding is fixed twice; continuing means a fresh run with your decision passed in verbatim. A git-diff check after every fix round halts on any change outside the scope. Before finishing, a last pass strips loop narration, collapses version bumps to one and checks the docs against the code, and its own edits are checked too. Nothing is committed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/e4dd0bb5b15535f7c5a0834187dffba6ac37e4ff/plugins/code-improver/skills/skill-improver"
