            {
              "label": "Libraries",
              "text": "Framer Motion and Lenis for React or Next.js, plus React Three Fiber for 3D; GSAP, Lenis and SplitType for plain HTML or Astro"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A set of standards for when a page has to feel high-end rather than merely work. The agent first commits to a strong identity, such as one of the four directions it describes: editorial brutalism, organic fluidity, cyber/technical or cinematic pacing. Pages then get layers a plain build would skip: a preloader that waits for fonts and images and leaves with a reveal, a full-viewport hero whose headline is split into words or letters for staggered entrances, and a sticky header that hides on scroll down and returns on scroll up. Motion is tied to scrolling, with pinned sections, horizontal galleries and parallax, plus magnetic buttons, a custom cursor that trails the pointer and 3D hover transforms. Typography uses extreme scale contrast, with clamp() headlines up to 12vw, premium or variable fonts, a faint noise overlay and frosted-glass panels. Performance rules come with it: animate only transform and opacity, use will-change sparingly, keep cursor and hover effects behind a fine-pointer media query and heavy animation behind prefers-reduced-motion. Whenever you ask for a premium or immersive page, it wraps the result in smooth scrolling and staggered entrances by default.",
