      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Rewrites your tweets for reach, explaining each change through how X's open-sourced ranking algorithm weighs replies, retweets, communities and reputation.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You've drafted a tweet and want more reach, or want to know why one underperformed"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks the draft's message, audience, engagement triggers and risks against the models in Twitter's open-sourced recommendation code, then rewrites it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "What holds the tweet back, an optimized version, and why it should rank better"
            },
            {
              "label": "Terms",
              "text": "Real-graph predicts whether followers interact, SimClusters finds interest communities, TwHIN maps users to topics, Tweepcred scores an author's reputation"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not for",
              "text": "Grammar fixes, tone changes unrelated to reach, or posts for other platforms"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It explains Twitter's recommendation pipeline, from finding candidate tweets through ranking and filtering to delivery, and the signals ranking weighs: likes, replies, retweets and quotes; implicit ones such as profile visits, link clicks, time spent and bookmarks; and negative ones such as blocks, reports, mutes and quick scrolls. Each model gets a strategy: for Real-graph, content your followers will answer, such as a direct question or a nuanced hot take; for SimClusters, one clear topic in a community's own language; for TwHIN, staying in your area of expertise; for Tweepcred, consistent, thoughtful engagement and no engagement bait. To optimize a tweet, the agent finds its core message and audience, maps it to those models, checks which signals it triggers and what could draw blocks or blur your niche, then rewrites it. Its examples turn \"I fixed a bug today\" into a relatable story ending in a question, with a breakdown of why the new version works. Its best practices favour community over virality, authenticity, threads and replying quickly.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills/tree/be2a406907dbc61b73e6827ded415c96139d13a2/twitter-algorithm-optimizer"
        },
