          "text": "OpenAI's image-generation skill, a system skill that the latest Codex installs automatically. The agent first decides whether the request is a new image or an edit (reference images alone mean a new one) and whether it needs one asset or many, then collects the prompt, exact text, constraints and input images, labelling each image as a reference, the edit target or a compositing input. The prompt becomes a short labelled spec: a use case from a fixed list of 16 (product mockup, logo, style transfer, background extraction and others), asset type, subject, style, composition, lighting, palette, verbatim text, constraints and things to avoid. Detail is added only to generic prompts, never extra characters, brands or slogans, and edits restate what must stay unchanged on every pass. After each image it checks subject, style, composition, text accuracy and constraints, then iterates with one targeted change. Only the selected finals are copied into the workspace; previews are just shown inline. The CLI fallback, scripts/image_gen.py, needs the openai Python package and an OPENAI_API_KEY, and writes under output/imagegen/; the agent never switches to it on its own. The openai/skills repository is marked deprecated; its README points to openai/plugins for current Codex skills.",
