          ],
          "text": "OpenAI's guide to writing skills, a system skill that the latest Codex installs automatically. It explains what a skill is, a folder with a required SKILL.md and optional scripts for code that would otherwise be rewritten, references loaded into context only when needed, and assets used in the output, and the progressive loading behind it: the name and description are always in context, the body loads when the skill triggers, and bundled files load as needed. The process has six steps: gather concrete examples of how the skill will be used, asking you a few questions at a time; work out which scripts, references and assets those examples need; run init_skill.py to generate the folder, a SKILL.md template with TODO placeholders and agents/openai.yaml; write the resources, testing scripts by running them, then SKILL.md in the imperative; validate with quick_validate.py, which checks the frontmatter and naming rules; and iterate after real use. It also matches how specific instructions are to how fragile the task is, from free text to fixed scripts, and names skills in lowercase hyphen-case under 64 characters. The openai/skills repository is marked deprecated; its README points to openai/plugins for current Codex skills.",
