        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Has the agent read every source file of a project in full before you start working on it.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You start on a new or unfamiliar project and want the agent to know all of it before working"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Has the agent read every source file in full, however many there are, paging through large files in chunks"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An agent that has read the whole codebase; it writes nothing"
            },
            {
              "label": "Costs",
              "text": "Many tokens and much of the context window, more the larger the codebase; the skill argues this up-front cost makes later work cheaper"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike smart-explore",
              "text": "That one, from the same plugin, fetches only the symbols a task needs; this one reads everything at once"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The whole skill is one instruction: read every source file in full, which it calls critical and non-negotiable, using the Read tool's offset and limit to page through big files. It includes a note asking reviewers not to warn you about the cost, since front-loading the codebase is meant to make development cheaper over the project's life; on a large codebase the reading still takes many tokens and much of the context window. With claude-mem installed, each read also becomes a memory observation, and claude-mem's how-it-works skill suggests running it to load a whole repo into memory in one pass.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem/tree/31ebffbb112260183c91bbf901a4da22e241018f/plugin/skills/learn-codebase"
        },
