      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/thedotmack/claude-mem/pathfinder",
        "installs": 5500,
        "weeklyInstalls": [99, 93, 88, 93, 124, 110, 131, 151],
        "firstSeen": "2026-04-25"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "31ebffbb112260183c91bbf901a4da22e241018f",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Maps a codebase into per-feature flowcharts, finds duplicated systems and proposes a unified architecture, with make-plan prompts for each change.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You suspect a codebase solves the same problem in several places and want an architecture audit before refactoring"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Sends subagents to map each feature as a Mermaid flowchart labelled with file:line, then hunts duplicated concerns within and across features"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A PATHFINDER-<date>/ folder: feature inventory, flowcharts, duplication report, unified architecture proposal and copy-paste make-plan prompts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Write implementation code; it stops at the handoff prompts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Next",
              "text": "make-plan, then do, from the same plugin"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "An agent that can start subagents"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The main agent orchestrates and keeps the judgment calls; subagents read files and trace flows, and any report without exact files and line ranges is sent back. First one subagent proposes feature boundaries from the source tree, imports and names, and the agent settles them before fanning out. Then one subagent per feature traces its main path from entry point to end state, with side effects and the features it calls. Two more hunt duplication, inside features and across them, and say whether each divergence is legitimate specialization, such as different trust models or data sources, or accidental; every claim cites at least two file:line locations. The agent writes the unified proposal itself: the simplest design for each accidental duplication, what each old call site becomes, any capability lost, and one combined flowchart. It rejects new abstraction layers, feature flags that keep both paths, and registries where a switch would do. Each handoff prompt names the target component, the call sites to rewrite, its flowchart and guards against those anti-patterns.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem/tree/31ebffbb112260183c91bbf901a4da22e241018f/plugin/skills/pathfinder"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:planning",
