      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Makes the agent turn a rule it keeps repeating into a lint, metadata flag, runtime check or script instead of more instructions.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You catch yourself, or the agent, writing the same instruction a second time, or making the same correction again"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Encodes the rule as a lint, metadata flag, runtime check or script; when the lesson needs judgment, it makes the instruction more prominent and adds an example of the failure"
            },
            {
              "label": "Length",
              "text": "Its description plus two sentences"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Only when you call it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "One of pstack's principle skills, in Cursor's plugin repo, and one of its shortest. Its corollary: when the fix is structural, use only the structural fix, because the repeated instruction is the symptom.",
