        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Has adversary subagents on different models try to break a change or design, keeping only findings that a run proves.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a change or design stress-tested by more than one model before it ships"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Restates the intent, gives each adversary its own worktree with your uncommitted changes, and keeps a finding only if rerunning its command shows a failure that breaks the intent"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The intent, each verified finding with its command, output, impact and who found it, and counts of dropped findings with reasons"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "Apply fixes, or report style, naming, structure or risks that need a future change to matter"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Only when you call it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The scope is what you name, or else the branch's diff from its merge base through the working tree. It states the intent from your message, the commits and the PR description with pstack's in-your-own-words skill, and asks you when the intent is unclear. It then reuses the setup and fan-out of pstack's arena skill, with adversaries taken from the interrogate reviewers line of pstack's model rule. Each is told to prove every finding with a run against the real code, such as a failing test, a repro script or command output, to run a prototype or probe the tree for a design or plan, and that no findings is a valid result. Unlike arena, nothing is judged or picked: different adversaries find different failures, so the report keeps every verified finding, merging those that share a root cause.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/8ecfb19f844b67a4bc7af7f66c366d57bc7b6d2b/pstack/skills/interrogate"
        },
