        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs a test plan for a system, choosing unit, integration or end-to-end tests per area, with coverage targets, example cases and gaps.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You ask how to test something, what tests you need, or for a test plan"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A test plan: what to test, the test type for each area, coverage targets, example test cases and gaps in existing coverage"
            },
            {
              "label": "Starts from",
              "text": "The testing pyramid: many fast unit tests, some integration tests and a few slow end-to-end tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "By component",
              "text": "API endpoints, data pipelines, frontends and infrastructure each get their own mix, from contract tests to chaos and load tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A one-page testing reference from the engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. It starts from the testing pyramid: many fast, focused unit tests, some integration tests and a few slow, high-confidence end-to-end tests. It then suggests a mix by component. API endpoints get unit tests for business logic, integration tests for the HTTP layer and contract tests for their consumers; data pipelines get input validation, transformation and idempotency tests; frontends get component, interaction, visual regression and accessibility tests; infrastructure gets smoke tests, chaos engineering and load tests. Tests should cover business-critical paths, error handling, edge cases, security boundaries and data integrity, and skip trivial getters and setters, framework code and one-off scripts. The result is a test plan listing what to test, the type of test for each area, coverage targets and example test cases, with the gaps in current coverage. It's short guidance with no step-by-step method.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/engineering/skills/testing-strategy"
        },
