      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Runs an incident from triage to postmortem: rates severity, drafts status updates, tracks the timeline and writes a blameless postmortem with five whys.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Production is down, an alert needs a severity, you owe a mid-incident update, or it's time for the postmortem"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Rates severity SEV1 to SEV4, assigns roles, drafts internal and customer updates, tracks mitigation and the timeline, then writes the postmortem"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Status updates in a fixed format, and a blameless postmortem with impact, timeline, root cause, five whys, action items with owners and lessons"
            },
            {
              "label": "With connectors",
              "text": "It pulls alerts and metrics, posts updates to your incident channel, creates a war room, and pages on-call through PagerDuty or Opsgenie"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "As /incident-response new, update or postmortem; with no mode it asks what phase the incident is in"
            },
            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A four-phase incident command from the engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. Triage rates severity, from SEV1 (service down for all users, an immediate all-hands response) to SEV4 (cosmetic, next business day), identifies the affected systems and users, and assigns an incident commander, communications and responders. Communicate drafts the internal status update and any customer message and sets up a war room and an update cadence. Mitigate records the steps taken and the timeline and confirms resolution. Postmortem writes a blameless document: summary, impact, a UTC timeline, root cause, five whys, what went well and poorly, action items with owner, priority and due date, and lessons learned. Status updates follow one template: severity, a status from investigating to resolved, impact, what's known, actions taken, next steps and a timeline. Updates stay factual and start before all the facts are in, and postmortems focus on systems and processes, not people. With monitoring, incident management or chat connected, it pulls alert details and metrics, creates or updates the incident, pages on-call and posts updates to the incident channel.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/engineering/skills/incident-response"
        },
