          ],
          "text": "A data-question command from the data plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. It first sorts the question into a quick answer (one metric or lookup), a full analysis (trends, drivers, comparisons) or a formal report, and works out the tables, metrics, dimensions and time range it needs. With a data warehouse connected, it explores the schema, writes and runs SQL, debugs failed queries and sanity-checks unexpected results. Without one, it asks you to paste results, upload a CSV or Excel file, or describe the schema so it can write queries for you to run, using the plugin's sql-queries skill for the dialect. It calculates metrics, finds patterns, outliers and anomalies, compares segments and periods, and breaks complex questions into sub-questions. Before presenting, it checks row counts, nulls, magnitudes, time-series gaps and that subtotals sum to totals, and notes caveats. Quick answers come with the query used; reports add an executive summary, methodology, findings, limitations and next steps. When a chart helps, it picks one with the data-visualization skill and draws it in Python or builds it into an HTML dashboard.",
