        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a deploy checklist for a release: pre-deploy checks, the rollout, post-deploy steps, and rollback triggers decided before you ship.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're about to ship a release, especially one with database migrations, feature flags or a breaking API change"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown checklist in four parts: pre-deploy, deploy, post-deploy, and rollback triggers on error rate, latency and a critical user flow"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "CI, review, migrations, flags, a rollback plan, staging and smoke tests, a canary, 15 minutes of monitoring, release notes and stakeholders"
            },
            {
              "label": "Adapts",
              "text": "Adds flag, migration or consumer-notification steps when you say your deploy has them"
            },
            {
              "label": "With connectors",
              "text": "It pulls the release diff, checks PR approvals and the CI pipeline, and pre-fills rollback thresholds from current monitoring baselines"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "As /deploy-checklist with a service or release name"
            },
            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A checklist command from the engineering plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. The checklist has four parts. Pre-deploy: tests passing in CI, code reviewed and approved, no known critical bugs, migrations tested, feature flags configured, a documented rollback plan and on-call notified. Deploy: staging first, smoke tests, production with a canary if available, 15 minutes watching error rates and latency, and key user flows verified. Post-deploy: metrics nominal, release notes or changelog updated, stakeholders notified, related tickets closed. Rollback triggers, set before the deploy: an error rate, a P50 latency and a critical user flow failing. Saying the deploy uses feature flags, includes a database migration or breaks an API adds matching steps. With source control connected it pulls the release diff and checks that all PRs are approved and merged; with CI/CD, that the pipeline is green; with monitoring, it pre-fills rollback thresholds from current baselines and sets up a post-deploy metric watch.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/engineering/skills/deploy-checklist"
