            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The design plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A design review command. You share the design as a Figma link, a screenshot, a file or a description, with what it is, who it's for and what stage it's at, and optionally a focus such as mobile or one flow. It reviews the design through five lenses. First impression asks what draws the eye in two seconds, whether that's right, and whether the purpose is clear. Usability asks whether users can reach their goal, whether navigation and interactive elements are obvious, and whether any steps are unnecessary. Visual hierarchy covers reading order, emphasis, whitespace and typography. Consistency checks spacing, color, typography and behavior against the design system. Accessibility covers color contrast, touch target size, text readability and alt text. Feedback is meant to be specific, explain why, propose an alternative, say what works and fit the stage. The critique rates usability findings critical, moderate or minor and ends with three priority recommendations; with Figma connected it also compares the design against your existing design system.",
