      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Scores a legal risk by severity and likelihood on a five-by-five matrix, says what each level calls for, and documents it in a memo.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're weighing a contract term, deal exposure or legal issue and need to rate it and decide whether to escalate"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Scores severity and likelihood from 1 to 5 each, multiplies them, and maps the score to green, yellow, orange or red"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A risk assessment memo with both ratings and their rationale, mitigation options, a recommended approach and next steps, plus a risk register entry"
            },
            {
              "label": "Escalation",
              "text": "Says what each level calls for, from accepting and logging green risks to briefing the general counsel and board on red ones"
            },
            {
              "label": "Outside counsel",
              "text": "Lists when to engage it: mandatory, as for litigation or a government investigation, strongly recommended, or worth considering"
            },
            {
              "label": "Not legal advice",
              "text": "The skill says its assessments should be reviewed by qualified legal professionals"
            },
            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "The legal plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A risk framework for in-house legal teams, from the legal plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. Severity runs from negligible to critical, with financial exposure bands such as under 1% or over 25% of the contract or deal value, and likelihood runs from remote to almost certain. Their product is the score: 1 to 4 is green, 5 to 9 yellow, 10 to 15 orange and 16 to 25 red. Each level comes with examples and actions. Green risks are accepted, logged and reviewed periodically; yellow ones get an owner, mitigations and monthly monitoring; orange ones go to senior counsel with a mitigation plan, a leadership briefing and possibly outside counsel; red ones go straight to the general counsel, executives or board, with outside counsel, a response team, litigation holds and any required regulatory notices. The memo template covers the risk, background, both ratings with rationale, contributing and mitigating factors, a table of mitigation options, the recommended approach, residual risk, a monitoring plan and next steps. The framework is a starting point to adapt to your organization's risk appetite and industry.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/ab4cb1cd383b4eb87383be8cf4e70cb5b2a2348d/legal/skills/legal-risk-assessment"
        },
