              "text": "The data plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A charting command from the data plugin of Anthropic's knowledge-work plugins. It works out the data source, the chart type if you named one, the purpose and the audience. Data comes from a query it runs on a connected warehouse, from pasted or uploaded data it loads into pandas and cleans, or from an analysis earlier in the conversation. Without a chart type, it recommends one from a table and explains the choice: lines for trends, bars for categories and rankings, stacked bars or areas for part-to-whole, histograms or box plots for distributions, scatter plots for correlations, plus choropleth maps, Sankey diagrams and heatmaps. Static charts use matplotlib and seaborn; interactive ones with hover and zoom use plotly. Its rules: a colorblind-friendly palette, color that carries meaning, one highlighted point against grey, titles that state the insight, categories sorted by value, bars from zero, consistent scales and readable numbers such as $1.2M. It saves the chart as a PNG with a descriptive name, shows it, gives you the code and suggests variations.",
