            {
              "label": "Review",
              "text": "design-review runs only when you ask, once something is built"
            },
            {
              "label": "Resumes",
              "text": "From the next unfinished phase, by reading what's already in .design/"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The entry point to Julian Oczkowski's designer skills. It reads and follows each skill's own SKILL.md in full rather than summarizing it: grill-me, which questions you until the key decisions are settled and writes no file, then design-brief, information-architecture, design-tokens and brief-to-tasks, then frontend-design, working through TASKS.md one task at a time with your confirmation after each. At the start it suggests common skips: grilling when your idea is already clear, information architecture for a single component, tokens when the project has them. Before each phase it says what the phase will produce; after each it sums up the file, the key decisions and open questions; between phases it carries decisions forward, such as the philosophy the brief names. You can stop at any point and it tells you where you are and what comes next. Each feature gets its own folder under .design/, so several can be designed side by side.",
