      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Breaks a design brief into an ordered checklist of vertical slices, each built, styled and made interactive in one task.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a design brief and want to know what to build first"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Reads the brief, information architecture and tokens, sorts your existing components into reuse, modify or new, and turns the work into self-contained slices"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "TASKS.md next to the brief: a checklist in foundation, core UI, states, responsive and polish groups, ending with a design review"
            },
            {
              "label": "Orders by",
              "text": "Dependencies first, then the most visible element, then the riskiest piece, so the look and the problems surface early"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The planning step of Julian Oczkowski's designer workflow, between design tokens and the build. It reads .design/*/DESIGN_BRIEF.md, plus INFORMATION_ARCHITECTURE.md and a tokens file if they're in the same folder, and asks you to describe the work if there's no brief. It then lists the components, pages, token files, naming conventions, tests and UI libraries already in the codebase; only components that need changing or creating get their own tasks. A vertical slice holds a piece of UI's structure, styling and interaction together, instead of separate HTML, CSS and JavaScript tasks. Each must be buildable on its own, checkable against the brief and small enough for one session, and never a bare \"set up the project\". Every task says what it reuses, modifies or creates, the first build task carries the brief's aesthetic philosophy, and the list stays at most one level deep. If tests sit next to components, new tasks include test expectations.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/julianoczkowski/designer-skills/tree/c259656c76d9758d7ead46b0d2f125cbe84f8665/brief-to-tasks"
