      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs a web UI brand-first, from adjectives to type, OKLCH color and tokens, records it in DESIGN.md, then audits it for generic AI tells.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're building or restyling a landing page, app, dashboard, deck or docs site and don't want the default AI look"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks what the artifact is, who it serves and which 3 to 5 adjectives it must feel like, derives type and color, then applies layout, states, motion and accessibility"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The UI plus a DESIGN.md at the project root with tokens, decisions and the audit result, which later sessions read first"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike Anthropic's frontend-design",
              "text": "This one writes a token table before any component, specifies every component state and keeps all decisions in a DESIGN.md that later sessions reuse"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks",
              "text": "Through the question tool, a few high-signal questions with 2 to 4 options each"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It names two causes of generic AI interfaces: no constraints, so the model samples the median of recent web code (Inter, indigo, rounded cards), and picking an aesthetic before knowing what's being designed. So it works brand-first. It reads an existing DESIGN.md or asks what the artifact is, who it's for and which adjectives it must feel like, grounding the direction in 1 to 3 references, searched on the web if you give none. It then commits to one direction: a display and body type pair with a stated scale ratio, an OKLCH palette in roughly 60-30-10 proportions away from the indigo band, a token table written before any component, and one signature move that makes it memorable, in plain CSS, Tailwind v4 or shadcn tokens. The craft layer follows: spacing rhythm and grids, every component state from hover to error, motion under 300ms that respects reduced motion, one icon system, art-directed imagery, designed dark mode and WCAG 2.2 AA. It suggests component catalogs to borrow from, minding licenses, then scores the build against a slop checklist, regenerates failing sections and records the audit in DESIGN.md. A NEVER list bans tells such as gradient text, glassmorphism and bounce easing.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/samber/cc-skills/tree/50a33836b20f690c668af557bd9ef9d07a8c7ef2/skills/frontend-design-deslop"
