          "writing"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "samber/cc-skills/skills/copywriting-tone-of-voice-creator",
      "name": "copywriting-tone-of-voice-creator",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/samber/cc-skills/copywriting-tone-of-voice-creator",
        "installs": 5800,
        "weeklyInstalls": [69, 189, 390, 564, 698, 756, 623, 308],
        "firstSeen": "2026-05-23"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "50a33836b20f690c668af557bd9ef9d07a8c7ef2",
        "updated": "2026-11-07",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Interviews you about a brand and writes TONE.md, a voice guide with attributes, tone matrix, word lists and channel rules.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're defining or refreshing a brand voice, porting it to a new channel, or setting up many writers or bots to sound alike"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks batched discovery questions, researches unfamiliar categories with a subagent, defines the voice, writes TONE.md and checks it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "TONE.md with 3 to 5 \"X but never Y\" voice attributes, a situation-by-channel tone matrix, preferred and banned words, mechanics and channel rules"
            },
            {
              "label": "Two modes",
              "text": "Create builds the guide from scratch; Adapt adds one channel to an existing TONE.md or forks a TONE-<channel>.md"
            },
            {
              "label": "Feeds",
              "text": "copywriting-prose-creator, from the same repo, which reads TONE.md when building a prose style guide"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It treats voice as a brand's fixed personality and tone as how that voice shifts by channel, audience and situation, and calls mixing them up the most common failure. Create mode reads a SOUL.md brand identity file if there is one, then asks four batches through the question tool: basics (category, markets, goal), audience and channels, personality and references (archetype, brands to sound like and not like, the founder's part) and constraints (regulation, taboos, localisation). Categories it doesn't cover, such as politics, healthcare or crypto, get a research subagent first. It places the voice on Nielsen Norman Group's four tone dimensions, clearly off-centre on at least three, and writes each attribute with a definition, three do's, three don'ts, an example and an anti-example from the brand's own content. The tone matrix gives a dominant tone and prohibited ones for situations such as a launch, crisis, complaint or layoffs on each channel. Before finalising, it checks the attribute count, the anti-examples, a non-empty banned-word list, one section per channel and that the do's are concrete. Adapt mode keeps the attributes and changes only tone for the new channel.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/samber/cc-skills/tree/50a33836b20f690c668af557bd9ef9d07a8c7ef2/skills/copywriting-tone-of-voice-creator"
        },
