              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The release in your target language with a note on the angle, then offers of a send plan, a journalist pitch email and social teasers"
            },
            {
              "label": "Checks",
              "text": "A 25 to 35 word lead answering who, what, when, where, why and how, 300 to 500 words, third person, \"said\", no \"thrilled\" or \"cutting-edge\""
            }
          ],
          "text": "It treats a press release as a news document, not an ad: when the angle is weak, it says so and suggests how to strengthen it. The facts it needs are the news, the release type, target outlets, region, media format, company details, spokespeople, supporting data, any embargo and the language. The angle is tested against news values: impact, timeliness, prominence, novelty and proximity. Reference files supply a template per release type, regional conventions such as style guide, dateline, regulations and send times, adaptations for print, wire, broadcast, social or trade press, and a journalist-pitch guide. The structure is fixed: release designation or embargo, a sentence-case headline, an optional subheadline, the dateline and lead, body paragraphs with an executive quote that adds insight rather than enthusiasm, an optional third-party quote, a factual boilerplate under 100 words, a media contact and an end mark. A humanizer skill then cleans the prose but leaves the headline and lead alone. Its next steps include advice on building a journalist list and the best day and time to send.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/samber/cc-skills/tree/50a33836b20f690c668af557bd9ef9d07a8c7ef2/skills/press-release-writer"
