        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Interviews a trainer about a session and writes a training or workshop report in Markdown, then a Word file once approved.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You ran a training, workshop or onboarding session and need to report on it to management, HR or a client"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks the language and reader, takes your .docx template if any, interviews you in batches, drafts in Markdown, iterates, then builds the .docx once"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A .md and a .docx covering context, starting levels, a step-by-step walkthrough, recommendations and next steps, plus optional sections"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Anthropic's docx skill for the Word file; a humanizer skill for the report's language is recommended, with built-in rules as a fallback"
            },
            {
              "label": "Voice-ready",
              "text": "It expects transcription errors and asks when a name or answer is unclear"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It works for any discipline, from coding workshops to safety training. Before asking anything it checks that the docx skill is installed and, if not, warns you and offers to start on the Markdown draft. The interview covers the session's details, goal and materials, the group's starting levels, each step (objective, what people did, how it landed), anything participants produced, general observations, feedback on individuals, recommendations, annexes and a closing note with your contact details. With survey data it first summarises the score, distribution and top themes for you to confirm. Optional sections appear only when you give content for them, and feedback on people describes behaviour, not character. Recommendations are kept to a few sharp ones and always include pacing. It confirms the outline before drafting, never shows an unhumanized draft, keeps one Markdown file as the source, and rebuilds the .docx from scratch after any later change. Images are embedded and other files referenced. Without a template or brand color, the document uses blue.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/samber/cc-skills/tree/50a33836b20f690c668af557bd9ef9d07a8c7ef2/skills/training-report"
