            }
          ],
          "text": "Midscene's skill for the web. Its default mode launches a headless Chrome through Puppeteer, isolated from your browser, that stays open across commands until you close it. When you ask it to use your Chrome, or the task needs your login, such as checking your orders, it connects over the DevTools Protocol after a quick check that remote debugging is on, or through the Midscene Chrome extension in Bridge mode. `act` takes a whole goal in plain words and handles clicks, hovers, typing, scrolling and drags itself; uploads only reach files inside a folder passed with the command, the smallest that holds them. `assert` checks the visible page against a sentence or reference images, and a recorder running in its own terminal catches toasts and transitions that vanish too fast. Tabs can be listed and switched without reloading, custom HTTP headers can go with every CDP command, and `--deep-locate` or `--deep-think` trade speed for precision. Commands run one at a time in the foreground, about a minute each; the agent reads each screenshot before deciding the next step and reports results at the end. Because it works from screenshots, it needs no selectors, DOM or accessibility labels.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/web-infra-dev/midscene-skills/tree/e6836973627a20edc34b844a2e20d4180602ae5d/skills/browser"
        },
