      "skillMd": {
        "version": "a1fc303b274ed06c32d405ba5a6db00ded6e5663",
        "updated": "2026-11-07",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews a plan, pull request or code change as an outsider: questions whether it should exist, traces the real code path, verifies its claims.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a second opinion on a plan, PR, diff or design doc; it also starts on its own when you ask for a review or sanity check"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Restates the goal, looks for a simpler way, traces each claimed behavior end to end beyond the diff, then hunts for inputs that break it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Findings ordered blocker, major, nit, each with file and line, why it matters, evidence and a minimal suggested change, then a verdict: ship, fix-then-ship, rework or reject"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Rubber-stamp: no LGTM, flattery or hedging; if it finds nothing, it lists what it traced and checked"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Thananon's review skill runs four steps in order. Intent comes first: it states the goal in one sentence of its own, stops if it can't, and, unless told not to question scope, spends one pass asking whether doing nothing, existing code, a smaller change or a different layer would do, because a better alternative is the most valuable thing it can report. Then it traces every behavior the change claims through the real call path, from entry point to side effect, including the unchanged code on both sides of the diff, and treats every surprise as a signal; a plan is traced against the existing system. Verification follows: for each claim it walks the path explicitly, lists inputs and states that would break it, notes what the change silently alters, such as performance, error semantics or on-disk formats, and checks whether the tests exercise the traced path or pass on mocks. Every claim about the code cites a path, file or line, and what the PR says stays separate from what was confirmed. Structural problems lead the report, and style nits are dropped when there's something bigger. Each finding carries a suggested change; the skill itself only reports.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/thananon/9arm-skills/tree/a1fc303b274ed06c32d405ba5a6db00ded6e5663/skills/engineering/scrutinize"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:debugging",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "code-review",
          "verification",
          "scope-control"
        ],
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
