      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Holds debugging to four steps: reproduce reliably, find the failing path, try to disprove each hypothesis, and check it against every earlier run.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You start debugging anything; it also starts on its own when you report a bug or paste a stack trace or error log"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Recites a four-line mantra verbatim in its first reply, then proposes no fix until there's a reliable repro and a hypothesis that survived a disproof"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A runnable repro, a ledger of every experiment and what it ruled out, and a root cause checked against all of them"
            },
            {
              "label": "Escalates",
              "text": "From a debugger, to a source trace listing every config flag, env var and branch to flip one at a time, to tagged log probes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From thananon's 9arm skills. Step one builds a fast, deterministic repro as a runnable artifact, such as a failing test, curl script or replay harness; a flaky bug gets its failure rate raised first, by looping, parallelising or adding stress, and with no repro at all the agent stops and asks for access, logs or permission to instrument. Step two finds where the code breaks, escalating from a debugger, to a source trace with every knob that could change the outcome flipped one at a time, to log statements tagged with a unique prefix such as [DBG-a4f2] so cleanup is one grep. Step three ranks three to five hypotheses and runs the cleanest disproof of each before any proof. Step four keeps a running ledger of what each run changed and what it ruled in or out, and rejects any hypothesis that contradicts an earlier run. Saying \"skip the mantra\" skips the recital but not the steps.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/thananon/9arm-skills/tree/a1fc303b274ed06c32d405ba5a6db00ded6e5663/skills/engineering/debug-mantra"
        },
