            {
              "label": "From an image",
              "text": "It states the scale it assumed, treats every measurement as an estimate and asks for the Figma link if one exists"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Add tokens, variants or arbitrary values to hit a number, design states the file doesn't draw, or touch code around the piece"
            }
          ],
          "text": "One of Jakub Krehel's interface skills, but it owns no design rules: the design decides, and where it breaks a rule, such as contrast or focus, the agent builds it as drawn and reports the conflict, naming the better-* skill that owns that rule. From a Figma link it first searches its tools for the Figma MCP server, asks you to sign in or connect one rather than build from guesswork, and reads each frame's design context, variables and screenshot, trusting named variables over raw hex, Code Connect mappings (Figma's links from component to code) over name matches, and auto layout over absolute positions. It reads your tokens and components before writing anything; a raw value with no token rounds to the nearest one and is reported, and it stops to ask when rounding would visibly change the design, such as more than 2px or a different color step. Data with no backend yet is fed by props and listed as unwired. With a browser it screenshots each frame width beside the design and fixes its own mismatches until only roundings and questions remain; without one it hands over the local URL and says the comparison is unverified.",
