          "text": "Upstash's Context7 skill for agents with the Context7 MCP server connected. When a question involves a library, such as configuring a Next.js proxy or writing a Prisma query, the agent first calls resolve-library-id with the library's name and what it wants to know, then picks the closest match, favoring higher benchmark scores, version-specific IDs when you mention a version, and official packages over community forks. It then calls query-docs with that ID, one concept per call: a question spanning routing, auth and caching becomes three calls on the same library unless it's about how they interact, because combined queries return shallow results for each. The answer uses the fetched documentation and its code examples rather than training data, and cites the library version when it matters.",
