          "text": "From OneWave AI's skills library. It pulls the brief from the conversation, your documents or the product's site before asking anything: the one action the page drives, where readers arrive from, the problem in their words, the real differentiator and the proof that exists. A line of the message hierarchy it can't fill is flagged as a gap instead of papered over. PAS suits readers who feel the pain, AIDA cold or comparing traffic, and StoryBrand brand-led or service businesses, with section guidance for each in a reference file. The draft runs hero, problem, solution, how it works, proof, pricing, FAQ and final CTA, cutting what the product doesn't need. Before delivering, it checks that a competitor couldn't paste the headline unchanged, that every feature answers \"so what?\", that every CTA points to the same action and starts with a verb, that sentences are short and in the second person, and that filler such as \"seamless\" or \"revolutionary\" is gone. A worked example builds a page for a physical therapy scheduling tool.",
