      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Runs committed changes through no-mistakes' review, test, lint, push, PR and CI pipeline, settling each gate's findings or bringing them to you.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a change validated before it reaches your remote, or type /no-mistakes with a task for the agent to do and then validate"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Drives the no-mistakes pipeline (intent, rebase, review, test, document, lint, push, PR, CI) and answers each gate, a stop that waits for a decision, with fix, approve or skip"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A PR with green checks, left for you to review and merge, and a summary of what was validated and every fix the pipeline made"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks you",
              "text": "About every finding marked ask-user, quoted verbatim, unless you passed --yes to let it drive the whole run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The no-mistakes CLI initialized in the repo, a coding agent for the pipeline, and your work committed on a feature branch"
            }
          ],
          "text": "no-mistakes puts a local gate in front of your remote, and this skill is how a coding agent drives it, through the `no-mistakes axi` commands. With a task, it does the work, commits only the related changes on a feature branch, then validates; bare /no-mistakes validates what's already committed. Every run needs your intent in full, not a diff summary, because the review step uses it to tell deliberate choices from mistakes. Each run and respond call blocks for minutes until a gate or an outcome; the agent reads every findings table, hands auto-fix findings to the pipeline, and never edits code itself while a run is active. Review auto-fix is off by default. Once checks pass the agent stops and the PR waits for you, while no-mistakes keeps watching it and, on a merge conflict, rebases, revalidates and re-pushes by itself. A failed run is fixed on the same branch and run again, with guarded sync and recovery commands instead of manual resets. It also bans tests that only grep source text: tests must check observable behavior against an independent oracle, an expected result from outside the code, such as a specification or worked example.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/kunchenguid/no-mistakes/tree/d950c619e3b90833f423b62848797116ac4ee604/skills/no-mistakes"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:debugging",
          "category:engineering",
          "type:tool",
          "effect:remote",
          "needs:cli",
          "by:official",
          "stack:no-mistakes",
          "stack:git",
          "code-review",
          "testing",
          "ci",
          "verification",
          "git"
        ],
        "note": "Needs the no-mistakes CLI, set up in the repo with no-mistakes init, and a supported coding agent CLI to run its pipeline. It pushes your branch and opens a PR, and after checks pass it keeps watching the PR, rebasing and re-pushing on a merge conflict.",
