            {
              "label": "Unlike agent-device's dogfood",
              "text": "That one, Callstack's skill of the same name, is for apps on phones, simulators and emulators; this one tests web apps in a browser"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Hermes Agent's QA skill runs in five phases. It creates an output folder and plans a rough sitemap: home page, navigation, key flows such as sign-up or checkout, forms, and edge cases like empty states and 404s. While exploring, it installs a console hook before each navigation so errors thrown during page load are caught, lists the visible interactive elements with their screen positions, looks at a screenshot, and tries buttons, links, forms with valid, invalid and empty input, keyboard focus and going back, checking for errors and visual changes after each interaction. Every issue gets a screenshot, URL, steps to reproduce, expected and actual behavior, a severity from Critical to Low and a category: functional, visual, accessibility, console, UX or content. It then merges duplicates, sorts by severity and fills its report template, ending with notes on what was and wasn't tested. Silent JavaScript errors count among the most valuable findings.",
