              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js, and a browser for the screenshot check; without either it falls back to lighter checks and says what it couldn't verify"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From the repo of @lucasmarkes/hairline, a package of isometric line figures that answer the pointer. Each figure is one idea: an object built from rounded solids in a single stroke, which the pointer does something to, with a read-out line under it. The agent pitches two or three concepts in one line each (object, gesture, read-out, tour stops) and waits for you to pick; given an SVG, it first measures the mark and keeps its parts in every concept. It then writes only the figure's own file, following ten rules and two example figures: geometry instead of labels, one stroke moved to a highlight instead of color, springs instead of timers, and a composed rest pose, because rest is the thumbnail. The tour is three to six points an unseen pointer visits when the page plays. A look script builds the page, validates it and takes eight pictures on one sheet; the agent fixes every failure, then reads the sheet against a list of questions. It publishes the page as an artifact when it can, or says where the file is, and asks you to press play and judge the lap. Later changes edit only the figure file.",
