        "skew": 86
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds or updates screens, modals and panels in Figma from your code or a description, using the file's published design system components and variables.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want an app page, modal, form or dashboard built in Figma from code or a description, or a Figma screen updated to match the code"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Finds design-system components via Code Connect files (code-to-Figma links), existing screens and library search, then builds section by section with its variables and styles, not hardcoded values"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "An editable Figma view of design system instances, local components for repeated pieces, imported SVG icons and the product's own font"
            },
            {
              "label": "Never",
              "text": "Imports a screenshot of the whole UI as the result; if the view isn't mostly editable layers, it rebuilds it or reports failure"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike build-design",
              "text": "That one, Jakub Krehel's, turns a Figma design into code; this one goes the other way, from code into Figma"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Figma's own skill for the code-to-design direction. It reads the source to list the view's sections and components, finds the product's typeface instead of defaulting to Inter, and checks for images. For a web app with photos, avatars or logos it also captures the running page into the same file with generate_figma_design: the capture sets exact spacing and supplies the image fills, then gets deleted. Component keys come first from Code Connect files next to the source, then from a search scoped to the file's libraries and an inventory of existing screens; variables and text and effect styles come from the same places, and an empty list of local variables never counts as proof there are none. Each section is built inside one wrapper frame, instance text set through component properties, variants taken from the component's source defaults. Validation reads back node counts, then compares one screenshot with the source for clipped text, overlaps, leftover placeholder text, wrong variants, wrong fonts and blank images, and makes targeted fixes. Raw HTML, or a new design with nothing rendered yet, goes through html_to_figma instead. Placeholder images from Figma's generate_image use Figma AI credits, and it tells you so.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/figma/mcp-server-guide/tree/19be8d51c6a2f8ca949d33e5cd8e9662c5d243e8/skills/figma-generate-design"
        },
