      "skillMd": {
        "version": "9f68af0274ca06c5decd6269d870d442b8e04500",
        "updated": "2026-11-07",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Asks two high-reasoning agents from different providers, through Paseo, for a root-cause analysis and plan, then relays their arguments until they agree.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You or the agent are stuck, going in circles or tunnel-visioned, or facing a hard planning problem"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Starts two agents from contrasting Paseo profiles, ideally from different provider families, gives both the same problem, then passes each one's arguments to the other until they converge"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "One agreed plan, with a summary of where the two disagreed and how that was resolved"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "Let the committee change anything: every prompt to a member ends with a line forbidding edits, new files and code"
            },
            {
              "label": "Takes",
              "text": "As long as the models reason, often 15 to 30 minutes; the agent waits for Paseo's finish notice instead of polling"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Paseo running with its MCP tools, and the repo's paseo skill"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A committee is two agents with fresh context and different reasoning styles. The skill reads Paseo's agent profiles and their notes, then picks one whose notes fit planning, research or root-cause analysis and a contrasting high-reasoning one, preferably from another provider family, unless you name the members. When fewer than two profiles fit, it falls back to Paseo's provider list and tells you. Both members get the same problem-level prompt and a [Committee] title. The agent then waits for both answers without hurrying or interrupting them, settles disagreements by passing each member's arguments to the other, and keeps going until they converge. You get the consensus, plus where the two diverged and how they resolved it.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo/tree/9f68af0274ca06c5decd6269d870d442b8e04500/skills/paseo-committee"
        },
        "tags": [
