      "skillMd": {
        "version": "d7b5633f91591ee3bf55c8d80831b515498cc0e6",
        "updated": "2026-11-07",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Places you in the AI Engineering from Scratch course with a ten-question quiz, then lays out a 20-phase path with hour estimates.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're starting AI Engineering from Scratch and don't know which of its 20 phases to begin with"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks two multiple-choice questions in each of five areas: math and statistics, classical ML, deep learning, NLP and transformers, and applied AI"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A score out of 10, an entry phase from Phase 1 to 14, and a table of all 20 phases marked Skip, Review or Do, with hours"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps answers apart",
              "text": "The key sits in a separate file the agent reads one round at a time, only after you answer"
            },
            {
              "label": "Next",
              "text": "start-learning saves the placement as a LEARNING.md study plan"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The quiz runs in five rounds of two questions, with a score for the area after each round and no explanations until the end. The total sets the entry point: 0 to 3 starts at Math Foundations, 4 or 5 at Deep Learning Core, 6 or 7 at Transformers Deep Dive, 8 or 9 at LLM Engineering, and 10 at Agent Engineering. Phases below the entry are Skip and the rest Do, but a phase you'd skip becomes Review when you got only one of its area's two questions right; Phase 0, tooling setup, is always Skip. Hours come from the course's ROADMAP.md, read locally or fetched from GitHub, and add up to a total for the Review and Do phases. It closes with where to start, what to focus on given your weakest area, and pointers to start-learning and learn. Unlike start-learning, which saves the placement to LEARNING.md, it shows the path in the conversation.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/rohitg00/ai-engineering-from-scratch/tree/d7b5633f91591ee3bf55c8d80831b515498cc0e6/skills/find-your-level"
        },
