      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reviews code changes by Sentry's engineering checklist, from runtime errors, performance and security to tests and design, with polite, actionable feedback.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're reviewing a pull request or code change and want a short, general checklist"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks for runtime errors, quadratic or N+1 performance problems, side effects, breaking API changes, security gaps, test coverage and fit with the architecture"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Polite, actionable comments, phrased as questions when unsure, with approval once only minor issues remain"
            },
            {
              "label": "Flags for a senior",
              "text": "Schema changes, API contract changes, new frameworks or libraries, performance-critical paths and security-sensitive code"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike find-bugs",
              "text": "That one, Sentry's branch review, has an 11-item security checklist and evidence for every finding; this one is a lighter reviewer's guide"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Sentry's code review guidelines, condensed for agents. They're written for Sentry projects, though nothing in them needs Sentry. The checklist covers problems to look for, from exceptions and out-of-bounds access to unbounded quadratic operations, N+1 queries, complex Django ORM queries, injection and exposed secrets; a design check of whether the change fits the architecture and current requirements; and test coverage at functional, integration and end-to-end level, without heavy branching in tests. The feedback rules say to be polite and specific, not to block a PR over style, and to remember the goal is reducing risk, not perfect code. Short examples show an N+1 query fixed with prefetch_related, a missing useEffect dependency, and SQL injection fixed with a parameterized query. It links to Sentry's published code review guide.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/getsentry/skills/tree/e94f22214528d69899d09c627b3315ddc3544816/skills/code-review"
        },
