      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Scrapes and crawls websites with Scrapling's CLI or Python library, from plain HTTP requests to stealth browsers that get past Cloudflare checks.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A page needs JavaScript or blocks plain requests, or you want a Python scraper or crawler written against Scrapling's current API"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Saves a page as Markdown, text or HTML with scrapling extract: get for simple pages, fetch with a stealth browser for JavaScript-heavy or protected ones"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The page content in a temporary file the agent reads and then deletes, or Python code built on Scrapling's fetchers, parser and spiders"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike plain web fetches",
              "text": "This one can impersonate a browser's TLS fingerprint, solve Cloudflare Turnstile challenges and route through proxies"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3.10+ with scrapling[all] installed, and scrapling install for its browser; a Docker image covers the commands but not Python code"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The official skill for Scrapling, a Python scraping library, from its author. For one-off jobs the agent runs scrapling extract: get, post, put or delete for HTTP requests, or fetch for a browser, picking the output format by file extension and narrowing the page with a CSS selector to save tokens. It always adds --ai-targeted, which keeps the page body, filters out common hidden elements and, in the browser, blocks ads, as a guard against prompt injection. It starts with get and moves to fetch when a page needs JavaScript or blocks requests, adding --solve-cloudflare for a Cloudflare challenge. For more, it writes Python: fetchers and sessions, the stealth browser, a connection to a running Chrome over CDP, recorded API responses, and parsing by CSS, XPath, text or similar elements, with a parser that relocates elements when a site changes. Spiders crawl concurrently, pause and resume from a checkpoint folder, follow link rules or sitemaps, read RSS and CSV feeds, and pull Shopify products. Its guardrails: scrape only what you're authorized to access, respect robots.txt and terms of service, add delays to large crawls, bypass no paywall or login without permission, and never scrape personal data.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/d4vinci/scrapling/tree/bc602488b44e978da3266841e913af17577ec0fd/agent-skill/Scrapling-Skill"
