      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Searches your codebase by meaning with CocoIndex Code's ccc CLI, setting up and refreshing the semantic index itself.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want the agent to find code by what it does, such as a user authentication flow, rather than by exact text"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs ccc search with a plain-language query, filtered by language or path and paged, then reads the matching line ranges"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "The index current itself: it initializes a project that isn't set up and re-indexes at the start of a session and after significant changes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Whenever the agent needs to search code, not only when you ask"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The ccc CLI from CocoIndex Code; if it's missing, the agent tells you how to install it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "CocoIndex Code indexes a codebase for semantic search, and this skill makes the agent own that index. When ccc search or ccc index fails because the project isn't initialized, the agent runs ccc init from the project root, builds the index and retries, without asking you. It won't initialize the directory that holds ccc's user settings, usually your home directory, and when a repo turns out to use a parent directory's project, it tells you and leaves resetting it to you. It re-indexes at the start of a session and after new files, refactors or renamed modules, or searches with --refresh. Queries describe a concept, such as error handling retry logic, not code syntax. Results can be narrowed by language or by a path glob, which defaults to the current directory, and paged with offset and limit, fetching the next page when every result looks relevant. Each result gives a file and a line range that the agent then reads for context. Settings for the embedding model, include and exclude patterns, and troubleshooting are in its reference files.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/cocoindex-io/cocoindex-code/tree/5676897a169fe1d46cf1e4d2eaf323c9d91c8587/skills/ccc"
        },
