      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Fetches hot items from 44+ tech, AI, finance and world news sources and writes a Simplified Chinese report summarizing and analyzing each one.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a scan or daily briefing of tech, AI, finance or international news, and you read Chinese"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs its Python script to fetch items from the sources you pick, optionally filtered by keyword and with full article text, then writes up each item"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown report in Simplified Chinese saved under reports/<date>/, each item with its source, time, heat, a summary and an insight paragraph"
            },
            {
              "label": "Sources",
              "text": "Hacker News, GitHub Trending, Product Hunt, arXiv, Hugging Face papers, AI newsletters, BBC, the Guardian, Al Jazeera, Weibo, 36Kr, podcasts, essays and your own OPML feeds"
            },
            {
              "label": "Presets",
              "text": "Morning briefings for general, finance, tech, social, AI and reading-list sources, most with their own instruction file"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3.8+ with its requirements, and Playwright's Chromium for Hugging Face papers and Ben's Bites"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It writes everything in Simplified Chinese, whatever language you ask in, keeping well-known English names. Every request follows three steps: fetch with scripts/fetch_news.py, format every item with one report template, then save the report to reports/YYYY-MM-DD/ and show it in full. You can name one source, several or all of them, set a limit per source, filter by keywords, which it expands (AI becomes LLM, GPT, Claude, Agent, RAG and DeepSeek), and add --deep to download article text for a richer analysis. Each item gets a title translated into Chinese and linked to the original, its source, time and heat, such as stars or upvotes, a one-line summary and an insight paragraph, with tweaks per source: Hacker News keeps its discussion link, GitHub adds language and tags, and Hugging Face papers get a real reading rather than a translated abstract. Its rules forbid inventing items or causal links and require a time on every item. When a time window has fewer than five items it fills in older ones, marked with a warning sign, except for international news, which stays within 24 hours. A Chinese phrase, 如意如意, opens an interactive menu, and a separate script runs the preset briefings.",
