      "skillMd": {
        "version": "5ed4b7989bd9c4ba803b0f3e6d69064ffc0826bb",
        "updated": "2026-11-07",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a whole app, site, bot or feature from your dictated idea: requirements, spec, tickets, subagent builds, code review and a blind acceptance check.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You read Russian and want a project built end to end from a description, without reading specs or reviewing code"
            },
            {
              "label": "In Russian",
              "text": "Its messages, stage names, dashboard and final report template are in Russian, though the skill's own rules are written in English"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Turns your words into a numbered requirements list, asks only where the idea forks, writes a spec and tickets, has subagents build and review each, then checks the result blind"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The project in git with one commit per ticket, a committed .autopilot/ folder of what was promised and delivered, and a final report"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "Only when you type /autopilot, with a mode from full to manual and a depth from strict to deep; a bare /autopilot resumes an interrupted run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Shows",
              "text": "A live local HTML dashboard of stages, tasks and your requirements, which it opens itself"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "Before deploying, publishing, paying, messaging a third party, deleting data or rewriting history, in every mode"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Subagents, git and Python 3 for its ap.py helper"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Autopilot takes one dialogue from idea to working project; the stage names, dashboard and report you see are in Russian. Your brief is first saved word for word, with secrets redacted, and turned into a numbered manifest of requirements that only you can remove. Four gates check against it: after briefing every requirement has a status; after the spec an independent reader given only the brief and spec finds nothing missing; after planning every requirement maps to a ticket; and at the end a blind acceptance from a clean clone compares the build with your brief, spec withheld. The mode sets how much you're asked: full asks nothing, semi, the default, asks about genuine forks, interview asks everything, and manual adds your approval of the spec and tickets. The depth sets how much it works out beyond your words. The orchestrator never writes project code itself: subagents build one ticket each, with reviews and capped repairs. It never asks for keys, leaving their names empty in .env.example, and never invents facts about you, using visible placeholders instead. It also writes project memory, AGENTS.md or a proposal for your own file, and a PROGRESS.md that the next run reads.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/nick-vels/skills/tree/5ed4b7989bd9c4ba803b0f3e6d69064ffc0826bb/skills/autopilot"
        },
