        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Drives your own Chrome, with its logins and extensions, through the Playwriter extension and Playwright code run from its CLI.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "A site is JavaScript-heavy or behind a login, cookie wall or infinite scroll, or you want the agent in the browser you're signed in to"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs Playwright snippets in a stateful sandbox connected to your Chrome, checking the URL, an accessibility snapshot and console logs after every action"
            },
            {
              "label": "First",
              "text": "The agent reads the whole guide that playwriter skill prints, once per session; the SKILL.md itself only points to it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also",
              "text": "Headless Chrome, direct CDP connections, control of a browser someone shares with you, cloud browsers, and recording what you do to turn it into a skill"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike Playwright MCP servers",
              "text": "Those launch a fresh browser; this one attaches to the Chrome you're already using"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "The playwriter CLI and its Chrome extension, enabled on the tabs it may use"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The SKILL.md only tells the agent to run playwriter skill and read every line it prints, a long guide kept in the repo; this summary follows that guide. Each task gets its own session, a sandbox whose state object persists between calls, and its own Chrome tab group. The agent opens or picks a tab and follows observe, act, observe: print the URL, an accessibility snapshot and new console logs, take one action, check again. Its rules include never closing the browser, clicking a field before typing, preferring snapshots to screenshots and proper waits to fixed timeouts. Helpers cover snapshots, layout inspection, page logs, labelled screenshots, network interception and low-level mouse and keyboard control. Beyond your own Chrome it can launch headless Chrome, connect to any CDP endpoint, drive a browser someone shares through a secret remote-control id, or start cloud browsers that solve Turnstile, reCAPTCHA and hCaptcha, hide automation signals and route through residential proxies. A recorder captures your clicks, typing and network requests so the agent can turn the workflow into a reusable skill. The sandbox's own fs writes only to the working directory and temp folders, but modules it imports run with full Node.js permissions.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/remorses/playwriter/tree/2cae912a9c1e68ae2b74fcaef9efd79b6d7d432f/skills/playwriter"
