          "text": "It picks one of four analyses, or a comparison, from your question. A basic overview gives a short description, price, key metrics, recent performance and news. Fundamental analysis looks at 3 to 5 years of revenue, earnings and cash flow, the balance sheet and profitability, judges business quality, computes valuation ratios such as P/E, PEG and EV/EBITDA against history and peers to estimate a fair value range, and lists risks and red flags. Technical analysis reads the trend, support and resistance, moving averages, RSI, MACD, Bollinger Bands, volume and chart patterns into a short and medium-term outlook with risk levels. The full report combines both into bull and bear cases, catalysts, a rating, a target price, conviction and an entry strategy. Comparisons put two or more stocks side by side and suggest an allocation. Data comes from web searches of sources such as Yahoo Finance, SEC filings and TradingView, preferring last quarter's figures, with sources and dates cited. Reference files hold the frameworks, metric formulas and report templates, and the tone stays balanced, with risks and uncertainty stated plainly.",
