        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Holds coding agents to six rules: read before editing, stay in declared scope, and claim nothing done without fresh, executed evidence.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a coding agent to stop editing files it hasn't read and announcing work done that it never checked"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Makes the agent read the target, its tests and its callers first, plan in proportion to risk, and verify after the last edit"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Replies in three parts, What Changed, Evidence and Why, with real command output; every check ends in VERDICT: PASS or FAIL"
            },
            {
              "label": "Enforced by",
              "text": "Gravitas's own runtime hooks where they're installed; with the skill alone, the rules are instructions only"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Gravitas calls itself a reliability runtime for coding agents. Its one rule is to report what actually happened: a claim that something is fixed must rest on output seen in this session. Six invariants follow: ground before mutating, stay inside the write scope a task contract declares, count a criterion done only when a Gravitas validator passed after the last relevant edit, never retry a failed approach unchanged, satisfy the contract's acceptance criteria rather than a generic test pass, and say what couldn't be verified. Before risky work the agent records a planning policy, direct, compact, deep or replan, set by blast radius rather than ceremony, and a decision record with the evidence for each non-trivial action. Evidence is ranked, from deterministic validators and project tests down to the agent's own review, which never counts as proof. Read-only modes such as plan and review forbid writes, and migrations need your checkpoint. It delegates to subagents only when the policy calls for it, and eco, balanced and deep profiles set how much it plans and verifies.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/udaysharmadev/gravitas/tree/e0d22cd4f7639b1af3899bc3e70d314b2ae6339a/skills/gravitas"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
          "category:debugging",
          "type:guidelines",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "verification",
          "scope-control",
          "planning",
          "agent-workflows"
        ],
        "note": "Installed alone it is instructions only; the hooks that deny out-of-scope writes, block repeated failed retries and gate completion come with Gravitas's Antigravity plugin or OpenCode shim.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
