          "text": "CLI-Hub is CLI-Anything's registry of command-line interfaces that make software usable by agents. The skill installs the hub with pip install cli-anything-hub, then lists, searches and installs from it: cli-hub install gimp adds the cli-anything-gimp package, run as a REPL or with one-shot commands, each taking --json for machine-readable output. For a task that spans several tools, a matrix packages a whole workflow, such as video-creation, as capabilities like transcription or visual generation mapped to providers: harness CLIs, public CLIs, Python libraries, native binaries and cloud APIs. The agent finds a capability with cli-hub can, runs a preflight to see what's usable on your machine, can preview the plan with --dry-run, and installs only the capability it needs rather than a whole 14-CLI matrix. After install, the matrix's own SKILL.md, with rules for choosing providers, renders locally. Some CLIs also publish previews, which cli-hub previews can inspect, render to HTML, watch or open.",
