              "label": "Unlike antislop",
              "text": "It sets exact values, such as a 240–260px sidebar and 14–16px body text, where antislop prescribes no colors, fonts or layouts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Uncodixify names \"Codex UI\", the default AI aesthetic of soft gradients, floating panels, eyebrow labels, hero sections inside dashboards, big rounded corners and dramatic shadows, and tells the agent to avoid all of it. A keep-it-normal list sets plain defaults for 30 kinds of element: a 240–260px sidebar with a solid background, buttons with at most a 10px radius and no pills, cards at 8–12px with subtle borders, labels above form fields, shadows no stronger than 0 2px 8px, 100–200ms opacity or color transitions, 14–16px body text and a 4–32px spacing scale. A hard-no list bans glassmorphism, metric-card grids as a first instinct, fake charts, decorative copy, generic startup lines and default font stacks such as Inter, Roboto or Arial unless the product already uses them, with HTML examples of banned headline and card patterns. For color it reads the project's existing palette from its files and otherwise takes inspiration from one of ten dark and ten light palettes, picked at random.",
