            }
          ],
          "text": "Unslop works in two passes. It first reads the source, extracts its facts and constraints, and runs bundled Python scanners: a phrase scan, a structure scan, a silhouette scan of how the ideas are laid out, and readability metrics. Scanner hits stay candidates until the agent confirms them in context. The second pass makes the smallest fix in each sentence with a confirmed finding, copies every other sentence byte for byte, and undoes any edit that changes a fact, meaning, register or attribution. Voice presets, crisp, warm, expert or story, shape the wording but can't add findings, and --strict fails a rewrite that scores under 32 of 40. Cleanup is the co-writer mode: reviewable suggestions, or a report-only audit that changes nothing. Teach builds a voice profile and a layered voice card from writing samples you approve, under .unslop/voice/, and ends with a scored demo paragraph; mimic then writes in that voice. Contribute turns a new AI-ism you found into a test case and a pull request upstream.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/theclaymethod/unslop/tree/17ed39c9d0b522f44190ff0c6233867eadee192a"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:writing",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "anti-slop",
          "writing"
        ],
        "note": "Its contribute flow opens a public pull request on theclaymethod/unslop with a snippet of your text, after asking you twice; teach collects writing samples from your agent transcripts and folders, keeping only those you approve.",
        "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
        "effort": "xhigh"
      }
    },
