            }
          ],
          "text": "Ghost Security's AI code scanner for SAST, static analysis of source code. It first reads the repository context that ghost-repo-context writes, then a planner picks scans for each project from criteria per project type: for backends, frontends and mobile apps, issues such as SQL injection, XSS, broken object- or function-level authorization and SSRF; for libraries, prototype pollution, unsafe deserialization, ReDoS, path traversal and zip slip. The plan becomes a checklist of project, agent and vector; nominators pick candidate files for each, analyzers examine each candidate and write findings, and verifiers recheck every unverified finding. Each stage runs through a loop script that starts fresh claude -p workers with file tools, up to five at a time, and picks up where it left off after a timeout. Arguments can narrow the scan to chosen vectors, files or areas. It ends by listing the finding files and counting verified against rejected findings.",
