              "text": "Editorial magazine with six paper-and-ink palettes, or Swiss International with one of four accent colors"
            },
            {
              "label": "Images",
              "text": "You choose once: your own, found on Unsplash, Pexels, Flickr CC or Wallhaven with copyright unverified, or AI-generated"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js and Playwright, installed with npm in the skill's folder; Live Photo cards also need makelive and an iPhone to publish"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A self-contained skill for static social posts that borrows the visual principles of the Guizang PPT skill. It asks only what changes the output: platforms, source text, which images go where and, if you sent only text, whether you'll supply photos, want them found on the web or want them AI-generated, asked once and in Chinese. It turns the source into a page plan, a cover hook and then one idea per page, and picks one style mode per set: Editorial Magazine × E-ink, with serif titles over a paper, ink or WebGL background, or Swiss International, with a strict grid and one bright accent. It copies a seed template, fills it from layout recipes and renders PNGs with a bundled script that embeds fonts and checks sizes. Text over a photo needs a mapped quiet zone and a 360px thumbnail test. Web images are logged in assets/SOURCES.md, and you decide on credits. Live Photo cards cut your videos to 5 seconds for Xiaohongshu or 3 for WeChat. It shows you the renders first and runs its overflow and density validator only if you ask.",
