          "text": "One of DeerFlow's built-in skills, and it works as written only inside DeerFlow. The agent works out the topic, the number of slides (5 to 10 by default), a style and the aspect ratio, then writes a JSON plan: a title, a style with guidelines for palette, typography, imagery and layout, and for each slide its type, title, key points and a detailed visual description. It then generates the slides strictly in order through the image-generation skill's script. The first slide sets the visual language; every later slide passes the previous image as a reference and says it must match it, because generating in parallel would break consistency. Image prompts are always in English, whatever language you write in, and spell out hex colors, font weights and effects. A bundled script then places each image full-slide in a PowerPoint file, keeping photo orientation and transparency, and writes each slide's title and key points into its speaker notes. Examples, such as a glassmorphism product-launch deck, show full plans and prompts.",
