      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Interviews you about a software idea, then writes a PRD and a JSON list of small implementation tasks, each with steps that verify it.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a rough app or feature idea and want it specified and broken into tasks before an agent builds it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks clarifying questions, checks prerequisites such as access, MCP servers, env variables and test users, and researches competitors"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": ".agent/prd/PRD.md, a short .agent/prd/SUMMARY.md, and a .agent/tasks.json index with a spec file per task in .agent/tasks/, 50 to 200+ tasks for a typical project"
            },
            {
              "label": "Part of",
              "text": "pageai's Ralph loop, whose agent loop works through that tasks.json until the list is done"
            },
            {
              "label": "Writes",
              "text": "No code and no real secrets: .env.local only gets placeholder values"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A two-part planning skill aimed at beginner developers. Part one turns a thin description into a PRD: the agent asks clarifying questions with AskUserQuestion, checks prerequisites such as access, MCP servers, docs, environment variables and test users, adds placeholder entries for missing values to .env.local, and shows an executive summary for your approval. It then researches the competition on the web and writes the PRD: overview and objectives, audience, success metrics, competitive analysis, core features and user flows, a recommended stack, prerequisites, security, assumptions and dependencies. Part two, once you approve, breaks the PRD into tasks: an index in tasks.json and a spec file per task. TASK-1 always verifies the prerequisites, each later task should take ten minutes at most, carries a category such as functional, ui-ux, api-endpoint or security, and has pass steps that verify it, and every task starts as not passed. A short SUMMARY.md describes the project, its main features, key flows and requirements. You can update the PRD or the tasks later, and at the end it checks that all three files exist.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/pageai-pro/ralph-loop/tree/eba65ebbb0a78c4a7fd25aab28e94966eddbca5b/.agent/skills/prd-creator"
