              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "Class, sequence, flowchart, ER, C4 and architecture diagrams in depth; state diagrams, git graphs, Gantt and pie or bar charts by name only"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Mermaid is a text format that renders as diagrams, so a diagram can sit in version control and change with the code. The skill opens with a guide to choosing the type: class diagrams for domain models and object-oriented design, sequence diagrams for API calls and login flows, flowcharts for processes, algorithms and user journeys, ER diagrams for database schemas, C4 diagrams for architecture at system, container and component level, plus state diagrams, git graphs, Gantt charts and pie or bar charts. It gives a starter example of a class, sequence, flowchart and ER diagram, and points to a reference for each main type: relationships and multiplicity, alt, loop and par blocks, node shapes and subgraphs, cardinality and keys, C4 boundaries, and cloud, infrastructure and CI/CD diagrams. Another covers themes, the ELK layout, the hand-drawn look and styling. Its advice: start simple, keep one diagram per concept, comment with %%, and store .mmd files next to the code. It tells the agent to diagram whenever a project or feature starts, a schema is designed or an architecture decision is explained.",
