              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A .pptx of 16:9 slide images with speaker notes, plus outline.md, speech.md and the slide images in a project folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "An image generator (Codex's built-in one by default, or an OpenAI-compatible API key), Python for its scripts, and subagents"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "Styles you ask it to save, in a personal library outside the skill folder that survives updates"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Each slide is one complete 16:9 picture made by an image model, and a script assembles them into PowerPoint. The workflow stops for your approval at each gate: the outline, with 3–5 points and a layout role per slide; a style, chosen from two or three directions or taken from an image, PDF or deck you supply; the image backend; and one sample slide. Only then does it write the deck spec and per-slide prompt jobs and dispatch one subagent per remaining slide, each using the method that made the approved sample. Local drawing, HTML screenshots or python-pptx layouts never stand in for a failed image. Figures, screenshots or logos you require on a slide are strict inputs, and you confirm which slide each goes on. Bundled scripts record each slide's dispatch and result, so a slide counts as done only when the state files say so. The agent then checks every slide for truncated text, outline mismatches, style drift, overlaps and stray page numbers, regenerates or edits failures, writes speaker notes and assembles the file. If anything is blocked, it reports the slide and the evidence instead of calling the deck complete.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/ningzimu/codex-ppt-skill/tree/941dcafe2f23ea4ae61de99e9b22fb0ef3d9e06c/skills/codex-ppt"
