      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes or updates a DESIGN.md of a product's design tokens and rules from its repo or a public website, keeping only evidence-backed values.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want coding agents to have lasting UI context for a product, or to reconstruct a live site's visual system"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Traces tokens, themes, shared components and guidance in your repo, or computed styles on up to three pages of a site, and keeps only what evidence supports"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "One DESIGN.md with token frontmatter and short guidance sections, linted and export-checked; from a URL, a draft labelled as reconstructed"
            },
            {
              "label": "Changes",
              "text": "Only DESIGN.md, never product source, dependencies or configuration"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js, to run Google's @google/design.md CLI; a browser for URL mode"
            }
          ],
          "text": "DESIGN.md is a file format with a spec and CLI from Google: design tokens go in YAML frontmatter, design guidance in Markdown. In repository mode the agent reads, in order, any existing DESIGN.md and guidance, then tokens and global styles, shared primitives, representative routes and local styling, counting a source only if the product actually uses it. In URL mode it inspects rendered pages at desktop and mobile widths, and a value earns a place only when a computed style matches a loaded CSS declaration or recurs across the sampled pages. A prose rule needs explicit guidance, a named shared token or a shared component used on at least two surfaces, so repetition, utility classes and one-off styling never become product rules, and a Don't appears only when a source states the prohibition. It picks an export target (Tailwind v4, Tailwind v3 or the DTCG design-token format), writes only schema-shaped tokens, lints the file and runs one export, rewriting until every populated category exports. On an update it diffs against the old file and restores accepted decisions. Its report lists the sources used and the conflicts left out of the file.",
