        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides content model design for Sanity and other headless CMSes: content over presentation, references versus embedded objects, reuse patterns and taxonomies.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You're designing or refactoring a CMS's content types, or a schema looks shaped like pages instead of content"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Loads the one reference that fits the decision: separating content from presentation, references versus embedding, reuse, or taxonomies"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Principles with good and bad examples, a Sanity schema snippet for each, and common mistakes to avoid"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "If the site were redesigned, the field names should still make sense: headline, not bigHeroText"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Sanity's guide to structured content, written for any headless CMS. Its four principles: content is data, not pages; keep one source of truth; design for channels that don't exist yet; and optimize for the editors. Separating content from presentation means names such as callout or tone instead of blueHighlightBox or backgroundColor, leaving the look to the frontend. References suit content that is reused, managed centrally, has its own lifecycle or must stay in sync, such as authors or products; embedded objects suit content unique to one document, such as a page's hero or SEO fields; a hybrid keeps a reference plus local overrides. Reuse runs from full duplication to full reference, through shared components, shared field sets, taxonomy references and content fragments, and it warns against over-abstraction, such as references used only once. Taxonomies can be flat, hierarchical or faceted, with advice on naming, depth, queries and governance.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/sanity-io/agent-toolkit/tree/3ed3a143f8d3413faa7790ac0b2274fd3a8a6320/skills/content-modeling-best-practices"
        },
