              "text": "By itself when you mention shoehorn, want `as` out of your tests, or need partial test data"
            }
          ],
          "text": "shoehorn (@total-typescript/shoehorn) is a small library for test data. A test often has to pass a large object, such as a request, when it only cares about one property, so people fake the whole object or silence TypeScript with `as`. With shoehorn, fromPartial() takes a partial object and still type-checks, fromAny() passes intentionally wrong data while keeping autocomplete, and fromExact() demands the full object until you swap it for fromPartial(). The agent first asks which test files have troublesome assertions and whether you need wrong data for error tests. It then installs the package with npm, searches .test.ts and .spec.ts files for `as` assertions, swaps each for the matching function, adds the imports and runs a type check.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/4ae2317ddb22b046e26455e4f9c9b3aaaf62212d/skills/misc/migrate-to-shoehorn"
        },
