        "skew": 135
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Rates every file, function and piece of logic of the code you point it at, then refactors until it's exceptionally good, one commit per refactor.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want a PR, branch, file or function made as good as it can be, not just working"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Rates every file, function and piece of logic from 0 to 10 with a reason, then refactors for simplicity, clean abstractions and readability"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "One commit per refactor, old => new ratings linked to the commits, the whole diff, and a list of opportunities beyond what you asked"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike improve-codebase-architecture",
              "text": "That one scans a whole codebase for modules worth restructuring and talks one through with you; this one works through the code you name until every part rates high"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "When you ask for a refactor, on the code you name or, by default, on what the agent is working on; it doesn't stop for your approval"
            }
          ],
          "text": "You point it at code, such as a PR, a function or a file; by default it takes what the agent is working on, and asks when that's unclear. Before changing anything, the agent lists everything in scope and rates each item from 0 to 10 with a reason, skipping nothing. Then it refactors on three fronts. Simplify: remove duplicated logic, boilerplate, needless indirection and tests that only restate the code, and treat comments that justify a design as claims to check, not rules to follow. Clean abstractions: make each file and function a sensible unit, and check that each responsibility sits on the right side of each function boundary. Readability: read each top-level function as prose, and push low-level details, such as flags or error plumbing, down into the functions it calls. It keeps going on its own until the code is exceptionally good, with a separate commit for each refactor, and ends with the ratings before and after, a link or git command for the whole diff, and the opportunities it saw beyond your request.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/brillout/skills/tree/5f3a48113e3039adb4e5d289d0c4de4680b6cc45/skills/refactor"
        },
