        "description": "Makes long replies, such as reports, plans and PR descriptions, quick to scan: TL;DR first, details buried, decisions numbered.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want the agent's long messages, such as summaries of its work, reports, plans or PR descriptions, readable at a glance"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Gives the gist first, such as a TL;DR of bullet points with one section per bullet, and moves the details into collapsibles, a gist or a file"
            },
            {
              "label": "Decisions",
              "text": "Numbered, with lettered choices and the agent's recommendation highlighted, so you can reply \"1B\""
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike caveman",
              "text": "That one makes every reply terse; this one leaves short answers alone and structures only the long ones"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "By itself, before the agent writes a long message"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It sets one goal for long messages: you get the gist in seconds, and can find any detail without reading everything. Short answers stay short, since structure there is overhead. The rest is a toolbox the agent picks from: a TL;DR of bullet points, then one section per bullet under the same name; details moved into collapsibles, a GitHub gist or a file; results ordered by what matters to you, not by the order the work happened; bold lead words, so your eye can scan the left edge; tables to compare items; before => after for changes; and a short snippet where it beats a paragraph. Decisions get numbered, with lettered choices and the agent's recommendation highlighted, so you can answer with something like \"1B\". The agent reads it before writing a summary of its work, a report, a plan, a review or a PR description, and at the start of a task that will end with one.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/brillout/skills/tree/5f3a48113e3039adb4e5d289d0c4de4680b6cc45/skills/human-parsable"
