          "text": "Defuddle is a command-line tool that keeps a web page's main content and drops navigation, ads and other clutter. This short skill has the agent call it with `--md` for Markdown, add `-o` to save the result to a file, or use `-p` to pull a single metadata field: the title, description or domain. `--json` returns both the HTML and the Markdown, and no flag returns HTML. The agent first checks that the tool is installed with `defuddle --help`, and doesn't claim an extraction worked when the tool is missing or returns an error.",
