      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns a design or spec document into a running MVP, one thin vertical slice at a time, through ECC's generator and evaluator build loop, with a plan you approve and commits you confirm.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a design or spec document, such as a PRD, and want a running MVP built from it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Reads the document, orders its features into thin vertical slices with one end-to-end path first, and scaffolds that first slice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Builds with",
              "text": "ECC's /gan-build loop: a generator agent writes the code and an evaluator scores it against the spec, until it passes or stops improving"
            },
            {
              "label": "Waits for you",
              "text": "To approve the slice plan, and to confirm each commit, until you confirm it; the scaffold and each slice get their own feat: commit"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A gan-harness/ folder with the spec, a scoring rubric and each round's feedback, and the MVP committed slice by slice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike gan-style-harness",
              "text": "That one builds a whole app from a one-line brief with its own planner; this one starts from your spec, skips the planner and gates each slice"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "ECC installed, for orch-pipeline's phases and gates and for the /gan-build command and its agents"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A thin wrapper over orch-pipeline, the shared engine of ECC's orch skills, set to its largest size so every phase runs. You pass the path to a design or spec document. The agent extracts its scope, locked decisions and feature list, and orders the work so one path runs end to end before anything is broadened, rather than all models first and then all views. After you approve the slice plan, it scaffolds the first slice, translates the document into gan-harness/spec.md and a scoring rubric, then runs /gan-build with its planner skipped: up to 15 rounds, passing at 7 out of 10, with the app tested in a browser through Playwright, or the code alone for slices without a UI. Every slice is reviewed, with ECC's security-reviewer agent for authentication, input handling and other sensitive areas, and becomes its own commit once you confirm it.",
