      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes or reviews interface microcopy, such as buttons, error messages, empty states and confirmation dialogs, with alternatives and the reasoning behind them.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You need the words for a button, error message, empty state, confirmation dialog, tooltip or onboarding step, or want existing copy reviewed"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Asks for the screen, what the user is trying to do and how they feel, the tone and any limits, then writes to a set pattern for each element"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "A Markdown block: the recommended copy, three alternatives with their tone and when to use each, the reasoning, and notes for translators"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "A connected knowledge base for your brand voice and style guide, and Figma for the screen's flow and character limits"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike better-writing",
              "text": "That one first lists the words and capitalization your product already uses and checks copy against them; this one works from the context and tone you give it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short copywriting guide from Anthropic's design plugin, run as /ux-copy with the context or the copy to review. Its five principles are clear, concise, consistent, useful and human. Each element has a pattern: buttons and other calls to action start with a verb and name the outcome (\"Create account\", not \"Submit\"); error messages say what happened, why, and how to fix it; empty states say what this is, why it's empty and how to start; confirmation dialogs name the action and its consequence, with buttons labelled \"Delete files\" and \"Keep files\" rather than OK and Cancel. Tone shifts with the moment: celebratory but restrained for success, empathetic for errors, clear and actionable for warnings. Its localization notes flag idioms to avoid and text that grows in translation.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/877a617b435ee2edfb002d9a3703c0a1a03aa1ba/design/skills/ux-copy"
        },
