        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Plans SEO work: keyword research and mapping, on-page optimization, technical audits, content optimization and rank tracking, with checklists and templates.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You want an SEO plan for a site or a page: keywords to target, on-page fixes, a technical checklist, a content brief or a monthly report"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Applies templates and rules of thumb, such as titles of 50 to 60 characters, the keyword in the first 100 words, and priority as volume times relevance over difficulty"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Written recommendations, like its blog post example: target keywords, a new title and meta description, a heading outline, word count, internal links and a checklist"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "Fetch any data: it names tools such as Google Keyword Planner, Ahrefs and PageSpeed Insights but calls none of them"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike iannuttall's seo",
              "text": "That one answers SEO questions from your own Search Console, Analytics and Bing data; this one is templates and checklists with no data source"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. A marketing playbook in five parts. Keyword research starts from seed terms (your product words, competitors' keywords, customer language from support tickets and reviews), sorts keywords by intent (informational, navigational, commercial, transactional) and maps them to the homepage, product pages, blog posts and landing pages. The on-page checklist covers the title, meta description, one H1, heading structure, word counts by page type, 1 to 2% keyword density, image alt text, URLs and internal links. The technical audit covers crawling, indexing, Core Web Vitals, mobile, HTTPS and structured data. A content brief template sets the target keyword, intent, word count, outline, competitors to beat and call to action, with checklists for before and after publishing. A monthly report template tracks traffic, conversions, ranking changes, top pages and technical health. Its frontmatter lists English and Chinese.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/claude-office-skills/skills/tree/9c4c7d5cd2813a8936bf2c9fdb174ea883b85a11/seo-optimizer"
        },
