        "updated": "2026-11-12",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Converts whole folders of documents between Word, PDF, Markdown, HTML and PowerPoint in parallel, with Pandoc, MarkItDown, pdf2docx and LibreOffice.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a folder of documents to convert at once, such as PDFs to Word, Markdown to PDF and HTML, or Office files to Markdown"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Runs a Python pipeline that converts files in parallel, handing each format pair to Pandoc, MarkItDown, pdf2docx, Marp or LibreOffice, and carries on past failures"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "Converted files in a converted folder inside the source folder, or one you name, and a success or error entry for each file"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python packages pdf2docx, markitdown, python-docx and openpyxl, plus Pandoc, LibreOffice, and the Marp CLI for slides"
            },
            {
              "label": "Gaps",
              "text": "Its code makes HTML only from Markdown and has no working converter from HTML, though its format table lists more; images aren't handled despite an example prompt"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike convert-documents-to-markdown",
              "text": "That one turns many document types into Markdown with one CLI so the agent can read them; this one converts whole folders between formats, Markdown included"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Claude Office Skills. You name a folder or files and a target format. Its DocumentConverter class picks up Markdown, Word, PDF, Excel, PowerPoint and HTML files, in subfolders too if you ask, and converts them four at a time by default. Markdown goes to Word, PDF and HTML with Pandoc and to PowerPoint with Marp; Word, Excel, PowerPoint and PDF go to Markdown with Microsoft's MarkItDown; PDF goes to Word with pdf2docx; Office files go to PDF with LibreOffice, run without a window. Examples export a docs folder to PDF, Word and HTML with an export_report.json, convert old .doc, .xls, .ppt and .rtf files to current Office formats, and turn spreadsheets into PDF and Word reports. It advises converting a few files first, checking disk space and spot-checking results, and warns that complex formatting may be lost. Its frontmatter names an office-mcp server, but its instructions never use it.",
