    {
      "id": "jsmastery-pro/skills/skills/develop",
      "name": "develop",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/jsmastery-pro/skills/develop",
        "installs": 5000,
        "weeklyInstalls": [689, 513, 414, 364, 307, 220, 237, 222],
        "firstSeen": "2026-07-09"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "43b69e44c9ca905fe3a3418ccdf4102255e20d40",
        "updated": "2026-11-12",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a feature, UI or backend, from its spec and AGENTS.md, and sends you to /architect first when a load-bearing decision is still open.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "You have a spec or design for a feature, page, component, API or service and want it built in an existing project"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "Checks that the spec names the source of every value the feature needs; if a decision such as an auth provider is still open, it stops"
            },
            {
              "label": "Open decisions",
              "text": "You choose: settle it with architect first, build anyway, or build on an assumption it records as an Assumed spec for architect to confirm later"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "The code, ticked tasks in the spec's build plan and in docs/scope/, and verify steps for each acceptance criterion, saved to verify.md if you want"
            },
            {
              "label": "First it checks",
              "text": "Whether you're behind the remote branch, have uncommitted changes in that area, or a teammate is partway through the same feature, and warns you"
            },
            {
              "label": "UI bar",
              "text": "A complete product page, never a lone form or default styling, built from Figma, a screenshot, your design.md, or a design system it sets up first"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "An existing project, unless this run is the scaffold step, and subagents for cheap read-only code mapping and doc lookups"
            }
          ],
          "text": "develop is the build step of JS Mastery's workflow, which keeps its state in files: a scope of features and their checkboxes in docs/scope/, numbered specs in docs/specs/ and conventions in AGENTS.md. Its rule is that it implements decisions and never makes them. Before writing code it lists every value the feature must produce or show; one whose source the spec doesn't name, such as a database column or a prior decision, counts as an open decision, however small. It then sorts the work into a UI track, a logic track (data layer, services, API, integrations) or both, reads only this feature's spec and the nearest AGENTS.md, and has a read-only subagent map the code to touch. It resumes at the first unticked task, applies database migrations and confirms the schema is live, and deletes the code it replaces. If the spec proves wrong partway, it stops and sends you back to architect. It marks the feature done only for a prototype; otherwise it leaves it in progress for the workflow's check and test skills, which SkillHub doesn't list, to close. It writes in plain words with no dashes or hyphens.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jsmastery-pro/skills/tree/43b69e44c9ca905fe3a3418ccdf4102255e20d40/skills/develop"
        },
